/* Automatisch erzeugt – KI-übersetzt, nicht von Hand bearbeiten. */
window.MTEC_NEWS_I18N = {"_info": {"sprache": "en", "hinweis": "KI-übersetzt aus dem Deutschen. _src = Prüfsumme des deutschen Originals; weicht sie ab, zeigt die Website das deutsche Original (scripts/update-news.mjs check warnt)."}, "2026-11-12-amd-26-11-1-ssd-fix": {"titel": "AMD Adrenalin 26.11.1 fixes the constant writing to SSDs", "schlagzeile": "Radeon driver 26.11.1: AMD finally stops the constant SSD writes", "kurz": "AMD has released the optional driver Adrenalin 26.11.1. It officially fixes the bug that made the driver constantly write data to the SSD in the background. However, the list of known issues has grown.", "zusammenfassung": "Radeon users had discovered that the Adrenalin driver constantly writes data to the drive in the background, even when idle. Heise warned that this can endanger SSD lifespan, and until now only a free community tool helped. Now, according to Wccftech and Neowin, AMD has released the optional driver 26.11.1, which is supposed to officially fix the problem. According to the release notes, owners of Radeon RX 7000 and RX 9000 were affected, and the bug also occurred when moving or resizing windows. The list of known issues includes nine new entries, mainly crashes and driver timeouts in certain games such as Cyberpunk 2077 and War Thunder. On RX 9000 cards, AMD also lists graphical artifacts in Phantom Blade Zero. Anyone affected by the SSD problem should install the update and can then remove the community tool.", "weitere_links": ["Neowin", "heise online"], "_src": "336a15b3"}, "2026-11-12-gdc-umfrage-entlassungen": {"titel": "GDC survey: one in three people surveyed in the games industry was laid off within two years", "schlagzeile": "GDC survey: one in three respondents in the games industry was laid off", "kurz": "In the new GDC survey of more than 2,600 industry professionals, 34 percent said they had been laid off in the past two years. More than half of them are still without a job. According to the survey, morale in the industry is poor.", "zusammenfassung": "The 15th edition of the GDC's State of the Game Industry survey questioned more than 2,600 industry professionals worldwide, VGC reports. 34 percent said they had been laid off in the past two years, and in the US as many as 39 percent. In the January survey, the figure was still 28 percent. Of those laid off, 54 percent are still unemployed, and 27 percent have submitted at least 100 job applications. 17 percent were even laid off twice in two years. Only 45 percent of those employed consider their job at least somewhat secure for the next twelve months. 81 percent are worried about their future in the industry.", "_src": "f0c14b73"}, "2026-11-12-steam-pruefstau-ki": {"titel": "Steam review backlog due to flood of AI games: more indie games have to be delayed", "schlagzeile": "Flood of AI games on Steam: indie games stuck in Valve's review queue", "kurz": "Valve's review of new games on Steam currently takes up to twelve days, according to developers because of a flood of low-quality AI games. Several indie titles have had to postpone their release. Valve has tightened its submission rules, but critics say that is not enough.", "zusammenfassung": "Since the beginning of November, developers have been complaining about long waiting times for Valve's approval of new games and builds on Steam. According to Eurogamer, Valve explained that reviews can take up to twelve days due to the number of submissions that need to be reviewed again. A flood of cheap games created with generative AI is seen as the cause. The tower defense game Australia Did It by Rami Ismail and Aesthetician Labs was supposed to launch on November 10 and is still waiting for approval. Amazing Slot Survivor also had to withdraw its November 13 date, and more indie games are affected. Valve has introduced stricter submission rules to weed out fully AI-generated games earlier. Ismail believes Valve cannot stay neutral on AI without harming genuine developers.", "_src": "5412161f"}, "2026-11-12-windows-signdrop-zero-day": {"titel": "SignDrop: new Windows zero-day grants SYSTEM privileges, no patch yet", "schlagzeile": "Windows zero-day SignDrop: SYSTEM privileges and no patch yet", "kurz": "A security researcher has published SignDrop, a new unpatched Windows flaw including an exploit. It is said to give attackers SYSTEM privileges and bypass the self-protection of antivirus software. According to the researcher, around 80 percent of Windows installations are affected.", "zusammenfassung": "According to BleepingComputer, researcher Abdelhamid Naceri, known as Nightmare Eclipse, has published a new zero-day exploit for Windows. SignDrop abuses, of all things, a protection measure that Microsoft introduced in October 2025 for the Common Log File System driver (CLFS). Through a detour, privileged processes such as Windows Defender can be made to create files with SYSTEM privileges. According to Naceri, this can also be used to bypass the tamper protection of antivirus and EDR software. He tested Windows 11 26H2 and Windows Server 2025 and estimates that around 80 percent of installations are vulnerable. Systems where the registry value for the CLFS authentication mode is set to 0 or 1 are vulnerable. According to Naceri, there is no workaround, and users have to wait for a patch from Microsoft. The report does not mention a statement from Microsoft.", "_src": "d8efd221"}, "2026-11-12-gta6-karte-leak": {"titel": "GTA 6: printed map from the Collector's Edition reportedly leaked via a merch event", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is the GTA 6 map online a week before release?", "kurz": "Photos of a printed, stylized map of Leonida are circulating online, said to come from the GTA 6 Collector's Edition. The pictures reportedly come from a merch event at Selfridges in the UK. Rockstar has not commented, and the map is probably not an exact copy of the game world.", "zusammenfassung": "One week before the release of GTA 6 on November 19, photos of a map are appearing, according to VGC and Insider Gaming. They are said to show the printed map from the Collector's Edition and to come from a GTA 6 event at the department store chain Selfridges. According to VGC, the clearest image came from a now-deleted Instagram account, and another photo shows the map folded in a display case in Manchester. According to Insider Gaming, a Selfridges employee is said to be the source, but this has not been proven. The map shows Leonida in stylized form with counties and clipart-like motifs, such as monster trucks, a UFO and planes. Insider Gaming assumes that it does not accurately reflect the game world. Rockstar has not confirmed the images. Anyone who wants to avoid spoilers should be careful on social media.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming", "Polygon"], "_src": "a2e2106c"}, "2026-11-12-xbox-25-sharma-memo": {"titel": "25 years of Xbox: Asha Sharma hints at AI development in a memo, plus Halo Firefight and Xbox Playback", "schlagzeile": "25 years of Xbox: boss wants small teams to build huge worlds", "kurz": "For Xbox's 25th birthday, boss Asha Sharma has published a memo that sounds a lot like generative AI. Small teams are supposed to build worlds that today require hundreds of developers. Xbox also announced a Firefight mode for Halo: Campaign Evolved and the year-in-review feature Xbox Playback.", "zusammenfassung": "Xbox boss Asha Sharma has published a memo titled \"25 Years of Xbox\" for the 25th anniversary. At the end, she writes that too many ideas never become games and that this must change. Soon, a single person will have capabilities that once required entire nations, and small teams could build worlds that today demand hundreds of developers. According to Eurogamer, the term generative AI is not used, but the wording strongly suggests it. Sharma comes from Microsoft's AI division, but when she started as Xbox boss she said she had \"no tolerance for bad AI\". For the anniversary, she also announced on X a Firefight mode for Halo: Campaign Evolved, coming as a free update this winter; according to Insider Gaming, it is a four-player PvE mode. In addition, Xbox Playback is rolling out, a look back at your own games and achievements on Xbox. Xbox did not name any specific AI projects in the memo.", "weitere_links": ["IGN", "Insider Gaming", "Asha Sharma auf X (Halo Firefight)"], "_src": "0b7ff29f"}, "2026-11-12-gta6-suedkorea-freigabe": {"titel": "GTA 6 almost did not get an age rating in South Korea because of nude scenes", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 almost banned? South Korea argued for weeks over nude scenes", "kurz": "South Korea's rating board GCRB struggled for a long time to agree on a rating for GTA 6. The sticking point was nudity without sexual context. In the end, it received an adults-only rating by eight votes to one.", "zusammenfassung": "According to IGN Germany, Rockstar applied for an age rating in South Korea on September 1. The first vote of the GCRB rating board on September 10 ended in a tie: three members wanted to refuse a rating, three were in favor of adults only. According to meeting minutes obtained by InvenGlobal, some members objected to nude scenes without sexual context. The decision was postponed until a playable version was available, and several dates were pushed back. On October 18, the committee then decided on an adults-only rating by eight votes to one. A refusal would have completely prevented sales in South Korea. GTA 6 launches on November 19 for PS5 and Xbox Series X and S.", "weitere_links": ["Polygon"], "_src": "c47f9d24"}, "2026-11-12-nvidia-linux-nvroot-forgeptr": {"titel": "NvRoot and ForgePtr: two security flaws in Nvidia's Linux driver published, 25 more announced", "schlagzeile": "Nvidia Linux driver: flaw turns container processes into root", "kurz": "Security firm Stealthium has published two flaws in Nvidia's open Linux kernel modules. Through ForgePtr, a process in a GPU container can become root on the host. Patches are already available, and 25 more disclosures are to follow.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Phoronix, the first two of a total of 27 announced security flaws in Nvidia's driver stack are now public. ForgePtr (CVE-2026-47501) allows an unprivileged process in a GPU container to gain root privileges on the host. With NvRoot (CVE-2026-47591), the GPU can overwrite files that the operating system has marked as read-only. Both flaws have been in Nvidia's open kernel modules for around four years and are rated high (CVSS 7.8). Cloud providers that rent out GPUs to multiple customers are particularly affected. NvRoot is fixed with drivers 610.57.04, 595.91.07 and 580.178.04, and ForgePtr with 615.71.09. According to Phoronix, Stealthium has announced 25 more disclosures concerning Nvidia's AI software stack. Anyone using Nvidia GPUs on Linux, especially in containers, should update the driver.", "_src": "fa81fb4c"}, "2026-11-12-huang-ruecktritt-kress": {"titel": "Jensen Huang steps down as Nvidia CEO after 33 years, CFO Colette Kress takes over on an interim basis", "schlagzeile": "End of an era: Jensen Huang resigns from Nvidia", "kurz": "Nvidia has announced the resignation of co-founder and CEO Jensen Huang, who is leaving all his positions with immediate effect. CFO Colette Kress will lead the company as interim CEO for now. Harvey C. Jones takes over as chairman of the board.", "zusammenfassung": "After days of crisis, it is official: Jensen Huang is stepping down after 33 years at the helm of Nvidia. According to ComputerBase, he is giving up his roles as president, CEO and board member, and according to PC Gamer with immediate effect. Huang was not fired; according to TechPowerUp, he signed a letter of resignation. The trigger was reports of two extramarital relationships, including one with a manager who reported directly to him. Before that, the board had met in an unscheduled session, and according to Bloomberg an outside firm had already been hired for the search for a successor. CFO Colette Kress is running the business as interim CEO and remains CFO at the same time. Harvey C. Jones takes over as chairman of the board. Kress said she would build on the foundation Huang created over 33 years. The announcement does not say whether Huang will play any future role at the company. Who will become permanent CEO is open; so far there is only speculation. Any impact on GeForce products, prices or drivers is currently not known.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware", "TechPowerUp", "PC Gamer", "heise online"], "_src": "330d1f5e"}, "2026-11-12-paradox-wester-ruecktritt": {"titel": "Paradox CEO Frederik Wester steps down, Mattias Lilja takes over in January", "schlagzeile": "After the Bloodlines 2 flop: Paradox gets a new boss", "kurz": "Paradox Interactive CEO Frederik Wester is giving up his post and moving to the board. His deputy Mattias Lilja takes over on January 4, 2027. The publisher has several difficult years behind it.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Eurogamer, Frederik Wester is stepping down as CEO of Paradox Interactive and will focus on long-term development as a board member. His successor will be the current deputy CEO Mattias Lilja from January 4, 2027, and Wester will remain in office until then. Wester led Paradox from 2009 to 2018 and again since 2021. His second term saw the difficult development of Vampire: The Masquerade Bloodlines 2, whose commercial failure caused operating profit to drop sharply. On top of that came the cancellation of Life by You, the delay of Prison Architect 2 and the bumpy launch of Cities: Skylines 2, whose console version is still missing. Lilja wants to invest more in the core business and work more closely with players and modders. Next up are Lego Skylines and the strategy game Afterworld.", "_src": "b6ea62b9"}, "2026-11-12-siren-halo-gddr7": {"titel": "Rumor: AMD's Siren Halo is said to use GDDR7 graphics memory instead of only LPDDR5X", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Will AMD's mega APU Siren Halo get real GDDR7 memory?", "kurz": "According to a leaker, AMD's upcoming Halo APU Siren Halo will use GDDR7 memory. Current Halo chips use shared LPDDR5X memory for CPU and GPU. Nothing is confirmed.", "zusammenfassung": "Hardware leaker Gotou_kai3 claims that AMD's Siren Halo will get GDDR7 memory, Wccftech and PCGH report. Like Medusa Halo, Siren Halo is said to use Zen 6 and RDNA 5, but to be a true successor rather than a simple refresh. Current Halo chips such as Strix Halo use LPDDR5X as shared memory for CPU and GPU. GDDR7 would bring much more memory bandwidth, which could especially help the graphics unit in games. According to Wccftech, it is unclear whether CPU and GPU could both use both memory pools or whether GDDR7 would be reserved for graphics only. For AI workloads, a GDDR7-only graphics solution might be less flexible than the large shared memory of today's Ryzen AI Max chips. AMD has not announced Siren Halo, and dates and specifications are unknown.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "6fee7dbc"}, "2026-11-12-apache-http2-luecke": {"titel": "Critical flaw in Apache's HTTP/2 module: update to 2.4.71 recommended", "schlagzeile": "Critical Apache flaw: update web servers with HTTP/2 now", "kurz": "The Apache web server has a critical flaw in the mod_http2 module that could allow remote code execution. Only servers with HTTP/2 enabled are affected. Version 2.4.71 fixes the bug.", "zusammenfassung": "According to heise, the flaw CVE-2026-119618 is located in the assign_headers() function of the mod_http2 module. Memory manipulation there could lead to remote execution of malicious code. According to Golem, Red Hat rates the flaw 9.8 out of 10. It was found by an OSS scanner from Anthropic and two researchers from Google Cloud Vulnerability Research. Since mod_http2 is not enabled by default, only servers using HTTP/2 are affected. Experts such as Kevin Beaumont consider an exploit difficult because of protections such as ASLR. Still, admins should update to Apache 2.4.71, which closes two more flaws. Anyone who cannot update right away should disable HTTP/2 for now.", "weitere_links": ["Golem.de"], "_src": "8ac52b3f"}, "2026-11-12-rtx5090-96gb-mod": {"titel": "Modified RTX 5090 with 96 GB of memory shows up on a Chinese second-hand marketplace", "schlagzeile": "RTX 5090 with 96 GB: China mod listed for around 900,000 dollars", "kurz": "A modified GeForce RTX 5090 with 96 GB of video memory is being offered on the Chinese platform Xianyu. The placeholder price is around 900,000 US dollars, with the real price negotiated privately. Whether the card actually works has not been proven.", "zusammenfassung": "Chinese modders move desktop GPUs onto their own boards and multiply the memory for AI workloads. Now, according to Wccftech and PCGH, a listing has appeared for an RTX 5090 with 96 GB, as much memory as the RTX Pro 6000. It was spotted by repair specialist VIK-on on Alibaba's second-hand marketplace Xianyu, and VideoCardz reported it first. The GB202 chip sits on a custom board with Samsung memory chips on both sides. Besides the card, the seller also offers board schematics and a patched BIOS, but only targets business customers with a confidentiality agreement. The listed price of 6,488,888 yuan, around 900,000 US dollars, is a placeholder; the actual price is negotiated privately. There are no benchmarks, so the card's functionality is unconfirmed.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "4c5d0781"}, "2026-11-12-swtor-directx12-test": {"titel": "Star Wars: The Old Republic starts public DirectX 12 test, graphics deliberately reduced at first", "schlagzeile": "SWTOR gets DirectX 12 – and looks worse for now", "kurz": "Almost 15 years after release, Star Wars: The Old Republic is testing a DirectX 12 client. The public test starts this week directly in the regular launcher. Many graphics effects are deliberately missing at first.", "zusammenfassung": "According to PC Games, developer Broadsword is modernizing the technology of the MMORPG Star Wars: The Old Republic. A public test of the new DirectX 12 client starts this week, with no sign-up or access code required. In the regular launcher, a small arrow lets you choose between the old and the new version; both use the same live servers and characters. Many environmental details and effects are still missing or simplified in the new client, and graphics options are limited too. This is intentional: the focus is first on stability, performance and compatibility with as many PCs as possible. Players are asked to report stutters, graphical glitches and crashes along with their hardware. The test is not available for Mac players for now. According to Broadsword, the project will run well into 2027, after which the graphics are to be gradually brought back to at least the old level.", "_src": "b512307b"}, "2026-11-12-apex-neural-rendering": {"titel": "Apex Neural Rendering: start-up promises a vendor-independent alternative to DLSS, FSR and XeSS", "schlagzeile": "Better than DLSS? Apex brings frame generation to all three GPU camps", "kurz": "The company Apex Compute has unveiled Apex Neural Rendering (ANR), with super resolution, ray reconstruction and frame generation for GeForce, Radeon and Arc. Frame generation is available now as a free beta on GitHub. The promises are big, but ComputerBase finds them hard to verify.", "zusammenfassung": "Apex Compute, so far specialized in edge AI accelerators, wants to take on DLSS, FSR and XeSS with Apex Neural Rendering (ANR). ANR is supposed to offer super resolution, ray reconstruction and frame generation independently of the vendor on Nvidia, AMD and Intel. According to the company, it is up to 2.4 times faster and delivers better image quality than DLSS. Only frame generation is available so far, as a free beta on GitHub; it is integrated via OptiScaler and offers 2×, 3× and 4× modes. According to Apex, super resolution and ray reconstruction are still in development. According to ComputerBase, frame generation runs on GeForce GTX 16 and RTX 2000 and newer, on Radeon RX 5000 and newer including the Steam Deck, and on Intel Arc A, under Windows 10, Windows 11 and Linux with Proton. ComputerBase criticizes inconsistencies in the company's claims, such as alleged FSR measurements with more than one AI-generated frame, and unclear factors in the comparison videos. There are no independent tests yet, so the performance and quality claims are unconfirmed.", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp", "Wccftech", "GamingOnLinux"], "_src": "6efb8d9d"}, "2026-11-12-samsung-hbm-onyang": {"titel": "Memory shortage: Samsung builds a new HBM packaging line and wants to finish it a year early", "schlagzeile": "RAM crisis: Samsung pulls new HBM fab forward by a year", "kurz": "Samsung has started building a new line for HBM packaging in Onyang. It is set to start operating in June 2028, a year earlier than planned. The reason is the ongoing memory shortage.", "zusammenfassung": "According to ComputerBase, Samsung has broken ground on its Onyang campus in Asan for a new production line that will package HBM memory. Operations are set to start in June 2028, a year earlier than originally planned. Samsung is investing 46 trillion won, around 31 billion euros, in Onyang, most of it in equipment. Around 31,000 square meters of cleanroom on three floors and around 700 new jobs are planned. In October, Samsung said it had already negotiated HBM supply volumes for 2027 and could not come close to meeting demand. HBM is mainly used in AI accelerators, but the shortage weighs on the entire memory market and thus also on RAM prices for PC users. In the short term, the new line will not change prices.", "_src": "7ecef997"}, "2026-11-12-outlook-mails-blockiert": {"titel": "Outlook.com: faulty spam rule rejected genuine emails for days – the messages are lost", "schlagzeile": "Outlook rejected emails for days – and they're not coming back", "kurz": "A faulty Microsoft spam rule rejected legitimate emails to Outlook.com, Hotmail and Live addresses for days. Microsoft has rolled back the update, and senders and recipients do not need to change anything. Rejected emails cannot be recovered, however, so you have to ask senders to resend them.", "zusammenfassung": "If you recently had a suspiciously quiet Outlook.com inbox, you may have been affected. According to Windows Latest, legitimate emails to Outlook.com, Hotmail, Live and MSN addresses were rejected from at least November 5. Senders received error messages saying their emails lacked SPF, DKIM or DMARC records, although that was partly untrue. Microsoft confirmed to Windows Latest that an update to its spam rules was the cause. The company has rolled it back, and according to Windows Latest mail flow has been working again since November 9. Neither senders nor recipients need to change any settings. The problem: the rejected emails did not land in the spam folder but never arrived. Microsoft therefore cannot restore them. Anyone who was expecting important emails should ask the senders to send them again. Admins can find the incident in the Microsoft 365 admin center under the ID EX1545193. Microsoft does not say how many users were affected.", "_src": "74d3487f"}, "2026-11-12-powershell-signatur-kb5132061": {"titel": "November update KB5132061: stricter checks make some signed PowerShell scripts fail", "schlagzeile": "Windows update trips up signed PowerShell scripts – here's the fix", "kurz": "With the November security update, Windows checks the text encoding of signed PowerShell scripts more strictly. Scripts with faulty UTF-8 may then be treated as unsigned and no longer run as usual in managed environments. Microsoft recommends saving them as UTF-8 with BOM and signing them again.", "zusammenfassung": "With update KB5132061 of November 10, Microsoft has tightened the verification of PowerShell signatures. Until now, Windows could still process scripts with invalid UTF-8 by replacing faulty characters. That no longer happens, and affected files are rejected. According to Microsoft, Get-AuthenticodeSignature then reports \"NotSigned\" for a script that is actually signed. Set-AuthenticodeSignature can abort with an error. On devices with App Control for Business, affected scripts may only run in constrained language mode. Mainly affected are scripts with faulty UTF-8, UTF-8 without BOM on systems with a different code page, and files in encodings such as Shift-JIS. Microsoft recommends checking the scripts, saving them as valid UTF-8 with BOM and signing them again. A sample script called Repair-SignedPowerShellUtf8.ps1 finds affected files and does not overwrite any originals. According to Neowin, the change applies not only to Windows 11 but also to Windows 10 Enterprise LTSC 2021 and Windows Server 2025. Home users without signed scripts will usually not notice anything.", "weitere_links": ["Microsoft Support (KB5132061)", "Microsoft Support (encoding guidance)"], "_src": "22fabd49"}, "2026-11-12-tomb-raider-catalyst-switch2": {"titel": "Amazon lists Tomb Raider: Catalyst for Nintendo Switch 2 as well", "schlagzeile": "Tomb Raider: Catalyst is apparently coming to Switch 2 too", "kurz": "A post on Amazon's official news site names Switch 2 as a platform for both upcoming Tomb Raider games. This was known for Legacy of Atlantis, but not for Catalyst so far. Amazon is the publisher of Catalyst, but confirmation from Crystal Dynamics or Nintendo is still missing.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Insider Gaming, a post on Amazon News updated on November 9 states that both new Tomb Raider games will be released for PS5, Xbox Series X/S, Nintendo Switch 2 and Steam. For Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis (2027), the Switch 2 version was already official, and the game can be pre-ordered on the eShop. What is new is the statement for Tomb Raider: Catalyst. The game was delayed to 2028 this year. Catalyst is published by Amazon Game Studios, which gives the statement weight. However, Insider Gaming considers an error in the article possible, even though it has been online unchanged for two days. Crystal Dynamics and Nintendo have not yet confirmed the Switch 2 version. There are no technical details or a date for the Switch 2 version.", "_src": "de9ab1dc"}, "2026-11-12-steam-erfolge-linux-64bit": {"titel": "Steam client update: Achievement Sets for everyone, and the Linux client finally runs as a 64-bit program", "schlagzeile": "Steam update: new achievement sets and 64-bit for Linux", "kurz": "Valve has released a new Steam update for all users. Games can now group achievements into sets for the base game and DLC without losing a 100 percent completion. On Linux, the Steam client is now a 64-bit program and runs in a Steam Runtime container.", "zusammenfassung": "On November 11, Valve released a Steam client update to the stable channel. The most important new feature for everyone is Steam Achievement Sets. Developers can use them to group achievements by base game and DLC. New achievements or DLC achievements thus no longer make an already completed achievement collection incomplete. Seasonal achievements or ones that can no longer be earned can be archived. There is also a redesigned achievements page. On Linux, the Steam client is now a 64-bit application and runs in a Steam Runtime container. According to Valve, this should ensure consistent behavior across different distributions; it is the same technology that games use. According to TechPowerUp, Steam on Linux was previously still a 32-bit program. The update also fixes, among other things, a crash when resuming from standby. Whether developers actually use the new achievement sets is up to them.", "weitere_links": ["Steam (Achievement Sets announcement)", "9to5Linux"], "_src": "95507831"}, "2026-11-12-witcher3-ki-stimme-geralt": {"titel": "The Witcher 3: CD Projekt adjusts Geralt's Polish voice with AI in the new expansion – with the actor's consent", "schlagzeile": "After a stroke: AI makes Geralt's Polish voice sound young again", "kurz": "In the upcoming Witcher 3 expansion Songs of the Past, Geralt's Polish voice is being reworked with AI. Voice actor Jacek Rozenek records all lines himself, but his voice has changed noticeably after a stroke in 2019. With his consent, AI company Respeecher matches it to how he used to sound.", "zusammenfassung": "CD Projekt Red has confirmed that it is using AI for the Polish version of the new Witcher 3 expansion Songs of the Past. Game File reported it first, and PC Gamer, VGC and IGN have picked it up. Jacek Rozenek has always voiced Geralt in Polish, but suffered a stroke in 2019 and was temporarily unable to speak. After long training he returned, but today his voice sounds deeper and rougher. Because the expansion takes place in the middle of The Witcher 3's story, the difference could have been noticeable. Rozenek therefore still records all lines himself, and Respeecher then adjusts them to how he sounded around twelve years ago. The model was trained on his earlier recordings for the game. Rozenek explicitly supports this and says the voice should be as close as possible to his voice back then. Localization producer Mikołaj Szwed calls it a special case because of the illness and sees it as an ethical use with consent. According to CD Projekt, nothing similar is planned for Doug Cockle's English voice. CD Projekt already worked with Respeecher on Cyberpunk 2077: Phantom Liberty, back then with the consent of a late voice actor's family. The reports do not give a release date for Songs of the Past.", "weitere_links": ["VGC", "IGN"], "_src": "b5c1fa87"}, "2026-11-12-helldivers2-kosmetik-mods": {"titel": "Helldivers 2: after anti-cheat switch and review wave, cosmetic mods should work again with the next hotfix", "schlagzeile": "Helldivers 2: Arrowhead wants to allow harmless mods again", "kurz": "Since the switch to Easy Anti-Cheat, many mods no longer work in Helldivers 2, and more than 10,000 negative reviews followed on Steam. Arrowhead announces that some purely cosmetic mods should work again with the next hotfix. Mods that change gameplay remain banned.", "zusammenfassung": "Arrowhead switched the anti-cheat system in Helldivers 2 from GameGuard to Easy Anti-Cheat. According to the studio, the goal was to stop mods that give unfair advantages or harm others. In the process, however, harmless cosmetic mods also stopped working. The reaction was fierce: according to PC Gamer, more than 10,000 new negative Steam reviews came in, and recent reviews stand at \"Mostly Negative\". In its new developer blog, Arrowhead admits that PC players have lost fan mods. After adjustments, some cosmetic mods should work again with the next hotfix. Mods that change gameplay remain banned because they are technically indistinguishable from cheats. Mods are still not officially supported. Arrowhead also apologizes for an inaccurate roadmap and missed patch dates. Planned for early December are, among other things, jetpacks that can be used while carrying two-handed items. The studio does not give a date for the hotfix.", "_src": "0f2f4919"}, "2026-11-12-marvel-1943-fast-fertig": {"titel": "Report: Marvel 1943: Rise of Hydra is said to be almost finished, but much smaller than planned", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Marvel 1943 almost done – but heavily cut down?", "kurz": "After rumors of a cancellation, Kotaku reports that Marvel 1943: Rise of Hydra is almost finished. However, the game is said to offer significantly less content and gameplay depth than planned. Skydance has not said anything official about it.", "zusammenfassung": "Marvel 1943: Rise of Hydra, Amy Hennig's Captain America and Black Panther game, was recently the subject of rumors about an imminent cancellation. According to Kotaku and Bloomberg reporter Jason Schreier, Skydance's leadership told employees via Slack that this is not true. Kotaku also reports that the game is \"close to done\", meaning almost finished. However, development is said to have been difficult and well over budget. As a result, scope and length are said to have been cut significantly. According to Kotaku's sources, the game is \"light on gameplay\", with much of it handled by a single button. Marvel 1943 reportedly started out as a Netflix game. It was announced in 2024 and has been delayed several times since. There is no release date. All details come from anonymous sources, and Skydance has not confirmed them.", "ursprungsquelle": "Kotaku (via IGN)", "_src": "3cff0819"}, "2026-11-12-nvidia-board-huang-abloesung": {"titel": "Reports: Nvidia's board is weighing the removal of CEO Jensen Huang and is already looking for a successor", "schlagzeile": "Nvidia facing a change at the top? Board weighs removing Huang", "kurz": "According to the Wall Street Journal, Nvidia's board is preparing to remove founder and CEO Jensen Huang. The trigger is a New York Times report about a second extramarital relationship, this time with a manager who reports directly to him. According to Bloomberg, an outside firm is already searching for successors. As of midday today, Nvidia still has not announced a decision; the reports rely on anonymous sources.", "zusammenfassung": "The crisis around Nvidia chief Jensen Huang is escalating. According to the Wall Street Journal, the board wanted to meet on Wednesday evening (US time) to discuss Huang's future, with a removal on the table. The trigger is a new New York Times report: besides the affair he has already admitted, Huang is said to have had a relationship with a vice president who reports directly to him. The paper cites five former employees and says it has not seen an alleged video of an incident in March itself. Neither Nvidia nor those involved have confirmed the report. According to Bloomberg, the board is already working with an outside firm to find a successor, and an interim CEO is also being considered. The background is the investigation running since Sunday into Huang's affair with a manager at Nvidia customer Megaspeed, who US authorities are said to have classified as a suspected Chinese agent; China denies this. Huang has led Nvidia since its founding in 1993, and according to PCGH there is no named successor. According to PCGH, a simple majority of the directors is enough to remove him. After the reports, the stock lost around eight percent in after-hours trading and fell to a 52-week low. Nvidia reports quarterly results on November 17, and a confidential briefing in the US Congress is planned for November 18. No concrete effects on GeForce cards, prices or drivers are known so far. Important: everything is based on media reports with anonymous sources from the Wall Street Journal, the New York Times and Bloomberg; as of midday today, Nvidia has not announced a decision, and the situation can change.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware", "heise online", "Golem.de", "IGN", "PC Gamer"], "_src": "f0402e6d"}, "2026-11-12-golden-joystick-2026": {"titel": "Golden Joystick Awards 2026: Resident Evil Requiem is Game of the Year, Crimson Desert wins on PC", "schlagzeile": "Golden Joysticks: Resident Evil Requiem takes Game of the Year", "kurz": "At the 44th Golden Joystick Awards, Resident Evil Requiem won the top prize as Ultimate Game of the Year. Crimson Desert was named best PC game. Multiplayer hit Meccha Chameleon took four awards, and The Witcher 4 is the most wanted game.", "zusammenfassung": "The Golden Joystick Awards are considered the games industry's oldest public vote and were held for the 44th time in 2026. Capcom's Resident Evil Requiem took the top prize as Ultimate Game of the Year. The horror game also won Console Game of the Year, Best Game Trailer and Best Lead Performer for Angela Sant'Albano as Grace Ashcroft. According to TheGameVerse, Capcom was also named Studio of the Year. Crimson Desert was named PC Game of the Year, even though it is also out on consoles. Hide-and-seek game Meccha Chameleon won four awards: Best Multiplayer Game, Best Indie Game (self-published), Streamer's Choice and Developers' Choice. The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt Remastered was named best remaster, and The Witcher 4 most wanted game. Fans voted the Steam Controller best gaming hardware. Other awards went to Onimusha: Way of the Sword (audio), Control: Resonant (visual design), Doom: The Dark Ages – Revelations (expansion) and Subnautica 2 (early access). The awards are organized by PC Gamer's publisher.", "weitere_links": ["TheGameVerse on X (winners list)"], "_src": "d4e2e75f"}, "2026-11-12-gta6-clip-realistisch": {"titel": "GTA 6: Rockstar shares in-game clip that many take for a real phone video from Miami", "schlagzeile": "Real or GTA 6? New Rockstar clip fools the internet", "kurz": "A roughly 15-second first-person GTA 6 clip is sparking debate because many people think it is real footage. It recreates a real phone video of the GTA cars from the marketing stunt in Miami. Rockstar shared the clip in its Instagram story, which according to IGN points to genuine game footage.", "zusammenfassung": "One week before the launch of GTA 6, a short clip is causing amazement. It first appeared on the Instagram account \"Only in Dade\", which collects bizarre scenes from Miami-Dade. It shows a drive along Ocean Drive past a row of flashy cars, plus a second perspective from the sidewalk. According to IGN, Polygon and Insider Gaming, the clip recreates a real video taken in October during Rockstar's marketing stunt with recreated GTA cars in Miami. Many viewers initially took the footage for real recordings or for AI. Rockstar shared the clip in its Instagram story and liked it, which IGN sees as a strong sign of genuine game footage. According to Polygon, however, Rockstar has not explicitly confirmed it. Fans speculate that the look could show what recordings with the in-game phone camera look like. Insider Gaming stresses that the clip says nothing about a possible first-person mode. GTA 6 launches on November 19 for PS5 and Xbox Series X/S and, according to Rockstar, runs at 30 fps on consoles. Preloading is already under way.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming", "Polygon", "GamePro (news overview)"], "_src": "34198252"}, "2026-11-12-black-forest-games-unabhaengig": {"titel": "Black Forest Games buys itself out of Embracer and founds the studio group Third Signal", "schlagzeile": "German Destroy All Humans studio buys itself out of Embracer", "kurz": "German studio Black Forest Games has separated from THQ Nordic and Embracer through a management buyout. At the same time, it is founding Third Signal, a group of independent studios. The team will continue to work with THQ Nordic.", "zusammenfassung": "After nine years under the umbrella of THQ Nordic and Embracer, Black Forest Games is independent again. According to Eurogamer and PC Gamer, this was achieved through a management buyout. The studio developed Giana Sisters: Twisted Dreams and the remakes of the first two Destroy All Humans games, among others. It was founded by former employees of Spellbound Entertainment, known for Desperados and Arcania: Gothic 4. Together with its independence, it is launching Third Signal, a group of independent studios that is also meant to help other indie teams in the future. Third Signal CEO Andreas Tobler says, in essence, that many of the best games of the last decade came from teams of 50 rather than 500 people. According to the press release, THQ Nordic and Black Forest Games will continue to collaborate on development. The studio apparently has not taken over the rights to Destroy All Humans. Managing director Adrian Goersch announces a new project but gives no details. The studio was hit by Embracer's layoffs in 2024 and lost around 50 jobs at the time.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "7dfb6efd"}, "2026-11-12-nintendo-dmca-github": {"titel": "Nintendo has 144 GitHub repositories with Switch modchip firmware and two emulators removed via DMCA", "schlagzeile": "Nintendo cleans up GitHub: Switch emulators and modchip firmware gone", "kurz": "Nintendo has sent four DMCA notices to GitHub targeting the Switch emulators Yuzu and Citron Neo as well as modchip firmware. GitHub has removed 144 repositories with the firmware. According to TorrentFreak, however, it can still be found elsewhere on the platform.", "zusammenfassung": "Nintendo is once again taking action against tools for bypassing the Switch's copy protection. According to IGN, GitHub received four DMCA notices, which it has documented publicly. The targets are the emulators Yuzu and Citron Neo, but above all firmware for modchips such as Picofly. Such chips are soldered onto the Switch mainboard and bypass the copy protection. GitHub removed 144 repositories with the firmware and replaced them with a DMCA notice. In its notice dated November 6, Nintendo argues that the technical protection measures are meant to prevent playing pirated copies and playing on unauthorized devices. According to TorrentFreak, however, the firmware is still available elsewhere on GitHub. Back in 2024, Nintendo had around 8,500 copies of Yuzu taken down. IGN links the new wave to reports that emulators had shortly before made the new Ocarina of Time remake run on PC; a direct connection has not been proven. Whether Nintendo plans further steps is open.", "_src": "788c053c"}, "2026-11-12-id-veteranen-hidden-horses": {"titel": "Around 20 former id Software developers found the studio Hidden Horses and plan an arena shooter", "schlagzeile": "After Xbox layoffs: ex-id developers found their own shooter studio", "kurz": "Around 20 former id Software developers have founded Hidden Horses, a studio owned by its employees. Their first project is the single-player arena shooter Danger Pay. It is to be financed partly through Kickstarter.", "zusammenfassung": "In the Xbox layoffs of July 2026, id Software reportedly lost 136 developers. Around 20 of them have now founded Hidden Horses, a studio owned by its employees. According to PC Gamer, the founders bring more than 250 years of combined experience. The studio is to be run democratically and to put long-term stability ahead of fast growth and questionable monetization. Co-founder Dustin Land says they want to keep the team together and make classic shooters. The first game is called Danger Pay, a single-player arena shooter about a brutal TV game show. The studio names the 1987 film The Running Man and the arcade game Smash TV as inspirations. A Kickstarter campaign is planned for financing. Platforms, date and the Kickstarter start are not yet known.", "_src": "2eb4f3a4"}, "2026-11-12-tes6-sentinel-pause": {"titel": "Bethesda: no news on The Elder Scrolls 6: Sentinel for Skyrim's anniversary – and none \"for some time\"", "schlagzeile": "15 years of Skyrim, but no Elder Scrolls 6: Bethesda tempers fans", "kurz": "For Skyrim's 15th birthday, fans had hoped for news on The Elder Scrolls 6: Sentinel. Bethesda Game Studios made clear on Reddit that there will be no big announcement. There will be nothing new on Sentinel \"for some time\".", "zusammenfassung": "The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim turned 15 on November 11. In the subreddit for The Elder Scrolls 6, fans speculated about an anniversary surprise, fueled by a podcast teaser about a \"big announcement\". The podcaster later clarified that it had nothing to do with Bethesda. Then the official Bethesda Game Studios account also chimed in on Reddit. There would be no big announcement, and nothing new on Sentinel would be shown \"for some time\", the studio wrote. Bethesda only made the title Sentinel official in early November. The Elder Scrolls 6 was announced back in 2018. For the anniversary, Skyrim is discounted on all platforms. The Elder Scrolls Online is making the Greymoor chapter part of the base game for free, and a Skyrim event runs there until December 2. When there will be new information on Sentinel is open.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "85003521"}, "2026-11-11-xbox-cloud-ohne-game-pass": {"titel": "Xbox Cloud Gaming without Game Pass: buy playtime or stream free with ads", "schlagzeile": "Xbox Cloud Gaming opens up: buy hours or play free with ads", "kurz": "Since November 11, players in supported countries can buy Xbox cloud playtime even without a Game Pass subscription. Xbox is also promoting free streaming with ads, with a time limit per session. Only games you own or selected free-to-play titles can be streamed.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft is overhauling Xbox Cloud Gaming. According to Xbox Wire, players in supported markets have been able to buy cloud playtime in the Xbox Store since November 11 without subscribing to Game Pass. During the Insider test phase, the ad-free packs cost 3.99 dollars for 10, 7.99 dollars for 25 and 11.99 dollars for 50 hours; these were explicitly introductory prices, and euro prices are not given in the sources. Purchased hours do not expire and, according to Xbox, offer shorter wait times and better stream quality. On the official cloud gaming page and on X, Xbox also promotes free streaming with ads, where available, with time limits per session. In the Insider test, the limit was one hour according to The Verge. You can stream your own games, selected free-to-play titles and Game Pass games. Since November, Game Pass subscribers have monthly allowances: 15 hours with Ultimate, 10 with Premium and 5 with Essential. Once they are used up, you can buy more hours or switch to the ad-supported option. Right on time, GTA 6 also launches via the cloud on Xbox One on November 19. Which countries are included at launch is unclear.", "weitere_links": ["Xbox Wire (GTA VI via cloud, playtime from Nov 11)", "Xbox Cloud Gaming (official page)", "Xbox Wire (prices in the Insider test)", "Xbox Wire (monthly allowances)", "The Verge"], "_src": "cfedef5c"}, "2026-11-11-dark-souls-server-zurueck": {"titel": "Dark Souls 2 and 3: online features available again after almost two weeks of downtime", "schlagzeile": "Dark Souls 2 and 3 are back online – the cause remains a secret", "kurz": "After a break of almost two weeks, the online features of Dark Souls 2 and 3 are running again on all platforms. According to PC Gamer, invasions and messages work again. FromSoftware has not revealed what exactly the server problem was.", "zusammenfassung": "The servers of Dark Souls 2 and Dark Souls 3 are back in operation. Almost two weeks earlier, the multiplayer features of both games had been switched off on all platforms because of an unexplained server problem. The official Dark Souls site now states briefly that the investigation is complete, a fix has been applied and the online features have been restored. According to PC Gamer, invasions and messages work as usual again. FromSoftware still does not name the cause. For comparison: in 2022 the PC servers of all Dark Souls games were offline for almost a year, back then because of a security vulnerability that allowed malicious code to be executed. Whether a security problem was behind it this time as well is not known. During the break, fan mods such as Seamless Co-op, which run independently of the official servers, helped out. Anyone who wants to play the classic invasions can do so again now.", "_src": "76889d66"}, "2026-11-11-kb5132061-installationsfehler": {"titel": "Windows 11: Microsoft confirms KB5132061 installation failures and is rolling out an automatic repair", "schlagzeile": "Microsoft confirms KB5132061 failures – fix comes via Windows Update", "kurz": "Microsoft has now officially confirmed the installation problems with the November security update KB5132061. On affected Windows 11 PCs the installation aborts or is retried repeatedly, with typical error codes 0x800f0993, 0x800f0989 and 0x80070306. According to Microsoft, a repair is running automatically via Windows Update and should reach affected devices within 24 to 48 hours after it started on Wednesday at 19:00 Vienna time; the security update is then installed on its own. Users do not need to do anything except stay online and get updates through Settings.", "zusammenfassung": "The November security update KB5132061 cannot be installed on some Windows 11 PCs, the installation sometimes aborts only at 99 percent, and repeated attempts often do not help. The error codes 0x800f0993, 0x800f0989 and 0x80070306 are reported, and occasionally also 0x800f0922. Microsoft documented the problem on Wednesday as a known issue in the English release notes for KB5132061. According to the company, a repair runs automatically on affected devices that are connected to the internet and use Windows Update in Settings; no manual steps are required to receive it. All affected devices should get the fix within 24 to 48 hours after the rollout started on Wednesday at 19:00 Vienna time (10:00 Pacific Time), and should then download and install the security update automatically. A Microsoft service message quoted by BleepingComputer says only a subset of devices that installed the optional October preview update KB5127936 are affected; devices without that preview update are not affected. Microsoft does not name the exact cause. Windows Latest and the DrWindows site had previously reported the errors, but many systems were never affected. Earlier tips about turning off Windows Sandbox or running DISM and sfc are now secondary, because the company is telling users to wait for the automatic repair. Anyone who still cannot install the update after the 48 hours should, according to Microsoft, use Windows Help or contact Support. This remains a security update, so it should not be paused permanently.", "weitere_links": ["Dr. Windows", "BleepingComputer", "Neowin", "Windows Latest"], "_src": "7755549c"}, "2026-11-11-harada-xbox-series-s": {"titel": "Former Tekken boss Katsuhiro Harada: consoles like the Xbox Series S should not be released", "schlagzeile": "Tekken legend Harada on Series S: “extra work for a weaker child”", "kurz": "Katsuhiro Harada criticized the Xbox Series S at a developer conference in South Korea while an Xbox representative was in the room. The main problem, he said, is that it is so similar to the Series X but noticeably weaker. A CD Projekt developer countered that the optimization helps all platforms.", "zusammenfassung": "Katsuhiro Harada, long-time head of the Tekken series and now head of the new VS Studio, spoke bluntly about the Xbox Series S at the Console Game Developers Conference 2026 in South Korea. According to Inven Global, quoted by Eurogamer, he said in front of a senior Xbox representative in attendance that he wished hardware like the Series S would not be released. The biggest problem is not just the tight memory, but that the console is very similar to the Series X yet awkwardly weaker. After the best version, it feels like having to do extra work for a slightly weaker child. With Switch 2, on the other hand, you can mentally switch to a separate device for Nintendo fans. Because there are more Series S than Series X users in the US, for example, you cannot cut corners, and complaints about worse textures then land with the developers. Paweł Sasko of CD Projekt Red countered: optimizing for weaker hardware makes games run significantly better on all platforms, and the low price expands the market. Shift Up CTO DongKi Lee said he is looking forward to the next Xbox, codenamed Helix. This is an opinion voiced on a panel, not an official position of Microsoft or any studio.", "weitere_links": ["Video Games Chronicle", "PC Gamer"], "_src": "8dad0743"}, "2026-11-11-rtx5080-24gb-gestrichen": {"titel": "Reports: Nvidia has reportedly cancelled the 24 GB RTX 5080 – the 16 GB model stays", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Nvidia has reportedly scrapped the 24 GB RTX 5080", "kurz": "According to the Chinese industry channel Board Channels, Nvidia has told its board partners that the 24 GB RTX 5080 planned for January 2027 is cancelled. The reason is said to be the expensive 3 GB GDDR7 chips. The 16 GB RTX 5080 will reportedly stay in production. Nvidia has not confirmed any of this.", "zusammenfassung": "According to new reports, there will be no RTX 5080 with 24 GB of video memory for now. TechPowerUp cites the Chinese industry channel Board Channels, which says Nvidia officially informed its board partners that the planned January 2027 launch is off. Cost is given as the reason: according to the post quoted by PC Gamer, 3 GB GDDR7 chips cost about three times as much as the 2 GB chips used so far. With the more expensive memory, the card would have had to launch at a price that would barely sell. The familiar 16 GB RTX 5080 is therefore said to stay in production. According to earlier rumors, the 24 GB model would have had the same number of compute units but more memory, more bandwidth and slightly higher clocks. PC Gamer points out that it was previously even said the 24 GB version could replace the RTX 5090 and the 16 GB variant; however, Nvidia executive Jeff Fisher had stressed that RTX 5090 production has not been discontinued. According to TechPowerUp, no Super refresh is in sight, and the next big step would be the RTX 60 series. Important: the 24 GB model itself was never officially announced, so this is a rumor about the end of a rumor. Nvidia has not commented.", "ursprungsquelle": "Board Channels (via VideoCardz, Gazlog, harukaze5719)", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "PC Games Hardware", "Wccftech"], "_src": "2c9fc45e"}, "2026-11-11-gta6-de-cix-rekord": {"titel": "GTA 6 pre-load: internet exchange DE-CIX measures new data record", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 download breaks record: 22.3 terabits per second in Frankfurt", "kurz": "On the first evening of the GTA 6 pre-load, the DE-CIX internet exchange in Frankfurt measured a new peak of 22.30 terabits per second. The operator also reports a worldwide record. GTA 6 is playable from midnight on November 19.", "zusammenfassung": "The start of the Grand Theft Auto VI pre-load has left measurable traces on the internet. As the DE-CIX operator told Golem on request, the Frankfurt exchange reached a new peak of 22.30 terabits per second on November 10 at 8:20 pm. That is 19.06 percent more than the previous high since January 2026. Across all DE-CIX locations worldwide, 33.01 terabits per second were measured, also a record. DE-CIX CTO Thomas King explained that big game launches are among the events that can make traffic rise sharply very quickly. By data throughput, DE-CIX Frankfurt is considered Europe's largest internet exchange. The pre-load for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S started in the night to November 10, and the file is around 210 to 212 GB. According to PC Games, a German internet provider also reported a multiple of its usual gaming traffic. GTA 6 is playable from midnight on November 19. Whether launch day itself brings new records remains to be seen.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games"], "_src": "b0fe5f64"}, "2026-11-11-mh-wilds-ascendance-beta": {"titel": "Steam changes point to a beta for the Monster Hunter Wilds expansion Ascendance", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Monster Hunter Wilds: Ascendance getting a beta soon?", "kurz": "Capcom has quietly renamed the old Monster Hunter Wilds beta app on Steam to “Ascendance Beta test”, as SteamDB shows. This points to an upcoming test of the expansion. Capcom has not announced anything yet, and a date is unknown.", "zusammenfassung": "The first big expansion for Monster Hunter Wilds is called Ascendance and is due in 2027. According to Eurogamer and PC Gamer, Capcom has now renamed the old beta app of the main game on Steam. According to the SteamDB change log, it is now called Monster Hunter Wilds: Ascendance Beta test and has received new key art. This points to an upcoming beta test. Because the app has the same ID as the earlier Wilds beta, it could reappear in former testers' libraries; a separate sign-up might then not be necessary. When a beta could start is completely open; Eurogamer cautiously guesses early 2027. Capcom last showed Ascendance in the September State of Play and at Tokyo Game Show, including the returning Elder Dragon Teostra. The expansion is meant to be more challenging after many players found the main game too easy at launch. These are hints from Steam data, not an official announcement.", "ursprungsquelle": "SteamDB-Änderungsprotokoll (via PC Gamer)", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "2faf2355"}, "2026-11-11-radeon-ssd-fix-tool": {"titel": "Unofficial open-source tool stops atieclxx.exe from constantly writing to the SSD", "schlagzeile": "Radeon driver wears out your SSD: free tool stops the constant writes", "kurz": "A community developer has released a free tool on GitHub against the Radeon bug in which atieclxx.exe copies itself to the SSD every second. It checks whether the PC is affected, estimates the wear and blocks the writes without disabling the service. It is an unofficial workaround, not from AMD.", "zusammenfassung": "On some PCs with a Radeon driver or AMD chipset driver, the file atieclxx.exe, which belongs to the AMD External Events Utility service, copies itself every second. This creates a constant write load on the system drive, and hundreds of gigabytes can quickly add up even without use, which ages SSDs unnecessarily. A community member called Necandi has now released the tool Radeon-atieclxx-SSD-Fix on GitHub, as ComputerBase and Wccftech report. It first checks whether the system is affected and estimates the SSD wear so far. This estimate is rough: it assumes the bug has existed since the AMD card was installed and, if the SSD reports no runtime, calculates with eight hours of operation per day. Instead of disabling the service, the tool only forbids the system account from overwriting the copy. As a result, the copy attempt fails, and FreeSync, frame pacing and hotkeys should keep working. Previous workarounds such as stopping the service or disabling Resizable BAR could cause problems exactly there. Anyone who does not want a tool can, according to ComputerBase, also revoke the rights themselves with an icacls command and restore them later. The developer stresses that he has nothing to do with AMD and that use is at your own risk. AMD has announced an official fix with driver 26.11.1, which is still pending.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "3c8c1851"}, "2026-11-11-zen6-epyc-tests": {"titel": "AMD Epyc 9006 Venice on sale: first tests show big leaps for Zen 6", "schlagzeile": "First Zen 6 tests: AMD's 256-core chip is 58% faster than its predecessor", "kurz": "AMD is now officially selling the Epyc 9006 Venice server processors with Zen 6. In Phoronix's first independent tests, the top model Epyc 9996 was on average 1.58 times as fast as the previous Zen 5c flagship. For gamers, this is a first look at the architecture of future Ryzen chips.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD has announced the sales launch of the sixth Epyc generation, codenamed Venice, which was already presented in July. It starts with nine models for the SP7 socket; according to Golem, another 22 for SP8 will follow in early 2027. Phoronix was allowed to test the two top models. The Epyc 9996 has 256 Zen 6c cores, up to 4.1 GHz and a 600-watt TDP and costs 14,904 US dollars according to AMD's list. In a dual-socket system, it averaged 1.58 times the performance of its predecessor, the 192-core Epyc 9965, across all benchmarks. In HPC applications it was about twice as fast as Intel's Xeon 6980P and delivered the best performance per watt despite higher power draw. According to Golem, the compact cores benefit from larger chiplets with 32 instead of 12 cores. The second chip tested, the Epyc 9686F, has 96 Zen 6 cores at up to 5.3 GHz. For gamers these are server chips, but they show independently for the first time what the Zen 6 architecture delivers, which is later also expected in Ryzen processors. How much of this reaches games cannot be derived from server benchmarks. Phoronix also points out that full performance requires fast MRDIMM memory, which is likely to be very expensive in the current RAM crisis.", "weitere_links": ["Phoronix (Epyc 9996 review)", "PC Games Hardware", "AMD on X"], "_src": "f935df7f"}, "2026-11-11-zelda-oot-5-2-mio": {"titel": "Zelda: Ocarina of Time remake sells more than 5.2 million copies in four days", "schlagzeile": "Zelda remake breaks Switch 2 record: 5.2 million in just four days", "kurz": "Nintendo reports more than 5.2 million copies of the Ocarina of Time remake sold in the first four days. That is the fastest sales launch of a Nintendo game on Switch 2. According to Nintendo, these are actual sales, not just shipments to retail.", "zusammenfassung": "The remake of The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time is a big success for Nintendo. According to a press release from the company, more than 5.2 million copies were sold worldwide in the first four days after launch on November 5. That makes it the most successful sales launch of a Nintendo-published Switch 2 game, according to Golem both worldwide and in Europe. According to Golem, Nintendo is talking about units actually sold, not just shipments to retail. There is no breakdown by region or between digital and physical. The record explicitly refers to Nintendo's own games, as Eurogamer stresses. The remake is also very well received by critics: Golem cites a Metacritic average of 96 points. New features include graphics, soundtrack, voice acting and reworked combat. The success is also remarkable because the game came out only two weeks before GTA 6. The remake is part of the celebrations for the Zelda series' 40th anniversary.", "weitere_links": ["Golem.de", "IGN Deutschland"], "_src": "6dbb5df2"}, "2026-11-11-ps5-100-millionen": {"titel": "Sony confirms: PlayStation 5 has sold more than 100 million units", "schlagzeile": "PS5 passes 100 million – now just behind the original PlayStation", "kurz": "Sony has confirmed that more than 100 million PS5 consoles had been shipped to retailers as of November 10. That puts it ahead of the PS3 and PSP and just behind the original PlayStation at 102.4 million. Recently, though, sales have been noticeably slower than a year earlier.", "zusammenfassung": "The PlayStation 5 has reached a milestone: according to Sony's official sales overview, more than 100 million consoles had been shipped by November 10, 2026. The figure counts shipments to retailers (sell-in), not sales to end customers. The PS5 has thus overtaken the PS3 (87.4 million) and the PSP (76.4 million). The original PlayStation is only just ahead at 102.4 million, while the PS4 at 117 million and the PS2 at more than 160 million are well ahead. The pace has slowed recently: according to Insider Gaming, 1.6 million units were shipped in the first quarter of the fiscal year instead of 2.5 million, and 2.6 million instead of 4 million in the second. The strongest year was fiscal 2023 with 20.8 million consoles. Sony also reports 127 million monthly active PlayStation users as of September 30. On the software side, PS4 and PS5 stand at 154.3 million units sold after two quarters of the current fiscal year. How strongly GTA 6 boosts console sales from November 19 will only show in the third-quarter figures.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming"], "_src": "0a83a0a1"}, "2026-11-11-nvidia-aktie-china-chips": {"titel": "Nvidia stock at its lowest since March: report says more than 240,000 AI systems reached China through a network of companies", "schlagzeile": "Nvidia stock keeps falling: chips worth $7.5B said to have gone to China", "kurz": "After two losing days, Nvidia stock closed at 168.89 US dollars on Tuesday, its lowest level since late March. Microsoft briefly overtook it in market value. According to a report by The Information, the woman with whom Jensen Huang admitted an affair is said to have brought Nvidia systems worth at least 7.5 billion dollars to China.", "zusammenfassung": "The scandal surrounding Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang keeps weighing on the company's stock. After falling more than 4 percent on Monday, the stock dropped another 5.5 percent on Tuesday and closed at 168.89 US dollars, its lowest level since March 30. That leaves the market value just above 4 trillion dollars; in early October it was still more than 5.5 trillion. Microsoft was briefly ahead of Nvidia on Tuesday, and Apple had already passed it before the allegations became public. The trigger is a new report by The Information, citing two people who know Alice Huang, with whom the Nvidia CEO has admitted an affair. She is said to have enabled shipments of more than 240,000 A100, H100 and H200 systems worth at least 7.5 billion dollars to China through a network of companies. A100 and H100 have been subject to US export restrictions since October 2022. According to the report, the Chinese data center company Century Litong and the Singapore-based firm Megaspeed, one of Nvidia's preferred cloud partners since October 2023, played a role. US agencies are reportedly pushing to put Megaspeed on a blacklist. China rejects the espionage allegation. Nvidia has launched an internal investigation, which an analyst quoted by CNBC expects to take four to six weeks. The same analyst puts the probability that Huang loses his post at about 15 percent. The figures on the chip shipments come from anonymous sources and have not been officially confirmed.", "weitere_links": ["heise online (report on the China shipments)"], "_src": "3a8f3e41"}, "2026-11-11-fortis-games-schliessung": {"titel": "Mobile studio Fortis Games closes, around 440 jobs affected as backer Las Vegas Sands ends funding", "schlagzeile": "Fortis Games shuts down – around 440 jobs lost as casino giant pulls funding", "kurz": "Mobile studio Fortis Games, founded in 2022, has closed, affecting around 440 jobs. According to a former employee, backer Las Vegas Sands ended funding and terminated all contracts worldwide. The studio's two games were still in an early test phase.", "zusammenfassung": "Another major closure in the games industry: Fortis Games is gone, affecting around 440 jobs. CEO Steven Chiang confirmed the closure to GamesBeat on November 10. He said the team was disappointed not to have reached its goals after more than five years and would now focus on helping staff find new jobs. A former producer wrote on LinkedIn that parent company Las Vegas Sands had decided to end funding and terminate all contracts worldwide. The San Francisco studio was founded in 2022 by Chiang, who previously worked at Electronic Arts and Zynga. Fortis was working on the mobile games Twilight Towers and Bloom & Breakfast, which were in an early soft launch; according to the producer, with solid metrics. A former communications director wrote, however, that the community-focused approach did not resonate enough with players. What happens to the two games is unknown.", "_src": "2298d3f0"}, "2026-11-11-windows11-speicherintegritaet": {"titel": "Windows 11 now turns on Memory Integrity (HVCI) automatically on more PCs, a protection that can slow down games", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 turns on Memory Integrity – what it means for gamers", "kurz": "With the November update, Windows 11 automatically enables Memory Integrity (HVCI) on more existing PCs. The protection blocks tampered drivers, but by Microsoft's own account it can cost performance in games. If you deliberately turned it off, it stays off, and it can still be disabled.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft is tightening a security setting that affects gamers. Since the optional October update, and now with the Patch Tuesday update KB5132061, Windows 11 can automatically enable Memory Integrity, also called HVCI, during updates. Until now it was mostly active only on new PCs and clean installs. According to Windows Latest, the change applies to Windows 11 25H2 and 26H2. Memory Integrity runs in an area isolated by the Windows hypervisor and checks there whether drivers and kernel code are trustworthy, so even a hijacked kernel cannot run unverified code. Some PCs will also get virtualization-based security (VBS) turned on for this. Before enabling it, Windows checks hardware, driver compatibility and performance, and the rollout is gradual. If you turned the feature off yourself before, Windows will not turn it back on; enterprise policies take precedence. The catch for gamers: Microsoft itself recommended a few years ago in a support article to turn off Memory Integrity for better gaming performance. It can be turned off under Windows Security, Device security, Core isolation details. Whether you should is a trade-off, because the protection targets malware that sneaks into the core of Windows through drivers.", "_src": "0b7240ab"}, "2026-11-10-fairgames-eingestellt": {"titel": "Sony cancels live-service shooter Fairgames after a disappointing playtest, no layoffs at Haven Studios", "schlagzeile": "Sony pulls the plug on Fairgames – another live-service shooter is gone", "kurz": "PlayStation has stopped development of Haven Studios' heist shooter Fairgames. According to an internal email reported by Bloomberg, player feedback and retention in a playtest fell short of its goals. There will reportedly be no layoffs; the studio will support other Sony teams.", "zusammenfassung": "Fairgames is history. Sony has ended development of the live-service shooter three years after its 2023 announcement, as Bloomberg first reported. An internal email from PlayStation executives Sean Decker and John Doyle says a recent playtest was convincing technically and organizationally, but feedback and player retention were mixed and fell short of the goals. Together with the difficult market for PvP shooters, they decided not to continue. According to the reports, developer Haven Studios will not be closed and no layoffs are planned; the team will instead support other Sony studios. Haven was founded in 2021 by Jade Raymond, who has since left the studio, and acquired by Sony in 2022. Fairgames is said to have been reworked several times since its reveal, and internal tests reportedly went poorly as early as 2025. Real gameplay was never officially shown, only rendered scenes from the announcement trailer. Sony's live-service strategy in 2022 planned at least ten such games by 2026. Alongside hits like Helldivers 2, there are now many cancelled projects and the Concord debacle.", "weitere_links": ["Polygon", "IGN"], "_src": "ff8dd113"}, "2026-11-10-nvidia-tsmc-bestellungen": {"titel": "Report from Taiwan: Nvidia could cut chip orders at TSMC, AMD and ASIC designers would benefit", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Nvidia cutting its chip orders at TSMC?", "kurz": "Taiwan's Commercial Times reports, citing unnamed supply chain sources, that Nvidia could order fewer chips from TSMC. It points to pressure from the scandal surrounding Jensen Huang and stricter export reviews. The report does not name a product, process node, volume or timeframe. Nvidia and TSMC have not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "Nvidia could scale back its orders at contract manufacturer TSMC. That is what the Taiwanese newspaper Commercial Times reports, citing unnamed supply chain sources; TechPowerUp picked up the report. It does not say which products, process node, volumes or timeframe are involved. As reasons, the report cites pressure from inside and outside: internally the scandal surrounding Jensen Huang and the Nvidia board's investigation, externally stricter export reviews. H200 chips are also said to be stockpiled in Hong Kong. The suspicion that some companies approved for H200 could be shell companies is mentioned too, but explicitly as a suspicion rather than a finding. If Nvidia gives up capacity, the newspaper expects AMD and developers of custom AI chips such as MediaTek, Alchip and GUC to take it. Suppliers such as TSMC and ASE would be hit hardest by cuts. For gamers this would not automatically mean cheaper graphics cards, because the memory that is currently scarce does not come from TSMC. The report relies on a single source; Nvidia and TSMC have not commented on it. Until confirmed, it should be treated as a rumor.", "ursprungsquelle": "Commercial Times (Taiwan), via TechPowerUp", "_src": "a929a8ec"}, "2026-11-10-gta6-xbox-fsr4-dateien": {"titel": "Dataminers find AMD FSR libraries in GTA 6's Xbox package, whether FSR 4.1.2 is used remains open", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Does GTA 6 on Xbox already use AMD's AI upscaling FSR 4?", "kurz": "GTA 6's Xbox preload contains two AMD files whose names match the FSR 4.1.2 integration for Xbox Series X|S. That is a hint, not proof: the game files are encrypted, and the same interface can also fall back to the older FSR 3.1. Rockstar has not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "Shortly after GTA 6's Xbox preload started, dataminers discovered two AMD libraries in the installation package: amd_fidelityfx_loader_xbox.dll and amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_xbox.dll. They were found by dataminer Tex2, and other users compared the names with the documentation for FSR 4.1.2 on Xbox Series X|S. VideoCardz reported it first, and PC Games Hardware put the find into context. AMD and Microsoft released FSR 4.1.2 for Xbox on November 4; it is the first AI-based upscaler for the consoles and comes with two INT8 models, Full and Lite. However, the file names do not prove that GTA 6 actually uses FSR 4.1.2. The same AMD SDK also contains the classic FSR 3.1.6, and the interface can fall back to it. Since the game files are encrypted, the contents of the libraries cannot be checked yet. For consoles, Rockstar has so far only confirmed 30 fps on all models and PSSR on the PS5 Pro; there is no official statement on upscaling on Xbox. Analyses should show which method is used by the launch on November 19 at the latest.", "ursprungsquelle": "Dataminer Tex2 (X), first reported by VideoCardz", "_src": "548f3594"}, "2026-11-10-patchday-november-1235": {"titel": "Microsoft Patch Tuesday November 2026: 1,235 flaws fixed, including an actively exploited Outlook zero-day", "schlagzeile": "Record Patch Tuesday: 1,235 flaws – Outlook bug already exploited", "kurz": "Microsoft fixed 1,235 security flaws on November's Patch Tuesday, 66 of them critical. A spoofing flaw in Outlook is already being exploited to steal NTLM account data. Windows 11 gets KB5132061 and KB5131087, Windows 10 in the ESU program gets KB5131096.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft's November Patch Tuesday is huge again: according to BleepingComputer, the updates fix 1,235 security flaws; another 108 were fixed earlier in the month and are not counted. October even had 1,411; Microsoft increasingly uses AI to find vulnerabilities. 66 flaws are rated critical, 48 of which allow remote code execution. Around 639 affect Windows and Windows components. Most urgent is a spoofing flaw in Microsoft Outlook that is already being attacked. According to Microsoft, it is enough for a victim to open a crafted message file: Outlook then connects to an attacker's server without the usual warning and can leak credentials in the form of NTLM hashes. Windows 11 receives the cumulative updates KB5132061 and KB5131087, Windows 10 22H2 in the Extended Security Updates program gets KB5131096. For some users, installing KB5132061 fails with error 0x800f0993, according to Neowin. Anyone using Windows or Office should still install the updates soon, especially because of the Outlook flaw.", "weitere_links": ["Dr. Windows", "Neowin (installation error)"], "_src": "e3b7656c"}, "2026-11-10-fritzbox-5690-pro-speicher": {"titel": "Fritz!Box 5690 Pro: support data shows newer units with only half the RAM and flash, under the same article number", "schlagzeile": "Fritz!Box 5690 Pro: newer units with half the memory – same article number", "kurz": "Newer units of the Fritz!Box 5690 Pro apparently have only 1 GB RAM and 2 GB flash instead of 2 and 4 GB. Article number and hardware version are the same; the difference only shows in the hardware subrevision. Fritz speaks of industry-standard adjustments with no effect on performance.", "zusammenfassung": "If you buy a Fritz!Box 5690 Pro today, you don't necessarily get the same hardware as buyers at launch. A user with two units noticed: the newer one showed much higher RAM usage on the same Fritz!OS version. According to the support data, a unit from July 2024 has 2 GB RAM and 4 GB flash, one from June 2026 only 1 GB RAM and 2 GB flash. Usable system RAM accordingly drops from 1,754 to 742 MB, and internal storage, used for example by Fritz!NAS, shrinks from about 1.7 GB to 680 MB. The variants can only be told apart by the hardware subrevision, which rose from 3 to 5; article number and hardware version are the same, and the routers look identical from the outside. When exactly the switch happened is unclear; at times both variants appear to have shipped in parallel. Fritz told Router-FAQ.de that internal components such as memory chips are occasionally adjusted over a product's life cycle; that is common in the industry and does not change specification or performance. The company did not explicitly confirm the specific halving. There are no comparison tests of both variants yet, and whether this affects future updates is also open. It is still awkward, because Fritz explicitly advertised the large memory capacity at launch in June 2024.", "_src": "aa5e40e9"}, "2026-11-10-auto-sr-xbox-ally-ryzen": {"titel": "Microsoft Auto SR leaves preview on ROG Xbox Ally X and X20 and comes to Copilot+ PCs with AMD Ryzen, new mode up to 120 fps", "schlagzeile": "Windows upscaling Auto SR: now handheld, with HDR and up to 120 fps", "kurz": "Microsoft's AI upscaling Auto SR has officially launched on the ROG Xbox Ally X and X20 handhelds. New are a performance mode with up to 120 fps, handheld use without a dock and the combination with Auto HDR. Auto SR now also runs on selected Copilot+ PCs with AMD Ryzen.", "zusammenfassung": "On the DirectX blog, Microsoft announced the official launch of Automatic Super Resolution (Auto SR) on the ROG Xbox Ally X and ROG Xbox Ally X20 handhelds. Auto SR runs games internally at a lower resolution and upscales them with AI on the NPU, without the game needing to support it. Until now, the feature was only available as a preview and only when docked. Now it also works on the built-in screen and on battery. Games running at 1080p are supported as well, and on a monitor Auto SR can then upscale to 1440p. A new performance mode raises the limit from around 60 to 75 fps so far to up to 120 fps; in Microsoft's Rocket League example, the average rose from 70 to 115 fps. In addition, Auto SR and Auto HDR can be used at the same time for the first time. Handheld use, 1080p and the new AMD Ryzen Copilot+ PCs are available now. Performance mode and Auto HDR support will roll out gradually with Windows updates. Current Windows 11 updates, an up-to-date Game Bar and the Auto Super Resolution package from the Microsoft Store are required.", "_src": "539f5a74"}, "2026-11-10-gpu-taskman-vram": {"titel": "GPU Taskman: open-source tool shows exactly which programs use how much graphics memory", "schlagzeile": "What's eating your VRAM? Free tool shows it per program", "kurz": "Microsoft and GitHub developer Scott Hanselman has released the open-source tool GPU Taskman. It shows per program how much graphics memory is in use, plus GPU load, temperature and clock speed. The tool is still experimental.", "zusammenfassung": "Scott Hanselman, Vice President at Microsoft and GitHub, has developed GPU Taskman, a free command-line tool. It is meant to show more precisely than the Windows Task Manager where graphics memory goes. It displays VRAM usage, system memory used by the GPU and the individual processes, plus load, temperature, power draw, clock speed and PCIe values. The tool distinguishes between the desktop, browsers, games and AI applications, for example. For local AI models in llama.cpp, Ollama or LM Studio, it can estimate the memory for model weights and KV cache separately. For gamers, it can help find VRAM bottlenecks that cause stuttering. Hanselman warns, however, that system RAM in use does not automatically mean a VRAM overflow, and the tool cannot identify individual textures. GPU Taskman supports NVIDIA and AMD cards on Windows 10 and 11, plus Linux, WSL and Apple Silicon Macs; version 0.3.5 adds Intel GPUs on Linux. It is available under the MIT license on GitHub, with a portable version for Windows. The software is still experimental, and some values are estimates.", "_src": "43537581"}, "2026-11-10-ps-plus-pc-app-ende": {"titel": "Sony is shutting down the PlayStation Plus app for PC on December 10, Death Stranding 2 joins the Extra catalog", "schlagzeile": "PS Plus streaming on PC is ending – only 0.4% used it", "kurz": "Sony is shutting down the PlayStation Plus app for Windows on December 10, 2026, ending the streaming of PS Plus games to PC. According to Sony, fewer than 0.4 percent of Premium members used the app. In the same post, Sony announces the new Extra and Premium games, led by Death Stranding 2.", "zusammenfassung": "At the very end of its post about the new PS Plus games for November, Sony announced the end of the PC app. From December 10, the PlayStation Plus app for PC will no longer be available, and with it the cloud streaming of PS Plus Premium games to Windows computers. Sony cites low usage as the reason: fewer than 0.4 percent of eligible Premium members had used the app. Memberships and benefits on PS5 and PS4 are not affected, and Sony says it will notify affected users directly. This removes one way to play PlayStation games on PC without a console. New in the Extra and Premium catalog in November are Death Stranding 2: On the Beach, Atomfall and Dragon Quest III HD-2D Remake, among others. Hell Let Loose follows on November 11, Like a Dragon: Pirate Yakuza in Hawaii, Trepang2, MotoGP 26 and Cricket 26 on November 24. Soul Reaver 2 and Freedom Wars Remastered are added for Premium only.", "weitere_links": ["Eurogamer", "PlayStation on X"], "_src": "235d58ff"}, "2026-11-10-amd-zen6-ipc-epyc": {"titel": "AMD reveals Zen 6 architecture: 27 percent more IPC, Epyc 9006 “Venice” launches with up to 256 cores", "schlagzeile": "Zen 6 is here: AMD promises 27% more IPC – server Epyc comes first", "kurz": "AMD has revealed the technology behind Zen 6 and cites 27 percent more IPC than Zen 5. The first Zen 6 chips are the Epyc 9006 “Venice” server processors with up to 256 cores and up to 5.3 GHz. The IPC figure comes from an unusual comparison by AMD. AMD has not said anything yet about Ryzen desktop CPUs with Zen 6.", "zusammenfassung": "With the embargo lifted this evening, AMD published many details about the Zen 6 architecture. According to AMD, IPC, meaning performance per clock, rises by 27 percent on average over Zen 5, with around 20 percent in regular applications and around 31 percent in AI workloads. ComputerBase and heise point out, however, that AMD compared 16 Zen 6c cores in a single chiplet with 16 Zen 5 cores across two chiplets, which is not a classic IPC comparison. Technically the core gets wider: the op cache grows to 6,750 entries and delivers 18 instead of 12 micro-ops per clock, while the register file and reorder buffer grow to 352 and 640 entries. AVX-512 stays, and so does SMT. The regular Zen 6 cores come twelve to a chiplet with 48 MB of L3 cache, the compact Zen 6c cores 32 to a chiplet with 128 MB of L3, made on TSMC's 2 nm process. The first products are the Epyc 9006 “Venice” server CPUs with up to 256 cores, 16 DDR5 memory channels, PCIe 6.0 and up to 600 watts. The high-frequency models reach up to 5.3 GHz. AMD says it is already shipping, and the first systems are due this year. In heise's first remote measurements, a single Zen 5 core took around 22 percent longer in Blender than a Zen 6 core, which however also runs at a higher clock. In 2027 a smaller platform follows, along with Venice-X with 3D V-Cache and Verano with LPDDR5X memory. After that, the roadmap lists Zen 7 “Florence” for 2028 and Zen 8 “Ravenna”. AMD said nothing at the event about Ryzen processors for desktops and notebooks with Zen 6 or their timing.", "weitere_links": ["heise online", "AMD on X"], "_src": "d9fcfe1b"}, "2026-11-10-amd-mext-flash-statt-ram": {"titel": "AMD MEXT: software moves rarely used memory to flash to save expensive DRAM", "schlagzeile": "RAM crisis: AMD wants to save up to 75% of DRAM with flash storage", "kurz": "AMD has introduced MEXT, software that moves rarely used memory pages from DRAM to flash SSDs. This is meant to let servers run almost as fast with much less expensive memory. For now the offer only applies to Epyc servers. All performance figures come from AMD.", "zusammenfassung": "With MEXT, AMD is responding to the ongoing memory shortage. According to AMD, DRAM accounts for 75 to 90 percent of a server's cost depending on configuration, while a large share of the memory is unused or oversized. MEXT detects “cold” memory pages and moves them to flash storage, meaning NVMe SSDs. AI models are meant to predict which data will be needed again soon and bring it back into DRAM in time. According to Wccftech, the software consists of a Linux driver, an AI engine that runs on a single Epyc core, and a monitoring tool. AMD says this can cut DRAM requirements by 20 to 75 percent with similar performance. In a chip design example, a server with half the DRAM is said to still reach 95 percent of the performance. These figures are manufacturer claims, and independent tests are still missing. According to Phoronix, the Linux driver is not open source. For now, MEXT is intended only for Epyc servers with NVMe drives, and a license is to follow later. AMD hinted that something like this could also become interesting for regular PCs, but there are no concrete plans for it.", "weitere_links": ["ComputerBase", "Phoronix"], "_src": "f9b8ff0f"}, "2026-11-10-gta6-vorbestell-rekord-xbox-cloud": {"titel": "GTA 6 is the most pre-ordered game in their stores according to Sony and Microsoft, Xbox One gets it via the cloud, Xbox signs 10-year partnership with Take-Two", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 breaks pre-order records – and even comes to Xbox One via the cloud", "kurz": "Sony and Microsoft report that GTA 6 is the most pre-ordered game in the history of the PlayStation Store and the Microsoft Store. Via Xbox Cloud Gaming it will also run on the old Xbox One at launch. Xbox CEO Asha Sharma speaks of a new 10-year partnership with Take-Two. Nobody gives concrete sales figures.", "zusammenfassung": "On the PlayStation Blog, Sony writes that GTA 6 is the most pre-ordered game in the history of the PlayStation Store. Microsoft reports the same for the Microsoft Store on Xbox Wire. Neither gives numbers; Take-Two most recently only said that pre-orders were far above expectations. Because of the expected rush, Sony and Microsoft advise preloading the game as early as possible. On PlayStation, GTA 6 launches on November 19 at midnight local time, starting in New Zealand. Xbox Cloud Gaming offers the game from November 19 at 1 a.m. US Eastern Time, i.e. 7 a.m. in Austria, on Xbox One and Xbox Series X|S, with Series S graphics settings. Streaming to PC or smartphones is not planned. On X, Xbox CEO Asha Sharma called this the “first step” of a new 10-year strategic partnership with Take-Two, without giving details. According to Xbox Wire, more Rockstar games such as GTA V and Red Dead Redemption 2 will come to Xbox Cloud Gaming in the coming months. From November 11, players in supported countries can also buy cloud playtime without a Game Pass subscription.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation.Blog", "Asha Sharma on X", "IGN"], "_src": "1f6dc907"}, "2026-11-10-eu-dfa-lootboxen-entwurf": {"titel": "Leaked draft of the EU Digital Fairness Act: loot boxes off by default for minors, pay-to-win banned for children", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Does the EU want to switch off loot boxes for kids by default?", "kurz": "An alleged draft of the EU's Digital Fairness Act has surfaced early. It proposes that loot boxes be switched off by default for minors and that all players can turn them off. The official presentation is planned for November 11, and it is far from being law.", "zusammenfassung": "The French trade publication Contexte has published an alleged draft of the Digital Fairness Act, and Eurogamer reports on it. According to Eurogamer, the EU Commission intends to officially present the proposal on November 11. The draft targets unfair practices in the digital world, including monetization in games. All players are to be able to turn off loot boxes, meaning rewards with random contents; for minors they are to be off by default. Pay-to-progress and pay-to-win mechanics are not to be offered to children if a product is aimed at them or the provider knows that minors use it. For virtual currencies, the real price of purchases is to be made transparent, along with the odds of winning for loot boxes. The text also foresees a mandatory age rating for games. Besides games, it covers influencer advertising, hidden prices and subscriptions that are hard to cancel. Important: this is a leaked draft that may still change before the presentation. Negotiations follow; according to Eurogamer, the law could be adopted at the end of 2027 and applied broadly by 2030.", "ursprungsquelle": "Contexte (via Video Games Industry Memo)", "_src": "792e7165"}, "2026-11-10-asrock-vbios-tool-1-0-6": {"titel": "ASRock releases VBIOS flash tool 1.0.6 for RX 7900 XT/XTX after version 1.0.5 bricked cards", "schlagzeile": "After bricked RX 7900 XTX cards: ASRock ships a new BIOS tool – no explanation", "kurz": "ASRock has released the ASRVBFlash 1.0.6 flash tool for the Radeon RX 7900 XT and XTX. According to user reports, the previous version 1.0.5 had killed cards after the update. ASRock does not say what has changed or what the cause was.", "zusammenfassung": "In early November, reports piled up that ASRock Radeon RX 7900 XT and XTX cards no longer started after an official VBIOS update. The culprit was the ASRVBFlash 1.0.5 flash tool: after the restart, the system no longer booted. ASRock then apparently pulled the version from its download pages. Now version 1.0.6 has quietly appeared, which according to TechPowerUp is meant to prevent the bricking and correctly apply the firmware update for better security. There is no changelog or explanation of the cause, which PCGH also criticizes. It remains unclear how ASRock handles cards that are already broken. According to TechPowerUp, a customer in Japan was told that a card destroyed by the official update is covered by warranty. A customer in Europe, by contrast, was told that removing the cooler to reflash the BIOS chip voids the warranty. Affected users should therefore go the RMA route instead of tinkering themselves. Anyone who has not updated yet can also wait for other users' experiences with 1.0.6.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware", "Wccftech"], "_src": "a328de5f"}, "2026-11-10-gta6-30fps-ps5-pro": {"titel": "Rockstar confirms: GTA 6 targets 30 fps on all consoles, PS5 Pro gets PSSR and exclusive ray-traced shadows", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 runs at 30 fps – on PS5 Pro too, but with ray-traced shadows", "kurz": "Rockstar has confirmed that GTA 6 targets 30 frames per second on all consoles, including the PS5 Pro. In return, the Pro gets sharper images via PSSR and exclusive ray-traced shadows. Preloading has been live since today, and the launch is on November 19.", "zusammenfassung": "As preloading began, Rockstar Games officially explained GTA 6's console technology for the first time. The game was developed from the ground up for the current console generation and targets 30 frames per second while pushing both platforms “to their absolute limits”. According to Rockstar, this applies to PS5, PS5 Pro, Xbox Series X and Series S. Rockstar does not mention a 60 fps mode. The PS5 Pro gets a sharper image through Sony's AI upscaling PSSR and ray-traced shadows that are exclusive to it. On PS5, GTA 6 uses the DualSense's haptics, adaptive triggers and speaker, plus Tempest 3D Audio; Rockstar and Sony say the game plays best on PS5. Remote Play is supported on PlayStation and Xbox. Via Xbox Cloud Gaming the game can be streamed on Xbox consoles with Series S graphics settings, but not on PC. Rockstar has still not announced a PC version. Depending on the console, the download needs up to 212 GB. There is also a new preload trailer with almost 30 seconds of new footage.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation.Blog", "Eurogamer", "Rockstar Games on X"], "_src": "1689ad08"}, "2026-11-10-steam-deck-framerate-daten": {"titel": "Steam now shows players' average Steam Deck frame rates on store pages", "schlagzeile": "Steam now shows real fps numbers – how well does a game run on the Deck?", "kurz": "Valve now shows the average frame rate on the Steam Deck for many games in Steam. The figures come from players who agreed to share the data. More devices are to follow later.", "zusammenfassung": "Valve has added a new performance display to Steam. In the Steam Deck compatibility section of a store page, clicking “Learn more” now shows the average frame rate on the Steam Deck. A histogram also shows how often each frame rate was measured, so fluctuations are visible too. The data comes from players who agreed to share frame rate data. The value is shown for games that Valve has reviewed for Deck compatibility, i.e. those rated Verified, Playable or Unsupported. Valve explains that the existing rating is based on fixed test criteria and does not match every player's standard for smooth gameplay. An “Unsupported” game may still be quite playable for some, while a Verified game may have low fps. According to Valve, the feature is to be extended to more devices in the future. Whether that includes regular desktop PCs with their many hardware combinations is open.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "GamingOnLinux"], "_src": "6dbc5420"}, "2026-11-10-msi-rtx50-preise-china": {"titel": "Report from China: MSI is said to sharply raise distributor prices for RTX 50 cards in November, RTX 5080 by up to 8,000 yuan", "schlagzeile": "Leak: MSI is said to raise RTX 5080 prices in China by up to 8,000 yuan", "kurz": "According to the Chinese industry channel ChannelGate, MSI is raising distributor prices of all RTX 50 cards in November. For the RTX 5080, the increase is said to be 1,300 to 8,000 yuan, roughly 190 to 1,200 US dollars. These are distributor prices in China, not official consumer prices. MSI has not confirmed this.", "zusammenfassung": "The Chinese industry channel ChannelGate (Board Channels) reports on new MSI price lists for November. According to it, distributor prices of all RTX 50 models in China rise compared with October. For the RTX 5080 series, 1,300 to 8,000 yuan more is cited, for the RTX 5070 Ti 800 to 4,000 yuan and for the RTX 5070 500 to 1,000 yuan. The RTX 5060 Ti is said to rise by 200 to 400 yuan depending on memory, the RTX 5060 by 200 to 500 yuan and even the RTX 3050 by 100 yuan. Wccftech converts the maximum for the RTX 5080 to around 1,200 US dollars. Important: the maximum only applies to individual models, and these are prices for retailers in China, not a new worldwide MSRP. Whether and how strongly this affects Europe is open. The report follows earlier ChannelGate reports about price increases by other board partners. The main reason is said to be the sharply higher memory prices. MSI itself has not commented, so it remains an unconfirmed report.", "ursprungsquelle": "ChannelGate / Board Channels (WeChat), via harukaze5719", "weitere_links": ["IT之家 (ChannelGate)", "TechRadar"], "_src": "59a47e79"}, "2026-11-10-arc-raiders-17-mio": {"titel": "Nexon: Arc Raiders has sold more than 17 million copies after one year, revenue expected to fall in the fourth quarter", "schlagzeile": "Arc Raiders tops 17 million – but sales are slowing", "kurz": "According to publisher Nexon, the extraction shooter Arc Raiders has sold more than 17 million copies by its first birthday. In the third quarter, however, only one million were added. Nexon expects lower revenue in the fourth quarter than at launch a year ago.", "zusammenfassung": "In its quarterly report, Nexon gave new figures for Arc Raiders by Embark Studios. The extraction shooter was released at the end of October 2025 and has since sold more than 17 million copies. According to Nexon, however, only around one million were added in the third quarter of 2026, so sales have slowed significantly. For the fourth quarter, Nexon expects lower revenue from the game than in the prior-year quarter, which included its successful launch. Compared with the previous quarter, revenue is expected to stay roughly flat. According to Nexon, revenue was within its outlook, and the Frozen Trail update brought back former players and won new ones. Arc Raiders remains one of Nexon's most important titles and was the main reason for the revenue growth in the first nine months of the year. It is still open whether a dedicated PvE mode will come permanently; it already exists in China.", "_src": "95842a04"}, "2026-11-10-nvidia-fbi-sammelklagen": {"titel": "Espionage suspicion around NVIDIA CEO Huang: according to Trump the FBI is looking into the case, law firms seek investors for lawsuits", "schlagzeile": "NVIDIA spy affair: FBI looks into the case, investor lawsuits loom", "kurz": "In the case of the alleged Chinese spy close to NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang, the FBI is now looking into it, according to US President Trump. Whether any investigation also targets Huang is unclear. Several US law firms are seeking investors for possible class actions against NVIDIA.", "zusammenfassung": "The affair involving NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang and the alleged Chinese spy Alice Huang is widening. According to Spiegel and Reuters, US President Donald Trump said the FBI is looking into the case. It is unclear whether the review also concerns Jensen Huang himself; despite the same surname, the two are not related. Trump defended Huang and said, in essence, that he believes him that he knew nothing about any spying. Huang had previously admitted the relationship and publicly apologized, and NVIDIA's board has started an investigation with outside experts. According to PC Gamer, several US law firms, including Rosen Law Firm, are recruiting investors for possible lawsuits over misleading statements. According to the Guardian, a lawsuit has already been filed in San José accusing NVIDIA and Huang of concealing a possible security risk. Alice Huang's employer, Megaspeed, is suspected of bringing NVIDIA chips into China without permission; NVIDIA and Megaspeed had previously denied this. According to PC Gamer, Huang is to testify behind closed doors before congressional committees on November 18. None of the allegations have been settled in court so far.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "79f7d817"}, "2026-11-10-chrome-zero-day": {"titel": "Chrome 157 fixes nine vulnerabilities, including the actively exploited CVE-2026-125350", "schlagzeile": "Chrome flaw already under attack – update to version 157 now", "kurz": "Google has released a Chrome update with nine security fixes. A flaw in the browser's XML component is already being actively exploited. Safe versions are 157.0.8103.50/.51 for Windows and Mac and 157.0.8103.50 for Linux.", "zusammenfassung": "Google has released a security update for Chrome that closes nine vulnerabilities, reports Golem. According to Google, at least one of them is already being actively exploited: CVE-2026-125350. It is a use-after-free bug in the component that processes XML data; the severity is rated high, but Google has not yet given a CVSS score. Google does not say how or against whom the flaw is being exploited. It is also unclear whether users have to click anything for an attack. Six of the remaining eight flaws are rated high and two medium; affected components include the V8 JavaScript engine, WebGL and interfaces to the GPU and file system. As usual, Google is holding back technical details until most users have updated. Safe versions are 157.0.8103.50/.51 for Windows and macOS and 157.0.8103.50 for Linux. Other Chromium browsers such as Edge, Vivaldi or Brave are likely affected too and should receive updates in the coming days. Tip: Help › About Google Chrome starts the update check; then restart the browser.", "_src": "3c9a011f"}, "2026-11-10-switch-eshop-geschenke": {"titel": "Switch system update 23.5.0 prepares a gifting feature in the Nintendo eShop for family groups", "schlagzeile": "Switch and Switch 2: gifting games is coming soon – but only within the family", "kurz": "With system update 23.5.0, Nintendo is preparing the ability to gift eShop games. The feature goes live with an eShop update in mid-November. Gifts can only go to members of your own family group.", "zusammenfassung": "Nintendo has released system update 23.5.0 for Switch 2 and the original Switch. It prepares a new feature: digital games, DLC and upgrade packs from the eShop can soon be given as gifts. The catch: recipients must be members of your own Nintendo Account family group, which has up to eight members. According to Nintendo, supervised child accounts cannot send gifts, some products are excluded and the number of gift purchases per period is limited; Nintendo does not give exact limits. When buying, you tick \"Give as a Gift\" on the product page, choose the recipient and their console and pay as usual. The gift arrives immediately in the recipient's HOME Menu. The feature is only activated with an eShop update: the patch notes name November 17, while Nintendo of America writes November 16, probably because of the time zone. On Switch 2, 23.5.0 also lets you set accessibility options during initial setup. Anyone who wants to give games to friends outside the family group still has to use eShop gift cards.", "weitere_links": ["VGChartz (patch notes)", "Nintendo of America on X (hint)"], "_src": "51b1c15b"}, "2026-11-10-mesa-26-3": {"titel": "Mesa 26.3 released: AMD Anti-Lag for RADV, Nova Lake graphics enabled by default, Vulkan Video for NVK", "schlagzeile": "Linux graphics driver Mesa 26.3: Anti-Lag for Radeon and more Vulkan", "kurz": "The open-source graphics driver collection Mesa 26.3 is out. Radeon users get the Vulkan extension for AMD Anti-Lag via RADV, and Intel Nova Lake graphics is no longer experimental. There is also Vulkan Video for the NVIDIA driver NVK and many Vulkan improvements.", "zusammenfassung": "Mesa 26.3 has been released, the fourth major release of the year of the open-source OpenGL and Vulkan drivers for Linux, report Phoronix and 9to5Linux. For gamers with a Radeon card, the most important new feature is VK_AMD_anti_lag in the RADV Vulkan driver, the Vulkan interface for AMD's Anti-Lag to reduce input latency. RADV also brings improvements for early GCN GPUs and support for GFX1171. On the Intel side, Nova Lake graphics is now enabled by default and no longer experimental, and the new Jay shader compiler is switched on. Intel also enables buffer compression, which according to Phoronix should improve gaming performance with DXVK, i.e. for Windows games via Proton. The open-source NVIDIA driver NVK gets Vulkan Video for video acceleration. There are also many new Vulkan extensions for Arm Mali, PowerVR and other drivers. Mesa 26.3 is available on FreeDesktop.org; most distributions will ship it with upcoming package updates. How much Anti-Lag brings in individual games depends on whether the game or translation layer uses it; no measurements are available yet.", "weitere_links": ["9to5Linux"], "_src": "24e0a075"}, "2026-11-10-take-two-ki-decompiling": {"titel": "Take-Two strengthens technical and legal defences against AI-assisted reverse engineering of GTA 6", "schlagzeile": "Unofficial GTA 6 PC port via AI? Take-Two steps up tech and legal defences", "kurz": "Take-Two boss Strauss Zelnick takes AI-assisted decompiling seriously and wants to strengthen technical protection and legal action. The background is concern that GTA 6 could appear unofficially on PC. Take-Two says nothing about an official PC version or a disc; that will come from Rockstar.", "zusammenfassung": "Ahead of the GTA 6 launch on November 19, there is growing concern that AI tools could decompile console games faster and spread them as unofficial PC ports. IGN asked Take-Two CEO Strauss Zelnick about this in an interview and during the investor Q&A. Zelnick says the industry was long largely spared from piracy because of file sizes, complexity and server connections, but that is becoming harder. Take-Two is therefore focusing on strengthening its technical defences and its legal activities. He expects piracy to affect the business \"to a greater or lesser extent\", but considers it manageable and does not see it as a financial threat. According to IGN, part of the concern relates to PS5 security: the homebrew scene is working on jailbreaks for newer firmware, and GTA 6 is said to require a recent firmware. Zelnick left open when GTA 6 will officially come to PC. According to Insider Gaming (citing Variety), he pointed out that such information always comes from the label, i.e. Rockstar; the same applies to a possible disc version. At launch, GTA 6 is only released for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. A former Rockstar North technical director recently speculated that Rockstar could bring a PC port forward for this reason, but that is not confirmed.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming"], "_src": "a25dcecd"}, "2026-11-10-sega-newsletter-leak": {"titel": "SEGA: attack on newsletter provider ARARA exposes around 2.2 million email addresses", "schlagzeile": "SEGA data leak: 2.2 million email addresses stolen from a service provider", "kurz": "In an attack on the Japanese newsletter provider ARARA, around 2.2 million email addresses of SEGA customers were stolen. According to SEGA, names, passwords and payment data are not affected, nor are SEGA Accounts. Customers should watch out for fake SEGA emails.", "zusammenfassung": "SEGA confirmed a data leak at its newsletter provider ARARA on November 9. 2,196,044 email addresses are affected; for 92,273 of them, information related to delivery also leaked, and exactly what is still being investigated. According to SEGA, it concerns eleven newsletters from SEGA and SEGA Fave sent between July and October 2026, for example about arcade games such as CHUNITHM and maimai, the Tokyo Game Show and lottery promotions. According to SEGA, names, dates of birth, addresses, phone numbers, credit card data and passwords are not affected. Email addresses from SEGA Account also run through a different system and are not part of the leak. Misuse of the data has not been confirmed so far. ARARA itself had reported the breach in early November; according to BleepingComputer and Infosecurity Magazine, around 77 million email addresses from about 380 corporate customers are affected there in total, apparently via a vulnerability in web servers. SEGA has suspended sending via ARARA and plans to inform those affected individually. Anyone who received SEGA newsletters should be especially alert to phishing in emails referring to SEGA.", "weitere_links": ["SEGA (notice, Japanese)", "Infosecurity Magazine"], "_src": "ba66609c"}, "2026-11-10-take-two-gta6-vorbestellungen": {"titel": "Take-Two: GTA 6 pre-orders far above expectations, up to $3.5 billion expected in the launch quarter", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: pre-orders \"far above expectations\" – Take-Two expects a record", "kurz": "Ten days before the launch of GTA 6, Take-Two reports pre-orders at \"unprecedented\" levels. For the current quarter the company expects net bookings of $3.35 to $3.5 billion. Take-Two still gives no concrete pre-order figures.", "zusammenfassung": "Take-Two presented its results for the second quarter of fiscal year 2027 on November 9, and GTA 6 was the centre of attention. According to CEO Strauss Zelnick, pre-orders are \"far above expectations\" and continue to reach \"unprecedented\" levels, report Insider Gaming, Eurogamer and PC Gamer. For the current third quarter, which includes the November 19 launch, Take-Two expects net bookings of $3.35 to $3.5 billion. According to PC Gamer, that is even slightly below the analyst estimate of $3.51 billion (LSEG, via Reuters). For the full fiscal year 2027 the company expects $8 to $8.2 billion. Take-Two still gives no concrete pre-order figures, because the raw numbers could be misleading without points of comparison. The past quarter was weaker: net bookings of $1.6 billion were below expectations and 18 percent below the previous year. One reason is NBA 2K27, which launched well but stayed below forecast; Zelnick sees anticipation for GTA 6 as a contributing factor. Take-Two also shared new sales figures: GTA 5 stands at around 235 million copies, and Red Dead Redemption 2 is approaching 90 million. The GTA series as a whole has sold almost 480 million units.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "Eurogamer", "Insider Gaming (GTA 5)", "Insider Gaming (RDR2)"], "_src": "38d7088e"}, "2026-11-10-skydance-games-entlassungen": {"titel": "Skydance Games lays off staff and scales down projects – one month after the Paramount–Warner Bros. merger", "schlagzeile": "After mega-merger: Skydance Games lays off developers and trims projects", "kurz": "Skydance Games has cut jobs and \"scaled down some of its projects\". This comes one month after the merger of Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery. The company does not say how many people are affected.", "zusammenfassung": "Skydance Games has confirmed layoffs, report IGN and PC Gamer, citing a statement to Variety. The company said it decided to scale down some projects, and roles are affected as a result; this is not a judgement on the talent or dedication of those affected. Employees of Paramount Games Studio, founded only in June, were the first to report that they had been let go. Paramount Games includes, among others, Skydance Interactive and Skydance New Media. Recently announced there were games such as Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles: The Last Ronin as well as adaptations of Yellowstone, Tulsa King and Lioness. It is not known which projects are being cut. Skydance does not say how many jobs are going; according to Insider Gaming, at least 30 developers are affected, probably more. The cuts come around a month after the merger of Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery under the Skydance umbrella was approved. What this means for the Warner Bros. Games division is still open.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "a7836025"}, "2026-11-10-rdna5-gfx13-linux": {"titel": "AMD publishes Linux driver patches for GFX13, the next-generation graphics IP (probably RDNA 5)", "schlagzeile": "RDNA 5 draws closer: AMD sends first Linux drivers for GFX13", "kurz": "AMD has published more than 12,600 lines of Linux kernel driver code for GFX13, the next Radeon graphics generation. Most likely this is RDNA 5. So far the patches reveal no new details on performance or features.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD developer Alex Deucher has published a patch series that prepares the AMDGPU Linux kernel driver for GFX13, report Phoronix and VideoCardz. GFX13 is AMD's next graphics IP and very likely stands for RDNA 5; AMD has not officially confirmed the name. The eight patches comprise more than 12,600 lines of code, excluding the usual large header files. They also include support for the specific variants GFX 13.0.1 and GFX 13.0.4. According to Phoronix, the patches reveal little so far about the capabilities or new features of RDNA 5. GFX13 patches for the LLVM compiler have existed since the beginning of the year; now the kernel driver follows. Phoronix expects support in Linux kernel 7.5. Other building blocks that are likely part of RDNA 5 GPUs, such as Display Core Next 6, are already in the kernel. AMD often publishes early Linux drivers months before market launch; AMD gives no date for RDNA 5 graphics cards.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz"], "_src": "c780eb89"}, "2026-11-10-nvidia-megaspeed-nyt": {"titel": "NYT report: NVIDIA allegedly intervened in US investigation into suspected AI chip smuggler Megaspeed", "schlagzeile": "Report: NVIDIA allegedly slowed an investigation into chip smuggling", "kurz": "According to the New York Times, NVIDIA's general counsel contacted the US Commerce Department directly in 2025 while it was investigating the company Megaspeed over suspected chip smuggling to China. The investigation stalled and was handed to the Justice Department. This is a report; we do not have a statement from NVIDIA.", "zusammenfassung": "After the report on the NVIDIA board's investigation involving CEO Jensen Huang, new pressure is building: according to Wccftech, the New York Times reports on NVIDIA's role in investigations into the company Megaspeed. The Singapore-based data centre company was suspected of acting as a front to move smuggled NVIDIA AI accelerators past US export controls into China. Megaspeed is run by Alice Huang, who according to US intelligence agencies worked for Beijing; she is the same woman with whom Jensen Huang has admitted an affair. According to the report, NVIDIA's general counsel Tim Teter contacted the Commerce Department's Bureau of Industry and Security directly in 2025. He reportedly claimed that Trump nominee Jeff Kessler had allowed him this direct contact. Several officials are said to have seen this as a serious breach of normal procedure. The investigation then stalled and was handed over to the Justice Department. Company lawyers talking to authorities is normal in itself; according to the report, the nature of the contact is what is disputed. According to Wccftech, Huang faces a closed-door hearing in the US Congress on November 18. The allegations come from media reports; we did not have a statement from NVIDIA on them.", "_src": "12d2733c"}, "2026-11-09-dark-heresy-release": {"titel": "Owlcat's Warhammer 40,000: Dark Heresy launches on January 28, 2027 for PC, PS5 and Xbox Series", "schlagzeile": "Warhammer 40k: Dark Heresy has a date – launching January 28, 2027", "kurz": "Owlcat Games has announced the release date for Warhammer 40,000: Dark Heresy. The tactical RPG launches on 28.01.2027 for PC, PS5 and Xbox Series X/S, with a Switch 2 version to follow later. You play an Inquisitor hunting heretics.", "zusammenfassung": "Owlcat Games has announced the release date of its tactical RPG Warhammer 40,000: Dark Heresy with a press release and trailer, Eurogamer and GameStar report. The game launches on January 28, 2027 for PC, PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X/S. A date for Switch 2 is to follow \"at a later date\". Dark Heresy builds on Warhammer 40,000: Rogue Trader, which Owlcat released a few years ago. This time you play an Inquisitor who tracks down heretics and dark influences in the 41st millennium. According to Eurogamer, Owlcat has overhauled many of the underlying systems. A beta containing the complete first act has been running for some time and is playable by buyers of the Founders Edition. This beta will be switched off on January 7 while Owlcat prepares the game for launch. Eurogamer recalls that Rogue Trader was praised for its setting and combat but struggled with bugs and weak performance at launch. How well Dark Heresy runs at release therefore remains to be seen. Owlcat is also working on an RPG based on the science fiction series The Expanse.", "weitere_links": ["GameStar"], "_src": "e9845177"}, "2026-11-09-ps-portal-speicher-japan": {"titel": "Sony launches a new PlayStation Portal model in Japan with internal storage for future features", "schlagzeile": "New PS Portal with its own storage – Sony hints at more features", "kurz": "Sony is releasing a new model of the PlayStation Portal with internal storage in Japan on 10.12.2026. According to Sony Japan, the storage is intended for future features, with details to follow later. The price stays at 39,980 yen, pre-orders start on 13.11.2026, and whether the model will also come to Europe is unclear.", "zusammenfassung": "Sony is releasing a revised model of the PlayStation Portal in Japan, IGN reports, citing Sony Japan's official blog. The most important difference from the previous device is internal storage. Sony writes that it added the storage with future features in mind and will share details once they are finalized. Sony has not yet said what those features will be. At the same time, Sony is changing the official Japanese name from \"PlayStation Portal Remote Player\" to \"PlayStation Portal Player\". In the blog, Sony also stresses that even players without a PS5 can play PS5 games on the Portal; this refers to the cloud streaming for PS Plus Premium members that Sony introduced last year. IGN sees the storage and the name change as a possible step away from a pure Remote Play accessory towards a more standalone handheld; that is an assessment, not an announcement from Sony. The new model launches in Japan on December 10, pre-orders begin on November 13, and the price remains the same at 39,980 yen. It is set to Japanese only and requires a Japanese PSN account. Whether and when it will come to other regions is not known.", "_src": "e6a33542"}, "2026-11-09-sshole-angriffe": {"titel": "OpenSSH flaw \"SSHole\" (CVE-2026-123158) is being actively exploited, attackers gain root on Alpine systems", "schlagzeile": "OpenSSH flaw \"SSHole\" now actively exploited – update Alpine servers", "kurz": "The OpenSSH flaw on musl systems such as Alpine Linux that we reported on 05.11.2026 is now being actively exploited. Several security firms report attacks, and in one honeypot attackers gained root access. The flaw is now called \"SSHole\" (CVE-2026-123158); the fix is OpenSSH 10.6p2 followed by a restart of sshd.", "zusammenfassung": "The OpenSSH flaw we reported on November 5 is now being actively attacked, BleepingComputer, SecurityWeek and The Hacker News report. It now carries the nickname \"SSHole\" and the identifier CVE-2026-123158 (CVSS 8.1). Affected is OpenSSH before version 10.6p2 on Linux systems using the musl C library without PAM, such as the default configuration of Alpine Linux; the discoverer also names OpenWrt, Buildroot, Yocto and many Docker images as worth checking. With a very long password of 257 to 1,024 bytes, attackers can log in to accounts that are not supposed to accept a password at all. According to BleepingComputer, exploitation attempts began on November 5, when a proof of concept appeared a few hours after the fix. The firm Previdian confirms successful root access on its own honeypot running real Alpine Linux and counted 20 attempts from 13 IP addresses in nine countries by November 8. GreyNoise recorded the first successful exploitation in the wild on November 7 and observed 16 successful attack chains: the attackers explored the system and containers, queried cloud metadata, tried to read password hashes and root SSH keys, and attempted to add their own keys for persistent access. The fix is OpenSSH 10.6p2 or the distribution's patched package; Alpine has released packages for all branches from 3.16 onwards. Important: sshd must be restarted after the update, otherwise the old version keeps running; according to watchTowr, mainly botnets and crypto miners are using the flaw so far. As an immediate measure, PasswordAuthentication no helps. Admins should also check logs for unexpected \"Accepted password for\" entries on accounts without a password and for unknown SSH keys.", "weitere_links": ["SecurityWeek", "The Hacker News", "Help Net Security"], "_src": "36ee778e"}, "2026-11-09-gta6-festival-miami": {"titel": "Rockstar announces \"Grand Theft Auto VI: The Festival\" on November 21 in Miami with Travis Scott, Cardi B and Justice", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 gets its own music festival – with Travis Scott and Cardi B", "kurz": "Rockstar is celebrating the launch of GTA 6 with a music festival in Miami. \"Grand Theft Auto VI: The Festival\" takes place on 21.11.2026 at Mana Wynwood, featuring Travis Scott, Cardi B, Kodak Black and Justice, among others. Tickets are awarded by lottery, and the game itself comes out on 19.11.2026.", "zusammenfassung": "Rockstar Games has announced a music festival on X to mark the launch of GTA 6, VGC and Eurogamer report. \"Grand Theft Auto VI: The Festival\" takes place on November 21 at Mana Wynwood in Miami, two days after the game's release on November 19. According to Rockstar, artists from the game and the official soundtrack will perform. Confirmed acts, according to VGC, include Travis Scott, Don Toliver, Kodak Black, Sofaygo, Cardi B, Ca7riel and Paco Amoroso, Justice, Metro Boomin, Rauw & Friends, Suero and Tainy, plus several back-to-back DJ sets. Tickets are handled by the provider DICE and are distributed via a lottery. According to Rockstar, you have to sign up for the pre-sale lottery by Tuesday, November 10, 4 p.m. Eastern Time (10 p.m. in Austria); the chance at tickets then comes on Wednesday at 12 p.m. Eastern Time (6 p.m. our time). Two soundtracks for the game will be released on CD, vinyl and streaming services: \"GTA 6: The Album\" with 34 new songs on November 19, including Travis Scott and Keith Richards, and on December 11 \"Grand Theft Auto VI: Original Score\" with 30 pieces by the French electronic duo Justice.", "weitere_links": ["Rockstar Games on X", "Rockstar Games on X (ticket lottery)", "Eurogamer"], "_src": "31cad77d"}, "2026-11-09-amd-ssd-fix-26-11-1": {"titel": "AMD confirms constant SSD writes caused by Radeon driver, fix expected with Adrenalin 26.11.1", "schlagzeile": "Radeon driver eats SSD lifespan: fix expected with 26.11.1", "kurz": "Follow-up to our report from 08.11.2026: according to TechPowerUp and PC Gamer, the bug in which a Radeon driver service constantly writes to the SSD is to be fixed with Adrenalin 26.11.1. According to TechPowerUp, versions 26.10.1 and 26.10.2 are affected, and there is no date for the new driver yet. Users report losing about 1 percent of SSD health per month.", "zusammenfassung": "There is a fix in sight for the Radeon driver bug with constant SSD writes that we reported on November 8. According to TechPowerUp, AMD has confirmed that the Adrenalin 26.10.1 and 26.10.2 drivers are affected and that the fix is to come with version 26.11.1. PC Gamer quotes AMD representative AMD_Vik on Reddit as saying the problem \"should be fixed\" in 26.11.1; there is no exact date, but according to PC Gamer the driver is expected later this month. The culprit is the atieclxx.exe service from AMD's External Events Utility, which handles things like detecting monitors and Radeon software hotkeys and apparently writes data in an endless loop. Reported rates range from 0.3 to 1.5 MB/s, and one Reddit user cites a sustained 5 MB/s. A user on X measured 19.5 GB of writes in 12 hours and believes the bug has existed since Adrenalin 26.7.1 from June. On Reddit, users report that their SSD health drops by about 1 percent per month as a result; these are user reports, not measurements by AMD. Not every system is affected, and PC Gamer could not reproduce the bug itself. As a workaround, TechPowerUp mentions disabling the AMD External Events Utility, which can cause display issues, or disabling Resizable BAR, which can cost performance. TechPowerUp rather advises waiting for the official driver.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "ComputerBase"], "_src": "fc743806"}, "2026-11-09-amdlss5-2-radeon": {"titel": "Mod AMDLSS5 2.0 brings DLSS 5-style neural rendering to Radeon cards with its own engine", "schlagzeile": "Mod brings DLSS 5 neural rendering to Radeon – now much faster", "kurz": "The unofficial mod AMDLSS5 has been released in version 2.0 and aims to bring DLSS 5-style neural rendering to Radeon cards. According to the developer, it now runs on its own engine and is significantly faster than other mods. The measurements come only from the developer. The mod has nothing to do with AMD or NVIDIA.", "zusammenfassung": "Wccftech reports on version 2.0 of the community mod AMDLSS5 by developer Wehaveall. It aims to bring DLSS 5-style neural rendering, meaning AI enhancements to lighting and materials, to AMD Radeon cards by hooking into existing DirectX 12 upscaling pipelines. New is a dedicated engine that replaces the previous reliance on another mod and is said to have less overhead. In a Reddit post, the developer shares PresentMon figures from Resident Evil Requiem at 4K with FSR on an RX 9070 XT: 101.2 fps on average and 78.5 fps in the 1% lows, compared with 91.3 and 66.0 with version 1.6.1 and 61.6 and 55.5 with other mods. That is where the advertised 64 percent more fps comes from, but only compared with other mods, not with the unmodded game or NVIDIA's actual DLSS 5. These are the developer's figures from a single scene with one card; there are no independent tests yet. Newly supported are PRAGMATA, Nioh 3 and GTA V Enhanced, the latter only in offline Story Mode with BattlEye disabled. The main targets are the RX 9070 and RX 9070 XT; the RX 9060 series should theoretically work, and RX 7000 cards have experimental alpha support, but according to Wccftech the developer has not validated either on real hardware. There are also 39 color presets, local tone mapping, improved ambient occlusion and indirect lighting, and revised 2x frame generation in selected games. The mod is free on GitHub, but the source code of the new engine has not been published yet.", "_src": "23e75a0d"}, "2026-11-09-amazon-us-amd-vor-nvidia": {"titel": "Amazon US in October: AMD sells more graphics cards than NVIDIA, RX 9070 XT is the best seller", "schlagzeile": "Amazon US: AMD sold more graphics cards than NVIDIA in October", "kurz": "According to Amazon US sales figures for October 2026, AMD sold slightly more graphics cards than NVIDIA: around 9,200 versus 8,900 units. The best-selling card was the Radeon RX 9070 XT with about 3,300 units. NVIDIA still made more revenue thanks to higher average prices. The figures come from a data collector, not from the manufacturers.", "zusammenfassung": "Wccftech reports on Amazon US sales figures for October 2026 compiled by the data collector TechEpiphany. According to them, AMD narrowly sold the most graphics cards there in October: around 9,200 units compared with about 8,900 for NVIDIA. Wccftech calls this notable because Amazon US is usually dominated by NVIDIA, while AMD more often leads in places like Germany. NVIDIA stays ahead in revenue, as its average selling price was $1,313 compared with $915 for AMD. The best seller was the Radeon RX 9070 XT with about 3,300 units; the RTX 5070 Ti managed only around a third of that. Second place went to the RTX 5060 Ti (8 and 16 GB combined) with about 2,250 units, followed by the RX 9060 XT with around 2,150. The RTX 5070 stayed below 2,000 units, and the RTX 5090 reached only about 150 due to poor availability. Even the old Arc A380 sold more often, with around 500 units. According to the data, Intel reached about 6.22 percent share, driven by the Arc B570, B580 and Arc Pro cards. Wccftech sees the sharply increased prices as the main reason buyers are turning to cheaper cards. Important: the figures cover only one shop in the US and do not come from AMD, NVIDIA or Amazon themselves; they are therefore only a snapshot, not market shares for the overall market.", "_src": "1307b37c"}, "2026-11-09-bit-reactor-entlassungen": {"titel": "Star Wars Zero Company: developer Bit Reactor lays off staff despite good reviews and a million sales", "schlagzeile": "Star Wars Zero Company: studio lays off staff – despite hit and 84 Metascore", "kurz": "Bit Reactor, the studio behind Star Wars Zero Company, has laid off staff. VGC reports this based on LinkedIn posts by affected developers. Yet the game was well reviewed and, according to EA, has sold one million copies. How many jobs are affected is unclear.", "zusammenfassung": "Bit Reactor, the developer of Star Wars Zero Company, has laid off staff, VGC reports, citing the site Bespin Bulletin. Several developers, including a senior environment artist, a UI engineer, a producer and a senior QA analyst, wrote on LinkedIn in recent days that they were affected. How many positions are being cut in total is not known. According to reports, the studio had furloughed around 80 percent of its staff without pay before the release in August because money was running short. In October, studio head Greg Foertsch said that some of the furloughed staff were returning; according to reports, this brought the studio back to more than half its former size. It is unclear whether returnees are now affected as well or only people who were not brought back after the furlough. At least one affected developer writes that he was laid off after three months of furlough. That is bitter because Star Wars Zero Company launched at the end of August to very good reviews and stands at 84 points on Metacritic. On October 9, the official EA Star Wars account reported one million units sold. VGC does not cite an official statement from Bit Reactor on the layoffs.", "weitere_links": ["GameStar"], "_src": "52d9b77e"}, "2026-11-09-notepadpp-7zip-luecken": {"titel": "Notepad++ 8.9.9 fixes six security flaws, 7-Zip 26.06 fixes unspecified vulnerabilities", "schlagzeile": "Notepad++ and 7-Zip: updates plug security holes – update them yourself", "kurz": "Notepad++ 8.9.9 fixes six security flaws, the most serious rated high. 7-Zip 26.06 also fixes vulnerabilities according to its developer, but gives no details. 7-Zip has no update function, so you have to update it yourself. On Windows, winget makes that easy.", "zusammenfassung": "Two widely used Windows tools have received security updates, heise online reports. Notepad++ 8.9.9 by developer Don Ho fixes six security flaws. The most serious is a heap buffer overflow in the SAML decoder of the mimeTools plugin: crafted SAML messages could overwrite memory when decoded and possibly execute malicious code. The advisory rates the risk as high but gives no CVSS score. The other five flaws are considered medium, and according to heise some of them can probably be used to escalate privileges on the system, for example via UAC saving of protected files or window messages. There are no CVE numbers yet. In addition, the version speeds up searching in files and updates the editor component Scintilla to 5.6.9. Notepad++ has its own update check; alternatively, winget update Notepad++.Notepad++ helps. The archiving tool 7-Zip was released in version 26.06 over the weekend. Developer Igor Pavlov only writes that some bugs and vulnerabilities were fixed, without saying which ones or how severe they are. He also improved support for files split with the Linux tool split. Because 7-Zip has no update check, users have to download the new version themselves or use winget upgrade 7zip.7zip on Windows. heise recommends installing all available updates at once with winget upgrade --all.", "weitere_links": ["heise online (7-Zip)"], "_src": "2abed807"}, "2026-11-09-sonicwall-sslvpn-angriffe": {"titel": "SonicWall: SSLVPN flaw under attack, firmware updates fix seven vulnerabilities", "schlagzeile": "SonicWall firewalls: VPN flaw under attack – update now", "kurz": "Attackers appear to be exploiting a flaw in the SSLVPN of SonicWall firewalls that allows SAML sign-in, and with it multi-factor authentication, to be bypassed. SonicWall and the US agency CISA advise updating quickly. The SSLVPN is only vulnerable if SAML is enabled for VPN sign-in. The new firmware fixes seven flaws in total.", "zusammenfassung": "SonicWall published a security advisory on Friday covering seven vulnerabilities in SonicOS, as heise online reports. For one of them, the manufacturer assumes it may already have been used in attacks; the US security agency CISA is also warning. It is CVE-2026-19868 (CVSS 7.1, high): anyone with valid credentials for an alternative sign-in method can use it to bypass SAML authentication, which is used for single sign-on, for example. This apparently also allows the multi-factor authentication enforced via SAML to be circumvented. According to SonicWall, the SSLVPN is only vulnerable if SAML is enabled for SSLVPN logins. The fix is SonicOS 7.3.4-7013 for Gen7 firewalls and 8.2.3-8015 for Gen8 devices, as well as newer versions. The updates close six further flaws, including two with CVSS 8.8 relating to cross-domain policy and session validation, and a heap buffer overflow in the SSL-VPN that can be triggered without authentication (CVSS 7.5). There are also two buffer overflows in TACACS+ and weak password hashing on virtual appliances, all rated medium risk. heise recalls that SonicWall had already reported a critical, maximum-score flaw in SMA1000 appliances in early October. Companies and admins are mainly affected; anyone who manages a SonicWall firewall at home or in the office should update the firmware now.", "_src": "6679ffee"}, "2026-11-08-windows11-app-updates": {"titel": "Windows 11 tests a central page for third-party app updates", "schlagzeile": "End of update pop-ups? Windows 11 tests central app updates", "kurz": "A new 'App updates' page has appeared in the Settings of a Windows 11 26H2 preview build. It is meant to collect updates for third-party programs such as browsers or media players in one place, instead of each app showing its own notices. This will only work if developers register their apps. In Windows Latest's test, not a single provider was registered yet.", "zusammenfassung": "Windows Latest discovered a page called 'App updates' under Settings > Apps in a Windows 11 26H2 preview build. The page was briefly visible in December 2025 and has now reappeared, which according to Windows Latest points to an imminent rollout. The goal is to bundle updates for programs outside the Microsoft Store in one place, instead of each app showing its own pop-ups, like the infamous Java updater used to. The basis is the 'Windows Update Orchestration Platform', which Microsoft presented in 2025. Developers can register their apps there as providers while keeping their own update servers and installers; Windows only handles coordination. MSIX and APPX packages as well as classic Win32 programs are to be supported. To register, developers must supply a script or program that checks for updates; by default, Windows runs this check every 22 hours. Windows is to schedule installation similarly to system updates, taking usage, battery and network into account so you are not interrupted in the middle of work. On Windows Latest's test machine, however, the page reported that no app provider was registered, not even Microsoft itself for Teams or Outlook, and the button to check for updates was greyed out. So this is a feature in testing that cannot be used yet. Whether it really helps depends on how many developers take part; Microsoft does not want to force anyone. Microsoft has not announced a launch date.", "_src": "06466579"}, "2026-11-08-nvidia-board-untersuchung-huang": {"titel": "NVIDIA board launches independent investigation into CEO Jensen Huang", "schlagzeile": "NVIDIA board opens investigation – Huang admits affair", "kurz": "NVIDIA's board has launched an independent investigation after media reported that CEO Jensen Huang had been the target of a foreign intelligence service. In a message to employees published by NVIDIA, Huang admitted he had been unfaithful to his wife. According to the board, there is so far no reason to believe national security or company secrets were compromised. Huang remains CEO.", "zusammenfassung": "NVIDIA published two statements on the evening of 8 November 2026. In the first, the board announces an independent investigation: a committee of independent directors, assisted by outside counsel, will examine whether founder and CEO Jensen Huang was the target of a foreign intelligence effort. The board writes that it has no reason to believe national security or NVIDIA secrets were compromised, but that it will examine all available information. Huang supports the review and will cooperate; the board expresses confidence in him and his leadership team. In the second statement, a message to employees first published by Axios, Huang apologizes to his family and staff and admits he was unfaithful to his wife. The background is reporting by the Financial Times and the New York Times in the preceding days. According to those reports, a memo based on US intelligence attributes a relationship to Huang with a woman named Alice Huang, a former executive at NVIDIA customer Megaspeed; according to the reports, US agencies believed she was an informant for China's Ministry of State Security. Despite the shared surname, the two are not related, according to the reports. Neither the memo nor its basis is public, and neither Huang nor the board addresses the espionage allegations in substance; according to Axios, Huang's message does not name Alice Huang. The board's statement therefore does not confirm the allegations. According to the NYT, the aim was to learn more about US AI chips. NVIDIA spokesperson John Rizzo said, according to ComputerBase, that the events would not slow the company's work. When results of the investigation will be available is unclear; the board says it will provide further updates as appropriate.", "weitere_links": ["heise online", "IGN"], "_src": "ae83deda"}, "2026-11-08-layden-ps5-300": {"titel": "Former PlayStation boss Shawn Layden: Sony needs a $300 PS5 rather than a $1,200 PS6", "schlagzeile": "Ex-PlayStation boss: No $1,200 PS6 – rather a $300 PS5", "kurz": "Former PlayStation boss Shawn Layden advises Sony to build a much cheaper PS5 instead of an expensive PS6. 'The innovation needs to come not from making PS6 for $1,200. It's to make another PS5 for $300,' he said on The Trophy Room podcast. The PS5 is the first platform that has become more expensive over time, he said. This says nothing about official PS6 plans.", "zusammenfassung": "Shawn Layden, former president and CEO of Sony Interactive Entertainment America, commented on the next PlayStation on The Trophy Room podcast, as IGN reports. In his view, a PS6 that mainly relies on more ray tracing and more teraflops does not offer enough real innovation. 'I think we have enough power in the machine,' Layden said. In his view, true innovation would not be a PS6 for 1,200 dollars, but another PS5 for 300 dollars. He pointed out that the PS2 was available for 99 dollars at the end of its life, while the PS5 is the first platform he has seen go up in price over time. Sony should make the console smaller and cheaper; the chip and operating system are good enough for the games people want to play. IGN adds context: at launch six years ago, the PS5 cost 499 dollars in the US and the Digital Edition 399 dollars. Directly from PlayStation, the standard version now costs 649, the Digital Edition 599 and the PS5 Pro 899 dollars. Sony attributes the increases to the difficult economic environment. There is little official information about the PS6: Sony said in May that it was still deciding on the timing, and a February report mentioned a possible delay to 2028 or 2029. Layden has not been at Sony for years; his statements are a personal opinion and not information about Sony's plans. No concrete PS6 price is known; the 1,200 dollars is Layden's pointed example.", "_src": "5da916e2"}, "2026-11-08-amd-radeon-ssd-writes": {"titel": "AMD confirms a Radeon driver bug that keeps writing to the SSD", "schlagzeile": "Radeon driver keeps writing to the SSD while idle", "kurz": "Some AMD Radeon users report that the graphics driver keeps writing to the system SSD even when the PC is otherwise idle. The process blamed is atieclxx, the AMD External Events Client Module. According to Wccftech and Neowin, AMD has acknowledged the issue and is working on a fix; it is not listed in the notes for Adrenalin 26.10.2 of 30.10.2026. Not every system appears to be affected, and how much this actually shortens an SSD's lifespan has not been established.", "zusammenfassung": "On 8.11.2026 Wccftech and Neowin reported a bug in AMD's Radeon graphics drivers that can cause constant writes to the system drive even when the computer is otherwise idle. The trigger is said to be the atieclxx process, the AMD External Events Client Module, which belongs to AMD External Events Utility and among other things handles monitor changes, hotkeys and FreeSync. User reports often sit between about 0.3 and 1.5 megabytes per second, while individual reports mention around 5 megabytes per second. Extrapolated, uninterrupted writes at 5 MB/s would theoretically mean about 432 gigabytes of host writes a day; Wccftech stresses that this is an upper bound under continuous load and does not automatically equal the amount actually written to NAND. Whether and how much the bug shortens an SSD's lifespan has not been established, according to the reports. The problem is said to be not entirely new and to appear on Windows 10 and Windows 11 across various Radeon cards and Adrenalin versions; some PCs on the current 26.10.2 driver show no unusual load, according to users. An AMD staffer named AMD_Matt is said to have confirmed the behaviour in October as a genuine issue under investigation. Another representative, AMD_Vik, later indicated that a fix had likely already been submitted but may have missed the cutoff for the next driver release. Adrenalin Edition 26.10.2, released on 30.10.2026, does not mention the bug in its official release notes. Neowin adds that AMD pointed to an interaction with Microsoft's PCIe filter driver and Resizable BAR. As workarounds, both outlets name temporarily stopping the AMD External Events Utility service through Windows' service manager or disabling Resizable BAR; either step can affect FreeSync, Adrenalin hotkeys or gaming performance. Some users nevertheless report that FreeSync and ReBAR kept working after the service was stopped. Anyone who wants to check whether their PC is affected should look in Resource Monitor on the Disk tab for sustained write activity from atieclxx. A driver update containing the fix is not yet available, according to the reports.", "weitere_links": ["Neowin"], "_src": "f2340f0a"}, "2026-11-08-gpu-preise-plus40": {"titel": "Graphics card prices: almost 40 percent higher on average since August", "schlagzeile": "Graphics cards have risen almost 40 percent since August", "kurz": "GameStar compared current graphics card street prices: since August 2026, the models it tracked have become almost 40 percent more expensive on average. Between January and August the change, excluding the RTX 5090, was still only around three percent. According to the analysis, the RTX 5090 itself rose from about 3,000 euros in January through 4,350 euros in August to around 7,500 euros now.", "zusammenfassung": "On 8.11.2026 GameStar published a new look at current street prices for graphics cards. In August the same review of 16 models from AMD, NVIDIA and Intel, excluding the RTX 5090, had still shown an average change of about three percent compared with January 2026. Since then the trend for virtually all of the cards covered has pointed only upward. The report deliberately leaves the RTX 5090 out of the average because, as a flagship with 32 gigabytes of memory, it occupies a special position. Its price is said to have risen from around 3,000 euros in January through 4,350 euros in August to about 7,500 euros now. Below that, down to the RTX 5050, the picture also looks grim: if the direction holds, the RTX 5080 will soon sit above 2,000 euros, and almost 400 euros would be due for the entry-level RTX 5050. Across the models tracked, GameStar arrives at an average increase of almost 40 percent since August. The text names the ongoing AI boom as the cause. Hardware companies such as AMD are also said to state clearly that they see themselves primarily as data-center firms rather than gaming companies. Every forecast of the memory and hardware crunch known to the author assumes the situation will last for years and get worse rather than better. Precise price predictions are difficult; the author nonetheless expects prices to keep rising and availability to get worse. The percentage figures come from GameStar's own price analysis; aside from the 5090, 5080 and 5050, the text does not list individual model prices in a table.", "_src": "cf2fd89d"}, "2026-11-08-12v2x6-kabel-rtx-pro-6000": {"titel": "Damaged 12V-2×6 cables found on two RTX PRO 6000 cards despite a premium power supply", "schlagzeile": "$32,000 PC: 12V-2×6 cables crumble on two RTX PRO 6000 cards", "kurz": "A Reddit user with two NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell cards found damaged sleeving on both 12V-2×6 power cables, even though the cards were limited to 500 watts. The damage appeared on both the GPU and PSU side, but nothing melted. The power supply is a Seasonic PRIME TX-1600 Noctua Edition. The cause has not been measured; this is a single case.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz reports on a Reddit post by user Doomslayer606, who runs two NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell cards in the 600-watt Workstation Edition with 96 GB of GDDR7 each in his workstation. According to VideoCardz, the cards together cost over 32,000 dollars. They are powered by a Seasonic PRIME TX-1600 Noctua Edition with two native 16-pin cables. Although the owner had limited both cards to 500 watts, he noticed on both cables that the sleeving of two individual wires was stiff, cracked and easy to peel off. The damage appeared both at the graphics card connectors and on the power supply side, where it was even worse, although those connectors were rarely touched. The actual wire insulation remained intact, and there were no visible signs of melting or discoloration on the cards or the power supply. Before that, the user had noticed that a GPU or an NVMe SSD occasionally disappeared from the PCIe bus, which is why he had reseated the cables several times. He suspects localized overheating caused by unevenly distributed current, but temperature and current were not measured. As a consequence, he has bought replacement cables with thermal protection and is considering limiting the cards to 450 watts; at 300 watts he lost 40 to 50 percent of performance in his workloads. According to the report, Seasonic and NVIDIA have not commented. It is a single case without manufacturer confirmation, but it fits the long series of problems surrounding the 16-pin connector. VideoCardz advises checking power connectors regularly without constantly unplugging and replugging them.", "_src": "a3d9d41a"}, "2026-11-08-rtings-woled-edge-rot": {"titel": "RTINGS long-term test: 14 of 16 older WOLED TVs show pixel failures along the edges", "schlagzeile": "'Edge rot': 14 of 16 WOLED TVs develop dead pixels at the edges", "kurz": "In RTINGS' 18,000-hour longevity test, 14 of 16 TVs with LG Display WOLED panels developed dead pixels along the screen edges. RTINGS calls this 'edge rot'; it has nothing to do with burn-in. The three QD-OLED TVs tested were not affected. Mostly 2020 to 2022 models are affected; newer panels from 2024 onward have not been tested.", "zusammenfassung": "The testing site RTINGS has published results from its accelerated longevity test, in which TVs ran for around 18,000 hours. Of 16 sets with LG Display WOLED panels, 14 developed dead pixels, small pixel clusters or visible damage along the screen edges, which is 87.5 percent. RTINGS calls the phenomenon 'edge rot'. Unlike burn-in, according to RTINGS it does not depend on whether static content is shown, and it cannot be avoided by watching varied content. Among the older WBC panels, 9 of 10 sets were affected, five of them severely; among the newer WBE panels, 5 of 6, including models from LG and Sony. The 2023 LG G3 showed no edge damage. The three QD-OLED TVs with Samsung Display panels had no edge rot; however, RTINGS stresses that three units are too few to declare QD-OLED immune. Three OLED monitors that were checked, including one WOLED model, also showed no edge damage. Two RTINGS employees also found the problem on their privately used sets from 2020 and 2021. The exact cause is unclear; possible explanations include contamination during manufacturing and weaknesses in the protective layer meant to keep moisture away from the panel. LG Electronics and LG Display confirmed to RTINGS that the phenomenon can occur in a small number of products exposed to prolonged heat, humidity or other harsh conditions, but is not expected under normal conditions. The 87.5 percent is a result from a small test pool under continuous load, not a failure rate for all sets sold. Whether panels from 2024 onward are affected has not yet been determined by RTINGS.", "weitere_links": ["Hardware Busters"], "_src": "d6fa466e"}, "2026-11-07-warzone-switch2": {"titel": "Call of Duty: Warzone is now free on Nintendo Switch 2", "schlagzeile": "Warzone is now free to play on Nintendo Switch 2", "kurz": "Call of Duty: Warzone has arrived on Nintendo Switch 2 and is available for free on the Nintendo eShop. You do not need to buy Modern Warfare 4, but you do need an Activision account. The launch coincided with Season 1; at the same time, support for PlayStation 4 and Xbox One ended.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Insider Gaming, Call of Duty: Warzone is available on Nintendo Switch 2 and can be downloaded from the eShop as a standalone free-to-play title. Anyone who does not own Modern Warfare 4 can still play the battle royale. An Activision account is required. The launch came together with Season 1; Activision says players can drop into Hajin, Zodiac and the other maps and playlists as the free-to-play game arrives on Nintendo’s handheld for the first time. Nintendo Life followed up on 7.11.2026 and measured a file size of 122 GB on its own device; we do not have an official download size from Activision. Insider Gaming frames the move as the series returning to Nintendo hardware: Modern Warfare 4 was, by that account, the first Call of Duty game on a Nintendo console since Ghosts on the Wii U. With Season 1, Activision ended support for PlayStation 4 and Xbox One; progress is said to carry over to supported platforms via the same linked Activision account. Resolution, frame rate and cross-play details for the Switch 2 version have not been specified in the reporting available to us. The launch itself was on 6.11.2026; the Insider Gaming report we used appeared on 7.11.2026.", "weitere_links": ["Nintendo Life (122 GB measurement)"], "_src": "88111250"}, "2026-11-07-pulse-elevate-verschoben": {"titel": "Sony indefinitely delays Pulse Elevate speakers over a production issue", "schlagzeile": "Sony delays Pulse Elevate indefinitely – just before launch", "kurz": "Sony has indefinitely delayed the sales launch of the wireless Pulse Elevate speakers. The 12 November date is off because quality testing found a production issue. Sony has not named a new date; what happens to existing pre-orders is unclear.", "zusammenfassung": "On 6.11.2026 Sony indefinitely delayed the launch of the Pulse Elevate speakers on the PlayStation Blog. Eurogamer and IGN picked up the statement on 7.11.2026. In the blog, Sony writes that ongoing quality testing identified a production issue with the product and that it therefore decided to delay the launch; the extra time is meant to ensure the product delivers the intended experience. Sony does not name a new date or describe the issue in detail. The speakers were due to go on sale worldwide on 12 November, only a few days after the statement. The recommended retail price on the updated blog page is 219.99 US dollars, 219.99 euros and 199.99 pounds. Pulse Elevate is Sony’s first wireless speaker pair for desktop gaming and sits alongside the Pulse Elite headset and Pulse Explore earbuds. They connect via PlayStation Link to the PS5, PCs, Macs and PlayStation Portal and can be paired with a phone over Bluetooth at the same time. The right speaker has a microphone with what Sony calls AI-enhanced noise rejection. The Midnight Black version was due to be available everywhere, the white version only in selected countries including Germany, Austria and the United Kingdom. Pre-orders had been open since September. Eurogamer writes that it is unclear what now happens to those orders.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation Blog (official statement)", "IGN"], "_src": "67242cb4"}, "2026-11-07-anno117-fsr3-rtx30": {"titel": "Anno 117 Update 3.0: FSR 3 Frame Generation now enabled by default on GeForce RTX 30", "schlagzeile": "Anno 117 now turns on AMD's Frame Generation on RTX 30 cards", "kurz": "With Update 3.0, Anno 117: Pax Romana enables AMD's FSR 3 Frame Generation by default on GeForce RTX 30 cards in the automatic graphics settings. Reason: NVIDIA's own DLSS Frame Generation only runs on RTX 40 and newer. More displayed fps do not mean lower input latency, though.", "zusammenfassung": "Ubisoft Mainz released Update 3.0 for Anno 117: Pax Romana on 5 November 2026 together with the expansion \"Dawn of the Delta\". According to the official patch notes, the automatic graphics detection now enables AMD's FSR 3 Frame Generation by default on GeForce cards of the RTX 30 series. PCGH picked this up on 7 November and explains the background: NVIDIA's DLSS Frame Generation is officially reserved for the RTX 40 and RTX 50 series, whereas FSR 3 works across vendors and does not need AI units. On systems that the game assigns the \"Low\" profile, however, Frame Generation is no longer enabled automatically, to avoid fluctuations on PCs close to the minimum requirements. Ubisoft does not give concrete figures for the fps gain. Frame Generation inserts intermediate frames: the displayed frame rate rises, but input latency does not decrease as a result. Further changes address stutters when panning over large cities, performance drops when highlighting roads, and the quest book archive. According to the patch notes, the update also fixes numerous crashes and bugs. Anyone who does not use the automatic setting or does not want Frame Generation can control it in the graphics options.", "weitere_links": ["Anno Union: Update 3.0 patch notes"], "_src": "e94737ea"}, "2026-11-07-assassins-creed-mars-rom": {"titel": "Report: Ubisoft working on Assassin's Creed \"Mars\" in ancient Rome and mobile spin-off \"Pocket\"", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Assassin's Creed heading back to Rome?", "kurz": "According to content creator J0nathan, Ubisoft is developing an Assassin's Creed codenamed \"Mars\" that is said to be set in ancient Rome, plus a mobile title \"Pocket\" set in Jerusalem. Insider Gaming knows the codenames but could not sufficiently verify the claims. According to the report, a release would only be conceivable around 2029/2030.", "zusammenfassung": "On 7 November 2026, Insider Gaming reported on claims by YouTuber J0nathan, who has often had accurate information about Assassin's Creed in the past. According to him, Ubisoft is working on an Assassin's Creed codenamed \"Mars\" that is said to be set in ancient Rome. Two sources with access to Ubisoft's internal systems are said to have confirmed this; a link to the planned Assassin's Creed TV series is considered possible. A second project codenamed \"Pocket\" is said to be a mobile game set in Jerusalem. Insider Gaming says it has also heard of the codenames but could not verify the details to its standards. The series has recently been in troubled waters, among other things after the departure of Marc-Alexis Côté. According to earlier Insider Gaming sources, the next big game, Assassin's Creed Hexe, was internally delayed by another year, probably to 2028. A Rome game would therefore not be expected before 2029/2030, according to the report. Ubisoft has not commented. Everything is unconfirmed; early projects can change or be cancelled.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: the origin is YouTuber J0nathan, who has a mixed but often accurate track record on Assassin's Creed. Insider Gaming knows the codenames but could not verify the details. No statement from Ubisoft.", "weitere_links": ["TheGamer: Codename Mars"], "_src": "ef82e5b6"}, "2026-11-07-microsoft-gpu-patent-ki": {"titel": "Microsoft patent application: spare GPU power of private devices for AI training in exchange for credits", "schlagzeile": "Money for your idle GPU? Microsoft patent describes AI training", "kurz": "A Microsoft patent application published on 5 November describes a system that splits AI training into small subtasks and distributes them to unused GPUs of end devices. Users would have to opt in and could receive credits. Microsoft has not announced a product.", "zusammenfassung": "Insider Gaming reports on a Microsoft patent application titled \"Opportunistic Micro-training on Edge Devices Using Spare GPU Utilization\" (US-20260349820-A1), published on 5 November 2026. It describes a system that splits large AI training tasks into independently trainable mini-tasks and distributes them to devices whose GPU currently has little to do. Whether a device is free is to be determined from GPU and CPU load, memory, temperature and power consumption. According to the text, the system should not disrupt use, i.e. not slow down programs, drain batteries or overheat devices. Only users who agree are to take part. The computing work performed is to be tracked and booked as a credit to the account, redeemable for software, model access or money, for example. Microsoft would act as an intermediary between third parties who need computing power and the device owners. Questions about privacy, permissions and additional wear on the graphics card remain open. Important: a patent application is not a product promise; many patents are never implemented. Microsoft has not announced any such service.", "_src": "1f47cb8a"}, "2026-11-07-hwinfo-rx7500-razor-lake": {"titel": "HWiNFO beta detects unannounced Radeon RX 7500 and Intel Razor Lake-H/HX/S", "schlagzeile": "Leak: HWiNFO knows RX 7500 and Razor Lake", "kurz": "HWiNFO beta 8.55 Build 6115 lists an AMD Radeon RX 7500 that AMD has not announced yet. The same build improves detection of Intel Razor Lake-H, -HX and -S as well as Nova Lake-E. Specs and launch of the RX 7500 remain unknown; name support in tools is not a launch guarantee.", "zusammenfassung": "TechPowerUp and VideoCardz report that HWiNFO beta version 8.55 Build 6115 detects \"AMD Radeon RX 7500\" for the first time. AMD has not officially introduced the card; the changelog only lists the name, without specifications or a date. TechPowerUp considers Navi 33 / RDNA 3 the most likely chip candidate, because that architecture already powers the RX 7400 and RX 7600 – a model in between would be tightly positioned. The name RX 7500 or RX 7500 XT already appeared in older rumors around 2024 according to reports, without a concrete launch. VideoCardz additionally points to earlier prototype hints of Navi 33 XE with 6 GB GDDR6 and device ID 749F; whether the final product looks like that is unconfirmed. The same HWiNFO build expands support for Intel Nova Lake-E and Razor Lake-H/HX/S. Razor Lake is considered a successor generation after Nova Lake; retail chips are far off, since Nova Lake-S is only expected around Q1 2027. CPU-Z 3.02 already added Razor Lake earlier this week; HWiNFO had provisional Razor Lake-AX support already in August. AMD and Intel have not confirmed the entries.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: Only name/ID support in HWiNFO beta 8.55-6115 plus reports from TechPowerUp and VideoCardz. No official announcement from AMD or Intel; specs and launch of the RX 7500 unknown. Tool detection is not a launch guarantee.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz: HWiNFO RX 7500 and Razor Lake", "HWiNFO Forum: Beta 8.55-6115"], "_src": "34935787"}, "2026-11-07-vulkan-1-4-368": {"titel": "Vulkan 1.4.368 with new extensions from Valve and NVIDIA", "schlagzeile": "Vulkan 1.4.368: Valve and NVIDIA bring new extensions", "kurz": "The Khronos Group has released Vulkan 1.4.368. The weekly update brings two new extensions: one from Valve's Mesa developer Mike Blumenkrantz for vertex data and an NVIDIA extension for internal driver handles. Nothing changes for players right away; it is a building block for drivers and engines.", "zusammenfassung": "Vulkan 1.4.368 is the latest weekly update to the specification of the cross-platform graphics and compute interface, as Phoronix reported on 7 November 2026. In terms of content, it is a small update: six internally reported issues in the specification were fixed. There are two new extensions. VK_EXT_vertex_address_binding_unrestricted comes from Mike Blumenkrantz of Valve's Linux graphics team, a well-known Mesa developer. It helps when vertex data for a draw call is moved into a separate buffer to save memory, and disables an address check for that case. The second, VK_NV_internal_handle, is an NVIDIA-specific extension: applications and engines can use it to query internal driver handles for certain Vulkan objects and pass them on to other NVIDIA interfaces. Both extensions first have to arrive in drivers and software before they make a difference in games. Vulkan is, among other things, the foundation of Proton on Linux and the Steam Deck, where Valve's contributions are particularly important. All details are in the Khronos Group's Vulkan-Docs repository on GitHub.", "weitere_links": ["Khronos Vulkan-Docs on GitHub"], "_src": "9f12e9de"}, "2026-11-07-razor-lake-lga1954-2028": {"titel": "Report: Intel Razor Lake-S to arrive in 2028 on Nova Lake's LGA 1954 socket", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Razor Lake could fit the Nova Lake socket in 2028", "kurz": "According to insider Jaykihn, Intel's Razor Lake-S is currently planned for 2028 and is said to use the same LGA 1954 socket as Nova Lake-S. Anyone switching to Nova Lake in 2027 could therefore upgrade one more CPU generation without a new motherboard. Intel has confirmed none of this.", "zusammenfassung": "On 7 November 2026, Wccftech and HotHardware summarized statements by Intel insider Jaykihn: Razor Lake-S is \"currently slated as a 2028 product\", and Intel has said nothing officially. Nova Lake-S, the next desktop generation, is expected in early 2027 and introduces the new LGA 1954 socket. According to the reports, Razor Lake-S is to run on the same socket, which would give Intel two desktop generations on one platform for the first time in a while. Back in June, Jaykihn had written that LGA 1954 will even support processors beyond Razor Lake on boards with 64 MB of BIOS flash, including all Z boards. The reports name Griffin Cove, a successor to Nova Lake's Coyote Cove, as Razor Lake's P-core architecture; the desktop chips are not supposed to have SMT. In addition, some variants originally planned for Nova Lake, such as Nova Lake-AX, are said to have moved into the Razor Lake family. No quarter in 2028 is known; Wccftech speculates about Computex 2028 or the second half of the year. Intel manager Robert Hallock hinted in March that the company is listening to criticism of frequent socket changes, but there is no concrete commitment. First preparations are visible: CPU-Z 3.02 and an HWiNFO beta already recognize Razor Lake. All details on timing and socket are unconfirmed and may change; purchase decisions should not be based on them.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: statements by insider Jaykihn (X), who has often been right about Intel roadmaps; picked up by Wccftech and HotHardware. No confirmation from Intel; timing and socket may change.", "weitere_links": ["HotHardware: Razor Lake-S on LGA 1954", "VideoCardz: LGA 1954 beyond Razor Lake (June)"], "_src": "4d9282a2"}, "2026-11-07-cpuz-ram-rueckgang": {"titel": "CPU-Z statistics: share of 32 and 64 GB PCs falls year over year for the first time", "schlagzeile": "Less RAM for the first time: CPU-Z sees 16 GB PCs on the rise again", "kurz": "According to CPU-Z Validator statistics, the share of PCs with 32 GB of RAM fell by 2.5% year over year, and by as much as 18% for 64 GB. 16 GB and 8 GB systems, on the other hand, are gaining, and DDR4 is gaining share over DDR5. The data only reflects submitted validations, not market figures.", "zusammenfassung": "Doc TB, one of the developers behind CPU-Z, published new figures from the CPU-Z Validator on 6 November 2026, and VideoCardz covered them on 7 November. According to them, the RAM configuration of the recorded PCs has declined year over year for the first time. 32 GB remains the most common configuration at 37.2%, but lost 2.5% of its share. For 64 GB the decline is 18%, with the share now at 7.3%. 16 GB systems grew by 12.9% to 33.0%, putting them just behind 32 GB. 8 GB also grew by 5.5% to 11.0%, and 24 GB by 19.7% to 2.3%. In terms of memory generation, DDR4 rose by 6.0% to 54.5%, while DDR5 fell by 2.9% to 32.9%. The figures do not name a cause, but they fit the sharply increased RAM prices of recent months, which the ticker has reported on several times. Important: the statistics are based only on systems that users actively submit to the validator and are not a market study. The changes are relative shares and do not mean that owners are removing RAM.", "weitere_links": ["Doc TB (CPU-Z) on X, 6 Nov 2026"], "_src": "299d8b24"}, "2026-11-07-custom-engine-wald-rtx3080": {"titel": "Own engine: developer renders dense forest at around 130 fps on an RTX 3080 – without hardware ray tracing", "schlagzeile": "130 fps on an RTX 3080: hobby engine renders forest without ray tracing", "kurz": "Developer and modder Toni Macaroni shows a self-written engine that is said to render a dense forest at 1440p at an average of around 130 fps on an RTX 3080. It relies on Nanite-like geometry, voxels and voxel lighting instead of hardware ray tracing. The figures come from the developer himself, and it is purely a tech demo.", "zusammenfassung": "PCGH and Wccftech report on a tech demo by developer and modder Toni Macaroni, whose YouTube video has more than 500,000 views according to PCGH. By his own account, he has been working on the engine for around eight months after using the open-source engine Godot for a long time. The scene shows a hilly landscape with dense forest, around one million instances and four million triangles. On a GeForce RTX 3080 at 1440p, it is said to reach about 130 fps on average, up to 200 in aerial shots and around 80 fps in dense undergrowth. Technically, the engine uses clustered levels of detail with Nanite-like virtual geometry, voxel representations for distant vegetation and simplified proxies for very distant objects. The lighting combines screen-space techniques with voxel-based global illumination and works without hardware-accelerated ray tracing, similar to the approach in Kingdom Come: Deliverance II. The engine is deliberately specialized: above all, it is meant to render many objects with high polygon counts well, and a weather system is only partially finished. The fps figures are the developer's own claims; the exact settings and any upscaling are not known. A demo without characters, physics and AI is not comparable to a finished game, and there is no public version so far.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech: Custom Forest Engine"], "_src": "9e0e5944"}, "2026-11-07-windows-hello-pin-parallel": {"titel": "Windows 11 Insider: PIN in parallel with Windows Hello face or fingerprint scan", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11: Type PIN while Windows Hello scans", "kurz": "In Windows 11 Insider Experimental Build 26340.9882 you can type the PIN while Windows Hello is still checking face or fingerprint. The lock screen shows \"Look at the camera or enter your PIN\"; whichever works first wins. The rollout is experimental; there is no retail date.", "zusammenfassung": "Windows Latest tests Build 26340.9882 from 6 November 2026 (based on Windows 11 26H2, Experimental channel): On the sign-in screen the PIN field appears in parallel with the Windows Hello check. Instead of waiting for face recognition to fail or awkwardly choosing sign-in options, Microsoft release notes say \"whichever method works first\". After a restart, PIN-first remains for security reasons. If Face fails, there is a direct \"Retry face sign-in\" hint. On devices with an IR camera and fingerprint sensor the prompt can name face and fingerprint, with PIN underneath. New are Event Log IDs 4628 and 4629 under Security for set-up or failed Hello methods; additional Operational events help IT. According to the test the feature appeared without ViVeTool. Experimental builds can contain bugs; Microsoft did not say when the behavior reaches the stable channel.", "_src": "fc64848d"}, "2026-11-07-tsmc-3d-dram-nvidia": {"titel": "TSMC is considering entering 3D DRAM – NVIDIA is said to have prompted the move", "schlagzeile": "TSMC considers 3D DRAM: NVIDIA is said to have prompted the move", "kurz": "According to a report by The Information dated 6.11.2026, contract chipmaker TSMC is considering entering 3D DRAM production. The prompt is said to have come from NVIDIA, TSMC’s largest customer. The report names no specific plants, investments or start date. TSMC declined to comment on market rumors to The Information and pointed to its role as a logic foundry; NVIDIA did not respond, according to the report.", "zusammenfassung": "The Information reported on 6.11.2026, citing two people familiar with the discussions, that TSMC is considering entering 3D DRAM manufacturing. The trigger is said to have been a request from NVIDIA. igor'sLAB picked up and assessed the report on 7.11.2026. According to that account, TSMC has begun working out possible production concepts for vertically structured DRAM; the options named are building new plants or acquiring an existing facility and converting it. No production start, investment figures or planned capacity were given. The initiative is said to be led by Hsu Kuo-chin, a TSMC vice president in Advanced Packaging who previously worked for Micron in Taiwan. TSMC told The Information that it does not comment on market rumors as a matter of principle and pointed to its focus as a logic-chip foundry. NVIDIA did not respond to an inquiry, according to the report, and Reuters could not independently confirm the information. Technically, 3D DRAM is different from already established High Bandwidth Memory: HBM stacks several separately manufactured DRAM chips, while 3D DRAM is meant to integrate the memory cell layers themselves vertically to raise density. A successful entry would take TSMC into a market still dominated mainly by Samsung, SK hynix and Micron. At the same time, the report does not imply a near-term start of mass production, because heat, process integration and adequate yields are seen as open hurdles and development could take years. Against the backdrop of scarce and expensive memory for PCs and data centers, an additional manufacturer would be significant, but for now there is only a media report and possible development discussions.", "weitere_links": ["The Verge (via The Information)", "Seoul Economic Daily", "Wccftech (update)"], "_src": "406e56e5"}, "2026-11-06-openai-gpt6-cyber-bugs": {"titel": "OpenAI presents GPT-6 Cyber: claims 81 Firefox and 948 Linux LPE finds", "schlagzeile": "OpenAI GPT-6 Cyber finds 81 Firefox and 948 Linux bugs", "kurz": "OpenAI has presented GPT-6 Cyber, a non-public security model. According to the company it found 81 previously unknown high-severity Firefox vulnerabilities and developed exploits for 948 Linux local privilege escalation cases. The figures come from OpenAI and are not an independent full-audit confirmation.", "zusammenfassung": "BleepingComputer, Phoronix and Golem report on OpenAI's announcement of GPT-6 Cyber. The model is not public and currently limited to enabled customers in the Daybreak Red program. OpenAI says it discovered 81 previously unknown high-severity vulnerabilities in Firefox and co-developed patches; many have already been rolled out at Mozilla. For Linux kernel research OpenAI cites 2308 potential finds, 1724 reproduced vulnerabilities and 948 local privilege escalation exploits from unprivileged to root. In the ExploitGym benchmark the company cites a 48.5 percent success rate versus 32.1 percent for predecessor GPT-5.6 Cyber. In the Preparedness Framework OpenAI rates the cyber capability as \"Critical\". Independent audit depth on the scope and severity of the finds is limited – the figures are company claims, not proof that \"Linux is generally insecure\". OpenAI warns of a limited time window in which defenders should use frontier models for hardening before similar capabilities become more widely available.", "weitere_links": ["Phoronix: OpenAI 948 Linux LPE Bugs", "Golem: OpenAI claims nearly 1000 root vulnerabilities found"], "_src": "1b3a3edb"}, "2026-11-06-zen6-tee-riscv": {"titel": "AMD Zen 6: Firmware hint of RISC-V-based TEE instead of ARM PSP", "schlagzeile": "Zen 6: AMD switches TEE from ARM to RISC-V", "kurz": "A linux-firmware commit for AMD PMF Trusted Application on Zen 6 client (Family 1Ah M80h) mentions a RISC-V-based TEE. Until now the Secure Processor typically ran on ARM Cortex-A5 with TrustZone. Whether RISC-V is truly new from Zen 6 or only newly documented remains open.", "zusammenfassung": "Phoronix reports on a linux-firmware commit that adds PMF TA firmware v4 for platform 1AH_M80H – that corresponds to upcoming AMD Ryzen Zen 6 client CPUs. The commit text says the Trusted Application now runs on a RISC-V-based TEE, uses a larger shared-memory layout and extended policy conditions including up to 20 custom BIOS inputs. The Platform Management Framework controls among other things power, thermal and system behavior. Traditionally the AMD Platform Security Processor / Secure Processor was based on ARM Cortex-A5 with TrustZone. Phoronix finds no older public hints of a RISC-V TEE in Ryzen/EPYC and leaves open whether the feature is new for Zen 6 or was simply never mentioned on older SoCs. The commit does not name a final marketing label for the Ryzen generation. For Linux enablement and security enthusiasts the architecture switch is still a rare Zen 6 detail ahead of product launch.", "_src": "73845857"}, "2026-11-06-epic-linux-launcher-distros": {"titel": "Epic Games Launcher Preview: broad Linux distro support and AppImage return planned", "schlagzeile": "Epic: new launcher to support many Linux distros", "kurz": "Epic confirms to GamingOnLinux that the new launcher in preview should support as many Linux distributions as possible – explicitly including Fedora, SteamOS, Cachy and Omarchy among others. Packaging is still changing; AppImage is to return later this month. Preview does not mean a finished distro matrix.", "zusammenfassung": "GamingOnLinux asked Jake Jones (Communications Director, Epic Games) about Linux support for the new Epic Games Launcher. According to the statement Epic plans to support \"as many Linux distributions as possible\", including Fedora, SteamOS, Cachy, Omarchy and others. The preview started with AppImage, later switched to a .deb for Debian/Ubuntu; the FAQ named Fedora as coming soon. Epic is testing and evaluating packaging formats and wants to restore AppImage later this month. Until the matrix is fixed, formats can come and go. Flatpak/Flathub remains open in the report. Launcher status is Preview, not a final store rollout for every distro. Fortnite or Easy Anti-Cheat v2 are a separate topic and are not sold here as \"Fortnite is coming to Linux\". Together with the already known GOG Galaxy Linux window for 2027, competition among store clients on Linux remains interesting.", "_src": "e2ba62e3"}, "2026-11-06-mindfactory-cyberangriff": {"titel": "Mindfactory reports cyberattack: customer passwords reset, authority informed", "schlagzeile": "Mindfactory: hacker attack – passwords reset", "kurz": "Hardware shop Mindfactory reported a cyberattack on 6 November 2026 and informed customers and the data protection authority. Possibly affected: address, email, phone and encrypted passwords; bank data is not in the shop system according to the shop. All shop passwords were reset; phishing caution is advised.", "zusammenfassung": "heise online and Golem report that Mindfactory has become the victim of a cyberattack and informed customers via notice. The company has filed a criminal complaint and involved the competent data protection authority. On current knowledge Mindfactory cannot rule out that attackers accessed address, email, phone as well as encrypted stored passwords. Cleartext passwords and bank/credit card data are not affected according to the company, because payment data sits with service providers. All customer passwords for the shop were reset as a precaution; the next login requires a new password, going forward with a modern hash method. Managing director Marcel Kirchner speaks of a forensic investigation, no extortion and a closed vulnerability. Customers should be careful with unexpected emails, SMS or calls, because contact data could be abused for fraud. Transparency note: Mindfactory has belonged to the heise group since mid-2025; heise online is part of the same corporate group. Scope and exact attack timing were still being clarified at reporting time.", "weitere_links": ["Golem: Hackers attack Mindfactory", "GameStar: Cyberattack at Mindfactory"], "_src": "c989d014"}, "2026-11-06-nier-366gb-update": {"titel": "NieR: Automata update accidentally demands 366 GB of storage – fix announced", "schlagzeile": "NieR: Automata update eats 366 GB – studio apologizes", "kurz": "A Steam update for NieR: Automata on November 6, 2026 (JST) demands far more storage than intended — Insider Gaming cites 366 GB versus about 50 GB for the base game. It was meant to add languages; a fix and a DLC-deselect workaround were communicated.", "zusammenfassung": "Insider Gaming reports a faulty Steam update for NieR: Automata: after the November 6, 2026 (Japan time) update, install size is far larger than intended — about 366 GB of storage versus roughly 50 GB for the base game. Update notes said simplified Chinese, traditional Chinese and Korean would be added. The NieR Series account on X apologized and announced a fix. As a workaround, players can open Properties → DLC, uncheck the DLC items and keep playing the base game for now. No new story DLC has shipped since 2024; the game passed 10 million copies shipped/sold in February 2026. The short note does not explain the exact cause of the inflated download.", "_src": "c9a67187"}, "2026-11-06-qnap-plex2shell": {"titel": "QNAP warns: attackers compromise NAS devices via Plex2Shell flaws in Plex Media Server", "schlagzeile": "QNAP: hackers breach NAS via Plex2Shell – update Plex now", "kurz": "QNAP reports compromises of NAS devices through the Plex2Shell vulnerability chain in Plex Media Server. Users should update Plex in the App Center to at least 1.43.3.10861; if compromise is suspected, a clean OS reinstall may be required. QTS itself is not affected.", "zusammenfassung": "BleepingComputer covers a QNAP security advisory: several users reported that Plex Media Server on their NAS devices was compromised via the Plex2Shell flaws. Plex2Shell covers four vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-96652, CVE-2026-96654, CVE-2026-96655, CVE-2026-96656) reported by Zach Main on July 27; exploitation began after technical details went public on October 16. CISA added the CVEs to its Known Exploited catalog on October 20, 2026, with a short deadline for agencies. QNAP says the flaws exist only in Plex Media Server, not in QTS/QuTS hero. It recommends updating to Plex 1.43.3.10861 from the QNAP App Center. Anyone running a vulnerable, publicly reachable Plex server should treat the device as potentially compromised: updating does not remove payloads already installed. QNAP advises a clean reinstall of QTS/QuTS hero, credential resets, and — if remote access is needed — VPN instead of forwarding port 32400.", "_src": "48cb0d6c"}, "2026-11-06-ratchet-ranger-rumble": {"titel": "Ratchet & Clank: Ranger Rumble shut down – servers end May 2027", "schlagzeile": "Ratchet & Clank: Ranger Rumble dies – servers off May 1, 2027", "kurz": "The mobile Ratchet & Clank spin-off Ranger Rumble is cancelled: final update on November 6, 2026, removed from stores on November 21, servers shut down on May 1, 2027. The game was still in soft launch ahead of a planned global release.", "zusammenfassung": "IGN reports the shutdown of Ratchet & Clank: Ranger Rumble. Per the developer statement, the final planned update rolls out on November 6, 2026; the app leaves stores on November 21, 2026. Owners can keep playing until May 1, 2027, when servers go offline for good. In-app purchases were removed; refunds point to Apple or Google. The arena-shooter spin-off came from Oh BiBi with Insomniac Games and PlayStation Studios and was still in soft launch before a worldwide start, per IGN. As recently as July the PlayStation Blog spoke of an upcoming global launch after a successful test phase. VGC likewise covers the cancellation of the free-to-play mobile shooter.", "weitere_links": ["VGC: Sony’s Ratchet & Clank mobile shooter cancelled"], "_src": "99d65582"}, "2026-11-06-poe2-1-0-exilecon": {"titel": "Path of Exile 2 full release on 11 December 2026: Shadow, Duelist and League Conquerors of Wraeclast", "schlagzeile": "Path of Exile 2 1.0: Shadow, Duelist, launch 11 Dec", "kurz": "Grinding Gear Games announced the full release of Path of Exile 2 for 11 December 2026 at ExileCon. New are the Shadow and Duelist classes plus finished campaign acts five and six. Also coming is the league \"Conquerors of Wraeclast\" with base and army building.", "zusammenfassung": "PC Gamer summarizes the ExileCon keynote on Path of Exile 2 version 1.0: The full release after about two years of Early Access is dated for 11 December 2026. Two new classes launch with it: the dagger- and trap-focused Shadow with stealth, and the sword-heavy Duelist. Shadow can ascend as Assassin according to the studio or choose the new Ascendancy Infiltrator; a third Ascendancy is planned later. Stealth prevents monsters from seeing the character at range, resets on kill and interacts with traps that only trigger from hiding when revealed. The campaign gets acts five and six including a return to Oriath and an introduction to the league mechanic. \"Conquerors of Wraeclast\" brings base building, armies, commanders and later faction-bound Atlas battles. The endgame heavily streamlines the Atlas skill tree, reworks gems and the passive tree including jewel slots, and adds many new bases and uniques. Exact launch time and further Ascendancy details may still follow after the ongoing ExileCon.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer: Shadow class for PoE2 1.0"], "_src": "6ec09cc3"}, "2026-11-06-nvidia-11mio-diebstahl": {"titel": "NVIDIA hardware worth $11.4 million stolen in transit from Oakland to Texas", "schlagzeile": "$11.4M NVIDIA hardware: six pallets vanish on the way to Texas", "kurz": "Oakland police are investigating the theft of six pallets of NVIDIA hardware worth $11.4 million. A truck with a food-transport logo picked up the load on August 29 and disappeared; the trail ended in San Bernardino County. No arrests have been announced.", "zusammenfassung": "According to VideoCardz and local broadcaster ABC7 News, Oakland police (California) are investigating a major theft of NVIDIA hardware. Six pallets with a declared value of $11.4 million were bound from Oakland to Fort Worth, Texas. On August 29, 2026, a truck bearing a food-transport company logo collected the load as planned — then the vehicle and drivers vanished. Investigators tracked several multi-hour stops and lost the trail in San Bernardino County. The theft was reported to police only on September 13. Which exact products were on the pallets (AI accelerators, complete systems, or consumer GPUs) has not been publicly confirmed; the average value is about $1.9 million per pallet. UC Berkeley professor Olaf Groth told ABC7 such chips sell for much more abroad and pose a security risk. VideoCardz also notes earlier NVIDIA-related thefts in the Bay Area (over $7.5 million in 2025) and a Brazil case involving stolen ZOTAC RTX 5090 cards. So far there are no arrests and no confirmation that the cargo was recovered.", "weitere_links": ["ABC7 News: $11.4M Nvidia cargo stolen from Oakland", "Wccftech: NVIDIA GPUs Worth $11.4 Million Stolen"], "_src": "8bfcec8e"}, "2026-11-06-micron-fab-stop": {"titel": "Micron reportedly pauses construction of a RAM fab in Taiwan amid union dispute", "schlagzeile": "Micron halts RAM fab build in Taiwan – clash with unions", "kurz": "PCGH reports, citing Bloomberg, that Micron has stopped construction on a semiconductor fab in Taoyuan and put expansion plans on ice. Background is a conflict with Taiwanese unions over profit sharing. A full exit is not confirmed.", "zusammenfassung": "According to PC Games Hardware and Bloomberg sources on the ground, Micron has stopped construction on a planned semiconductor fab in Taoyuan, Taiwan, and wants to pause expansion plans. PCGH puts the investment at around €4 billion. The move falls into a longer conflict with unions demanding employee participation in soaring profits. In Taichung a compromise was reached two weeks ago whose acceptance among workers is disputed; in Taoyuan talks continue, including a symbolic strike — the first in Taiwan’s semiconductor industry. The Taoyuan Labour Union rejects blame and says it does not want to endanger company profits. Whether the stop is permanent or a bargaining lever remains open. For PC buyers the story matters because extra RAM capacity is seen as a way out of the memory shortage — and that capacity is now stalled.", "_src": "2080eae5"}, "2026-11-06-switch2-verkauf-minus37": {"titel": "Switch 2: Nintendo reports 37.4% fewer hardware sales in the half-year comparison", "schlagzeile": "Switch 2: 37% fewer sales than record prior year – software up", "kurz": "Per Nintendo’s results and GameStar, Switch 2 sell-in from April to September 2026 fell 37.4% to 6.49 million units (prior year 10.36M). Software rose 18.8%; the full-year forecast of 16.5 million devices stands.", "zusammenfassung": "GameStar summarizes Nintendo’s half-year figures: from April to September 2026 Nintendo sold 6.49 million Switch 2 consoles to the trade — 37.4% fewer than the 10.36 million in the prior-year period. Q1 saw 3.82 million, July–September another 2.67 million. The year-ago comparison is skewed by the June 5, 2025 launch and pent-up demand. Since September the Switch 2 has been more expensive (Europe officially €499.99). Nintendo cites memory prices, exchange rates and oil prices for the hike. The full-year forecast of 16.5 million units through March 2027 remains unchanged per GameStar and VGC. Switch 2 software rose 18.8% to 24.49 million units in the half; net profit rose eleven percent. VGC also notes Switch 2 still leads original Switch and PS5 on a launch-aligned cumulative basis. These are sell-in figures, not necessarily end-customer sales.", "weitere_links": ["Nintendo IR: Financial Results Explanatory Material", "VGC: Switch 2 sales down 37%, still beating original"], "_src": "9aaf69f1"}, "2026-11-06-rtx5070ti-doppel-msrp": {"titel": "GeForce RTX 5070 Ti nears twice MSRP in US online stores", "schlagzeile": "RTX 5070 Ti hits $1,340 – nearly double MSRP in US shops", "kurz": "After the RTX 5090 and 5080, the RTX 5070 Ti is also surging: the cheapest tracked US online offer is $1,339.99, with some models at $1,499.99. Launch MSRP was $749. NVIDIA had previously denied discontinuation rumors.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz reports that the GeForce RTX 5070 Ti is now selling well above MSRP at major US online retailers. The card launched in February 2025 at a $749 MSRP; the cheapest tracked offer on November 6, 2026 is $1,339.99 (about 79% above MSRP). Individual models at B&H and Best Buy sit around $1,400 to $1,499.99 — near or at double the launch price. Within eight days the cheapest tracked price rose by $160 (from $1,179.99 on October 29). Cited examples: GIGABYTE AERO OC at Newegg for $1,339.99, ASUS PRIME OC and TUF GAMING OC at B&H for $1,399.99 and $1,499.99. In January 2026 NVIDIA denied discontinuation rumors for the 5070 Ti; ASUS then pointed to memory supply constraints. The card remains available, so a production stop is not proven — but the price spiral after the RTX 5090 and 5080 continues for the 5070 Ti.", "_src": "d18a0453"}, "2026-11-06-asus-xg-core-9060xt": {"titel": "ASUS XG Core: external Radeon RX 9060 XT LP 16 GB over USB4 for laptops and handhelds", "schlagzeile": "ASUS XG Core: external RX 9060 XT LP 16 GB via USB4", "kurz": "ASUS unveils XG Core: a compact external graphics box with Radeon RX 9060 XT LP 16 GB GDDR6 and USB4 for compatible laptops, mini PCs and handhelds such as the ROG Ally X. No official price yet; a Swedish shop lists about €1,207 incl. VAT per TechPowerUp.", "zusammenfassung": "In a press release published by TechPowerUp, ASUS announces XG Core: an external graphics unit with AMD Radeon RX 9060 XT LP (RDNA 4) and 16 GB GDDR6. The box measures about 144 × 117 × 39 mm and connects via USB4 to compatible hosts — ASUS also mentions Thunderbolt 3 systems and handhelds such as ROG Ally X and ROG Xbox Ally X. HDMI and DisplayPort are built in; tuning uses GPU Tweak III. ASUS pitches gaming, creative work and local AI workloads (e.g. ComfyUI, LM Studio, Ollama). An official list price is missing from the release; TechPowerUp comments cite a Swedish shop at about $1,346 / €1,207 incl. 25% VAT — not a confirmed MSRP. Availability in DE/AT is still unclear.", "_src": "e27a1951"}, "2026-11-06-medusa-point-6-8-kerne": {"titel": "More Zen 6 Medusa Point samples: 6 and 8 cores in Lenovo Geekbench entries", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Medusa Point 2/3 with 6 and 8 cores shows up at Lenovo", "kurz": "After the 10-core sample, two more AMD Zen 6 Medusa Point engineering samples supposedly appeared in Geekbench 7: 8 cores (2+6) and 6 cores (1+5), both labeled Medusa Point 2/3 on Lenovo systems. Unconfirmed; clocks and scores vary widely.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz reports two further Geekbench 7 entries for AMD Zen 6 Medusa Point, this time with 6 and 8 cores and the Medusa Point 2/3 label. Both samples were tested on Lenovo systems. The 8-core sample (100-000002152-50_Y) has 16 threads in 2+6 clusters and 8 MB L3; the 6-core sample (100-000001658-50_Y) has 12 threads in 1+5 and 4 MB L3. Both share CPU ID Family 26 Model 224 Stepping 0, unlike the 10-core Medusa Point 1 sample. Geekbench 7 scores: 8C later run 2,889 / 15,099 (max reported 5.28 GHz), earlier run much weaker; 6C 1,732 / 8,340 at only ~2.04 GHz. VideoCardz stresses that clock readings and scores for engineering samples fluctuate heavily and are not final. A Zen 6 mobile debut is expected around CES 2027. AMD has not confirmed the samples.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: Geekbench 7 entries of engineering samples on Lenovo systems, reported by VideoCardz. Clocks and scores vary widely between runs. Not a final product; AMD has not confirmed.", "_src": "66dba83d"}, "2026-11-06-windows11-27h2": {"titel": "Windows 11 27H2 is set to renew the technical platform for the first time in three years", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 27H2: real platform update, not just another UI year", "kurz": "Dr. Windows reports, citing The Verge: version 27H2 in 2027 should renew Windows 11’s kernel and driver foundation — the first change since 24H2/25H2/26H2, which were technically identical. Reports say Windows 12 is not planned for 2027.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Dr. Windows (citing The Verge), Windows 11 faces a platform update with version 27H2 in 2027. Since 24H2, versions 25H2 and 26H2 have been identical at the technical base (kernel, driver model and core components); new features mainly touched UI and swappable parts. 27H2 is set to change that base for the first time in three years. That can require compatibility checks — especially for system-near software such as security products. Whether some features will be artificially tied to 27H2 remains open. The reports also stress that this does not announce Windows 12 for 2027; it stays Windows 11. The story largely confirms plans Microsoft sketched earlier. The Verge itself is paywalled; the core claim is corroborated via Dr. Windows and Golem (“no Windows 12”).", "weitere_links": ["Golem.de: No Windows 12 likely next year"], "_src": "76b75cda"}, "2026-11-06-msi-claw-fsr41": {"titel": "MSI aims to bring FSR 4.1 to the Claw A8 in December via OEM driver", "schlagzeile": "MSI Claw A8: FSR 4.1 due in December via OEM driver", "kurz": "MSI confirms the Claw A8 (Ryzen Z2 Extreme / Radeon 890M) should get AMD FSR Upscaling 4.1 through its own graphics driver — target December 2026, subject to validation. A current driver fixes render bugs but does not yet include FSR 4.1.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz reports, citing MSI: the Claw A8 handheld should receive AMD FSR Upscaling 4.1 via a manufacturer graphics driver. MSI targets December 2026 if validation succeeds. The Claw A8 uses AMD’s Ryzen Z2 Extreme with Radeon 890M. AMD opened FSR 4.1 for Ryzen Z2 Extreme and other handheld APUs on October 20; standard Adrenalin drivers do not officially support handhelds, so makers such as MSI, ASUS or Lenovo must ship their own drivers. Driver 32.0.32016.5 for the Claw A8 BZ2EM is already available: it fixes wrong shadows, lighting glitches, FSR artifacts, particle issues and black squares — but still lacks FSR 4.1. That confirms an official FSR 4.1 path instead of unofficial modded drivers.", "_src": "fa2c559e"}, "2026-11-06-nvidia-dlss-override-19": {"titel": "NVIDIA App: DLSS Override for 19 more games, including Witcher 3 and PUBG", "schlagzeile": "NVIDIA App: DLSS Override enabled for 19 more games", "kurz": "An NVIDIA App update adds DLSS Override profiles for 19 more titles. They include older games such as The Witcher 3 and PUBG as well as upcoming or announced releases. Override lets users force newer DLSS models and modes where the driver supports it.", "zusammenfassung": "TechPowerUp reports NVIDIA App update 11.0.9.585 with DLSS Override support for 19 more games plus Optimal Settings profiles for six titles. The Override list includes Honeycomb: The World Beyond, WARDOGS, PUBG: Battlegrounds, Aniimo, 007 First Light, Active Matter, Enlisted, Dragon's Dogma 2, The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt, AION 2, Halloween: The Game, HOT WHEELS Infinite Rush, Silent Hill: Townfall, Control Resonant, Ace Combat 8: Wings of Theve, Dynasty Warriors 3 Complete Edition Remastered, Star Wars: Galactic Racer, Gears of War: E-Day and Clive Barker's Hellraiser: Revival. Optimal Settings arrive among others for AION 2, Aniimo, Control Resonant, EA Sports FC 27, Gears of War: E-Day and Star Wars: Galactic Racer. Some titles were already listed in earlier builds according to TechPowerUp; NVIDIA does not explain the duplicates and does not say which override options each game gets. DLSS Override sits under Graphics program settings and can force newer DLSS models or modes such as DLAA when a game does not offer them. The changelog otherwise only mentions general stability and security fixes.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz: 19 DLSS Override profiles"], "_src": "df35ce8c"}, "2026-11-06-unity-buyout-gespraeche": {"titel": "Reports: Silver Lake and Saudi PIF allegedly held preliminary talks on a Unity buyout", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Silver Lake and PIF allegedly talking about buying Unity", "kurz": "According to a Reuters report, Silver Lake and the Saudi Public Investment Fund held preliminary talks about acquiring Unity after the EA deal. Secondary reports mention valuation figures around about $25 billion. No deal is guaranteed; shares jumped on the buzz.", "zusammenfassung": "Several outlets, citing Reuters, report that Silver Lake and the Saudi Public Investment Fund held preliminary talks about a possible Unity acquisition. The same actors were recently involved in the large EA deal; Silver Lake reportedly already holds a minority stake in Unity. Insider Gaming cites a valuation on the order of about $25 billion and says Unity is reviewing options with a bank. These are explicitly early talks; a deal is not guaranteed. The rumors alone reportedly pushed the share price up noticeably, with one report citing nearly 15 percent. Unity is best known for its namesake engine and powers many large games. The situation remains unconfirmed until Unity or the investors comment officially. Reliability: medium because Reuters is the origin, but talks are preliminary.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: Reuters report on preliminary talks, picked up by PC Gamer, Insider Gaming and IGN. No completed deal; Unity is reviewing options with a bank. Figures and outcome open.", "ursprungsquelle": "Reuters", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming: Silver Lake and PIF allegedly want Unity", "IGN: Silver Lake and PIF reportedly seeking Unity"], "_src": "f1589ccc"}, "2026-11-06-amd-pc-markt-2027": {"titel": "AMD plans for a double-digit decline in PC shipments in 2027 due to high memory prices", "schlagzeile": "AMD: PC market set to shrink double-digit in 2027 – RAM prices weigh", "kurz": "On the earnings call, Lisa Su said AMD is planning for a double-digit decline in global PC unit shipments in 2027. The reason is higher memory and component prices weighing on demand. This is a planning assumption for the overall market, not measured decline yet.", "zusammenfassung": "On the Q3 2026 earnings call, AMD CEO Lisa Su said the company is planning for PC market unit shipments to decline by a double-digit percentage in 2027. She cites higher memory and component costs that make desktops and notebooks more expensive and weigh on demand. AMD will align sell-in with sell-through to keep customer and channel inventories healthy. Despite the expected market weakness, AMD expects to outperform via its Ryzen roadmap and growing commercial business. In parallel, AMD expects Data Center to account for more than 80 percent of company revenue in 2027. Client revenue rose 7 percent in Q3 to $2.9 billion; Gaming fell 40 percent to $773 million, mainly on weaker semi-custom sales in the console cycle. PCGH stresses this is a planning assumption, not a measured market result yet. VideoCardz covers the same earnings-call remarks. RAM prices barely register in Google Trends DE right now, but the story still matters for hardware buyers.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz: AMD expects double-digit PC market decline in 2027"], "_src": "093d57bb"}, "2026-11-06-rx9070xt-clustered-geometry": {"titel": "Microsoft Agility SDK: biggest DirectX ray tracing update since 2018 – Clustered Geometry and PTLAS", "schlagzeile": "DirectX: biggest ray tracing update since 2018 – Clustered Geometry", "kurz": "With Agility SDK 1.722 Preview, Microsoft released its most extensive DirectX ray tracing update since 2018. Clustered Geometry and Partitioned TLAS are meant to speed up building ray-tracing structures and cut memory use. In independent PCGH demo measurements, an RX 9070 XT rises from 1.7 to 91 fps; games still have to adopt the APIs.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft calls the new DirectX ray tracing features in Agility SDK 1.722 Preview the most extensive expansion since DXR launched in 2018. Key pieces are Clustered Geometry (CLAS), Partitioned Top-Level Acceleration Structures (PTLAS) and indirect acceleration-structure builds. Clustered Geometry splits geometry into reusable clusters of up to 256 triangles; that should make building ray-tracing structures in detailed, dynamic scenes much faster and enable more accurate reflections and shadows without costly proxy geometry. PTLAS is meant to update only changed scene regions. According to ComputerBase and Microsoft, an example on a Radeon RX 9070 rose from 1.2 to 79 fps, while structure memory fell from about 7519 to 774 MB; scratch memory rose sharply instead. PC Games Hardware also measured the D3D12RaytracingClusteredGeometry demo independently: an RX 9070 XT went from 1.7 to 91 fps at 1600×920 (about 54×), with BVH memory from 7518 to 771 MiB; an RTX 5080 from 1.4 to 310 fps. Without Clustered Geometry the Radeon was slightly ahead; with the feature the RTX 5080 was clearly faster. The preview runs on GeForce RTX, Radeon RX 9000, Intel Arc B-series and supported Core Ultra iGPUs; new hardware features are not required, but driver support is. Existing games do not benefit automatically: studios must integrate the APIs. Advanced Shader Delivery and other Agility SDK 1.620 features are part of the same release package but are not part of the ray-tracing demo numbers.", "weitere_links": ["Microsoft DirectX Blog: Agility SDK 1.620 / 1.722 Preview", "Microsoft: Clustered Geometry and PTLAS Preview", "PCGH: RX 9070 XT / RTX 5080 in Clustered Geometry demo"], "_src": "3d54cb6e"}, "2026-11-05-asrock-rx7900-vbios": {"titel": "ASRock VBIOS for RX 7900 XT/XTX: owners report bricked GPUs after official update", "schlagzeile": "ASRock VBIOS bricks RX 7900 XT/XTX – downloads apparently pulled", "kurz": "After the official ASRock VBIOS from late October, owners of Radeon RX 7900 XT and XTX Phantom Gaming as well as Taichi report that their cards no longer start. The update was meant to address AMD-SN-6023 and ran via ASRVBFlash 1.0.5. HTTP downloads are reportedly now 404; some cards were only recovered with an external EEPROM programmer.", "zusammenfassung": "In late October ASRock released new VBIOS files for ten Radeon RX 7000 cards, including as part of AMD security measure AMD-SN-6023. Several owners now report that after flashing with ASRVBFlash 1.0.5 the system no longer POSTs with the GPU installed. Models named include RX 7900 XT Phantom Gaming as well as RX 7900 XTX Phantom Gaming and Taichi including the White edition. Reports involve different motherboards, for example from ASRock and MSI. VideoCardz documents the sequence: the tool checks compatibility, Windows restarts, then the PC no longer boots with the card. At least two users restored their RX 7900 XTX Phantom Gaming with external EEPROM programmers, including a T48 with a test clip. The October downloads reportedly return HTTP 404 now, while FTP links may still work. A user in Japan reportedly received confirmation from ASRock support that the failure would be covered under warranty; there is no public company-wide statement or official recovery procedure yet according to VideoCardz and Guru3D. Until ASRock clarifies and ships corrected firmware, owners of the named models should not install the October firmware. Source: VideoCardz, with Guru3D as secondary.", "weitere_links": ["Guru3D: ASRock RX 7000 VBIOS and brick reports"], "_src": "1ae75289"}, "2026-11-05-gog-galaxy-linux-2027": {"titel": "New GOG Galaxy coming in 2027 – with full Linux support", "schlagzeile": "GOG Galaxy 2027: new client with full Linux support", "kurz": "At its first GOG Showcase, GOG confirmed that a new Galaxy client with full Linux support will arrive in 2027. The Windows and Mac clients are being reworked in parallel. Galaxy remains optional; offline installers stay.", "zusammenfassung": "GamingOnLinux reports from the first GOG Showcase: in 2027 a completely new GOG Galaxy client for all platforms is to arrive, for the first time with full Linux support. GOG had already told GamingOnLinux in July it was working on this; the timeline is now public. According to GOG’s statement the client on Windows and Mac should become simpler and faster with a cleaner library view. The core promise remains: Galaxy is optional, and games can still be downloaded and kept via offline installers. Interested users can sign up for the beta on the GOG anniversary page once it opens. GOG is also working on GOG Social, a modernized community experience with threads, media and game-related tags. The report does not name further Linux-client feature details; nothing is speculated here.", "_src": "aa4b3b79"}, "2026-11-05-medusa-point-gb7": {"titel": "AMD Zen 6 Medusa Point appears in Geekbench 7: 10 cores, single-core above 9950X3D average", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Medusa Point in Geekbench 7 – 10C ES beats 9950X3D in SC?", "kurz": "An unconfirmed Geekbench 7 result shows an AMD Medusa Point engineering sample with 10 cores and 20 threads. The single-core score is 3100 points, slightly above the Ryzen 9 9950X3D average. Reported clocks around 2.0 GHz look implausible for a final product.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz and TechPowerUp report a Geekbench 7 listing for engineering sample 100-000001713-32_Y on a Lenovo platform. It shows 10 cores and 20 threads in two clusters of 4 plus 6 cores, plus 16 MB L3 cache. The single-core score is 3100 points, about 1.6 percent above the Ryzen 9 9950X3D average of 3051 according to VideoCardz. Multi-core is 18313 points. Base and max frequency are listed around 2.0 GHz / 1996 MHz; that looks unbelievable for retail clocks and is treated as a typical ES or misread artifact. TechPowerUp describes the clusters as a possible Zen 6 and Zen 6c mix and notes AVX-512 support in the listing. This is not a final product; specs, clocks and launch date remain open. Earlier Geekbench 6 scores for the same product are not directly comparable due to different workloads. Reliability: medium, because only a public benchmark listing via leaker channels is available.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: Geekbench 7 listing of an engineering sample (100-000001713-32_Y) on a Lenovo platform, reported by VideoCardz and TechPowerUp via HXL. Clocks look implausible (around 2.0 GHz). Not a final product; AMD has not confirmed anything.", "ursprungsquelle": "Geekbench via HXL", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp: Medusa Point 10C/20T in Geekbench"], "_src": "ba3c17d9"}, "2026-11-05-switch2-keine-preiserhoehung": {"titel": "Nintendo rules out further Switch 2 price rises – despite weaker console sales", "schlagzeile": "Nintendo: no further Switch 2 price increase planned", "kurz": "Nintendo president Shuntaro Furukawa rules out further Switch 2 price increases. The company says it is sufficiently supplied with memory chips. At the same time, media report falling console sales and lower profit in the latest quarter.", "zusammenfassung": "Presenting the latest results, Nintendo president Shuntaro Furukawa said according to PC Games, Eurogamer, VGC and IGN that no further Switch 2 price increase is planned. Nintendo has secured enough memory capacity and currently sees no reason for another adjustment. Nintendo had already raised Switch 2 prices earlier, including by $50 / €30 in several regions. IGN cites Bloomberg with a 16 percent drop in operating profit to 73.9 billion yen in the quarter to end of September, and 2.67 million Switch 2 units sold in that period. VGC speaks of an about 37 percent decline in Switch 2 sales in the same reporting context, while Nintendo says Switch 2 still outsells its predecessor in the comparison window. By end of September about 26 million Switch 2 consoles had been sold in total. Nintendo is keeping its forecasts for the current fiscal year according to PC Games. Memory shortages remain an industry theme; Nintendo is positioning itself differently from recent PS5 and Xbox price hikes.", "weitere_links": ["IGN: Nintendo rules out further Switch 2 price rises", "Eurogamer: No plans for more Switch 2 price hikes", "VGC: Nintendo not considering Switch 2 price hike"], "_src": "487162c1"}, "2026-11-05-dlss5-hogwarts-legacy": {"titel": "Hogwarts Legacy gets DLSS 5 with 3D-Guided Neural Rendering on GeForce RTX 50", "schlagzeile": "DLSS 5 Neural Rendering now in Hogwarts Legacy", "kurz": "Since 5 November 2026 Hogwarts Legacy on PC supports NVIDIA DLSS 5 with 3D-Guided Neural Rendering. The feature needs a GeForce RTX 50 and a current Game Ready driver; Display settings have the \"Neural Rendering\" switch. Marketing FPS figures are not an everyday promise.", "zusammenfassung": "NVIDIA and Portkey Games report that Hogwarts Legacy on PC has received DLSS 5 with 3D-Guided Neural Rendering. The tech is meant to enrich lighting and material detail with AI while keeping the engine's geometry and textures as the foundation; developers can steer the result via artist controls. Requirement per support article: a GeForce RTX 50 series plus GeForce Game Ready Driver 616.64 or newer. Activation under Display settings: Upscale Type to NVIDIA DLSS, then enable Neural Rendering; shortcut Shift+Alt+B. Supported stores: Steam, Epic Games Store and Windows Store. Per NVIDIA blog of 5 November 2026, War Thunder follows with DLSS 5 mid-November, Where Winds Meet on 23 November. The feature is tied to RTX 50 or matching cloud/Spark paths and does not replace classic upscaling alone. We do not take FPS marketing from demos as a practice promise.", "weitere_links": ["Portkey Games: Enable DLSS 5 in Hogwarts Legacy", "NVIDIA Blog: GFN Thursday Hogwarts DLSS 5"], "_src": "beddaa04"}, "2026-11-05-xbox-pc-app-60": {"titel": "Xbox PC app: Microsoft promises up to 60 percent faster launch for Insiders", "schlagzeile": "Xbox PC app launches up to 60% faster – Insiders first", "kurz": "Xbox Insiders can try a revised Xbox PC app from 05.11.2026. Microsoft talks of an up to 60 percent faster launch as well as noticeably snappier pages and windows. In parallel, a refreshed web and cloud gaming experience is rolling out to more players.", "zusammenfassung": "Jason Beaumont, VP Xbox Experiences, announced a faster and clearer Xbox experience for PC, web and cloud on Xbox Wire on 05.11.2026. Xbox Insiders should be able to use the updated Xbox PC app right away. According to Microsoft tests, the app launches up to 60 percent faster; pages such as Home, Store and Game Pass load up to 50 percent faster, and in-app windows open up to 65 percent faster. The figures depend on device, network, configuration and usage, Microsoft notes. The library gets simpler navigation, new filters and better sorting. Friends and social features move into the main navigation. Search covers games including installed titles and add-ons as well as people. Visually there are revised game cards, Home, settings and animations. The web experience for Xbox Cloud Gaming previously shown to Insiders is meant to reach more players automatically in the coming weeks; anyone who wants to try earlier can open play.xbox.com. There is a Library tab for cloud games (purchased and Game Pass), a desktop mode for larger screens, plus dark/light mode and five high-contrast themes. A similar refresh is also beginning for cloud apps on supported TVs and VR headsets. Anyone who is not yet an Insider can join via the Xbox Insider Hub for Series X|S, Xbox One or Windows. The Verge, Neowin and IGN cover the announcement.", "weitere_links": ["The Verge: Xbox PC app redesign", "IGN: Xbox PC app 60% faster according to Microsoft", "Neowin: Redesign and faster launches"], "_src": "f708d215"}, "2026-11-05-nova-lake-h-foto": {"titel": "Leak: Photo allegedly shows an unreleased Intel Nova Lake-H package with multi-tile design", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Does this photo already show Intel's Nova Lake-H with 16 cores?", "kurz": "A photo shared by momomo_us allegedly shows an as-yet unreleased Intel processor package with several visible silicon tiles. When asked, Jaykihn confirmed a Nova Lake-H configuration with 4+8+4 cores. Intel has confirmed nothing; the image origin remains unclear.", "zusammenfassung": "Hardware leaker momomo_us (188号) shared a cropped photo on X on 05.11.2026 that, according to VideoCardz, is meant to show an as-yet unreleased Intel processor package with several visible silicon tiles. VideoCardz could not trace the industrial or embedded motherboard origin of the image; only the package is visible. Asked whether it was Nova Lake-H with a 4+8+4 configuration, leaker Jaykihn replied \"Yes\". In an update, momomo_us according to VideoCardz named 16 CPU cores, 4 Xe GPU cores and 18 MB of cache. That core count matches the rumored Core Ultra 9 4970H with 4+8+4, i.e. 16 CPU cores. In the VideoCardz table, however, the rumored 4970H is listed with 12 Xe3P graphics cores – that differs from momomo's \"4 Xe\" figure; which GPU figure is correct remains open. Whether the pictured sample is specifically the 4970H is unclear; VideoCardz does not mention clock speeds. For comparison, several Panther Lake-H models also use 4+8+4. TechPowerUp and Wccftech pick up the leak. Intel has not confirmed the claims.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: photo from leaker momomo_us (@momomo_us / 188号); Jaykihn replied \"Yes\" when asked about the 4+8+4 configuration. VideoCardz could not trace the origin of the cropped image. Intel has confirmed nothing; clock frequencies unknown.", "ursprungsquelle": "momomo_us (@momomo_us) on X", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp: Nova Lake-H SoC surfaces", "Wccftech: Nova Lake-H with six-tile setup"], "_src": "86f9c2aa"}, "2026-11-05-gta6-39-screenshots": {"titel": "Rockstar releases about 39 new official GTA 6 screenshots – two weeks to the US launch", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: Rockstar shows 39 new screenshots – two weeks to launch", "kurz": "Rockstar Games has released about 39 new official screenshots for Grand Theft Auto VI. The occasion is the countdown: in the US about two weeks remain until the 19.11.2026 launch. The images include scenes from Vice City / Leonida as well as Jason and Lucia.", "zusammenfassung": "Rockstar Games has officially released a large set of new screenshots for Grand Theft Auto VI. IGN and other outlets speak of 39 new images marking the final two weeks before the US launch. The US launch date 19.11.2026 is cited as the reference point. According to IGN, IGN Germany and PC Gamer, motifs include Vice City / Leonida scenes, protagonists Jason and Lucia, crime and nightlife moments, plus details such as dancers, combat dogs and very detailed skin pores. The screenshots come from Rockstar / the official site and the Rockstar X channel; they are confirmed marketing images, not leaks. Nothing beyond what the sources describe is speculated here. Google Trends DE shows GTA 6 at 60 as the highest of the compared terms over seven days; AT is at 41.", "weitere_links": ["IGN Germany: 39 new GTA 6 screenshots", "PC Gamer: launch screenshots with dancers, combat dogs and pores", "Rockstar Games (official site)"], "_src": "eb8f6ed6"}, "2026-11-05-discord-native-windows": {"titel": "Discord rebuilds Windows client in Rust: early build uses about 290 MB RAM instead of Electron gigabytes", "schlagzeile": "Discord leaves Electron: Rust client aims to end RAM hunger", "kurz": "Discord wants to move the Windows desktop client from Electron to a native Rust app with GPUI. An early build called Discord Phoenix shows about 290 MB RAM in a CTO screenshot. The current Electron app can reportedly reach the range of 4 GB.", "zusammenfassung": "Discord CTO Stanislav Vishnevskiy announced that Discord is dropping Electron for a Rust desktop app using GPUI. ComputerBase and Windows Latest cover the announcement. An early Windows 11 screenshot lists Discord Phoenix at 290.2 MB RAM. Windows Latest notes that Discord itself tested restarting the client when memory exceeds 4 GB, and that normal use is often under 1 GB while idle can easily reach 1 to 2 GB. Discord already uses Rust for infrastructure, voice and parts of the current client; now the whole client is to follow. When tests or the public rollout start is open. The move fits Microsoft’s Windows 11 efficiency agenda to run less memory-hungry apps on weaker PCs. It remains to be seen whether feature parity and stability will match the Electron version.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Latest: Electron out, Rust build at ~290 MB"], "_src": "5da0f5ef"}, "2026-11-05-fsr-412-xbox": {"titel": "AMD FSR Upscaling 4.1.2 available to Xbox Series X|S developers in the October 2026 GDK", "schlagzeile": "FSR 4.1.2 comes to Xbox – AI upscaling for the first time", "kurz": "With the Microsoft GDK from October 2026, developers can use AMD FSR Upscaling 4.1.2 on Xbox Series X and S. For the first time, ML-based AMD FSR upscaling is available on the consoles. Existing games do not get it automatically; studios must integrate it.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD announced on GPUOpen that FSR Upscaling 4.1.2 is available for Xbox Series X|S via the Microsoft Game Development Kit from October 2026. Alexander Blake-Davies writes that this brings ML-based AMD FSR upscaling to the Xbox consoles for the first time; previously only analytical FSR was available there. For Series X and Series S there are two INT8 models: Full and a new Lite. According to AMD, Lite is less than half the size and offloads the GPU more. Both run on Series X and Series S. Upscaler memory use depends on render and output resolution, not on the model – so the choice is a performance trade-off, not a memory one. The API matches the FSR SDK under Windows; quality modes are Native AA, Quality, Balanced, Performance and Ultra Performance. Via FSR SDK 2.4 and an ASUS preview driver, the technology also applies to ROG Xbox Ally handhelds (Ally X and X20 first). This is about developer access: studios must integrate it, there are no automatic updates for existing games, and AMD has not named specific titles. VideoCardz, PC Gamer and TechPowerUp report on it.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz: FSR 4.1.2 with ML on Series X|S", "PC Gamer: FSR 4.1.2 on Xbox and handhelds", "TechPowerUp: FSR Upscaling 4.1.2 for Xbox"], "_src": "71d4e824"}, "2026-11-05-geforce-8800-gtx-demo": {"titel": "Free Steam demo \"GeForce 8800 GTX – 20 Years of a Legend\" celebrates 20 years of the CUDA GPU", "schlagzeile": "Nvidia lets you unbox the 8800 GTX – but needs an RTX 4070", "kurz": "Since 05.11.2026 the free demo \"GeForce 8800 GTX – 20 Years of a Legend\" is available on Steam. It lets you unbox the 2006 card and install it in a contemporary PC – rendered with path tracing and DLSS 4.5. An RTX 4070 is required as a minimum.", "zusammenfassung": "For the roughly 20th anniversary of the GeForce 8800 GTX (market launch on 08.11.2006), the free Steam demo \"GeForce 8800 GTX – 20 Years of a Legend\" was released on 05.11.2026. It was created by Unreal Engine artist Dylan Browne with support from NVIDIA. The semi-interactive demo lets you unbox the card, install it in a PC of the era and explore a 2006 gaming room with Easter eggs. Technically it uses path tracing, DLSS 4.5 with Ray Reconstruction and Dynamic Multi Frame Generation as well as RTX Mega Geometry. Steam system requirements list an RTX 4070, 32 GB RAM, 30 GB of storage and driver 621.12 or newer as the minimum; an RTX 5080 is recommended. The 8800 GTX was considered the first CUDA-capable GPU. A version for GeForce NOW Ultimate is said to follow soon according to reports from eTeknix and The Verge. VideoCardz and Wccftech also cover the campaign.", "weitere_links": ["eTeknix: 20th-anniversary Steam demo", "The Verge: 8800 GTX unboxing demo", "VideoCardz: Unboxing game needs RTX 4070", "Wccftech: GeForce 8800 GTX turns 20"], "_src": "16d23a91"}, "2026-11-05-openssh-musl-bypass": {"titel": "OpenSSH and musl: Long passwords can crack passwordless accounts – fix in 10.6p2", "schlagzeile": "OpenSSH flaw: long passwords crack locked logins (musl)", "kurz": "On some Linux systems with musl and without PAM, attackers can crack accounts without a password hash using a very long password. OpenSSH 10.6p2 and updated Alpine packages close the gap; sshd must be restarted afterwards. Until then, PasswordAuthentication no helps.", "zusammenfassung": "OpenSSH and Alpine Linux warn of a severe but niche flaw in OpenSSH without PAM on musl-based systems. According to Alpine and heise, the Alpine package openssh-server (without PAM) or openssh-server-pam with UsePAM no is mainly affected. If an attacker reaches the SSH port and PasswordAuthentication is enabled, they can log in without knowing a password – if at least one account has \"*\" in the shadow field (typical for key-only) and at the same time at least one local account has a $5$ or $6$ hash. The attack sends a very long password of 257 to 1024 bytes: musl-crypt() returns \"*\" as an error value for keys over 256 bytes, which matches the stored \"*\" and lets the check pass. No CVE had been assigned at the time of the advisories. The fix is in OpenSSH 10.6p2; Alpine has published updated packages. After the upgrade, sshd must be restarted. Workaround: set PasswordAuthentication no and restart sshd. OpenSSH developer Damien Miller advises disabling password logins immediately. According to heise, the project assumes the bug is rather not caused in OpenSSH itself, but 10.6p2 mitigates it. The issue was reported by Özgün Kültekin of Wakefield; BleepingComputer and Alpine describe the conditions in detail.", "weitere_links": ["heise: OpenSSH and Alpine warn of flaw", "BleepingComputer: Flaw in password-locked accounts"], "_src": "beadd996"}, "2026-11-04-gta6-vorbestellungen-750-mio": {"titel": "GTA 6: Sensor Tower estimates over 750 million US dollars in pre-order revenue", "schlagzeile": "Analysts: GTA 6 makes over $750M before it even launches", "kurz": "According to an estimate by analytics firm Sensor Tower, GTA 6 had been pre-ordered around 7.7 million times by 03.11.2026. That equals roughly 751 million US dollars in revenue on PS5 and Xbox. There are no official figures on this from Rockstar or Take-Two.", "zusammenfassung": "According to IGN, analytics firm Sensor Tower has analysed the pre-orders of Grand Theft Auto VI. By 03.11.2026, an estimated 7.71 million copies had been pre-ordered, which equals around 751 million US dollars in revenue. Most of it comes from the PlayStation 5: Sensor Tower sees about 74 percent of pre-orders and around 559 million US dollars there, and about 26 percent and around 192 million US dollars on Xbox. The Ultimate Edition costs 100 US dollars, the standard version 80 US dollars. According to IGN, Take-Two CEO Strauss Zelnick sees the pre-orders mainly as a sign of the most loyal fans. For comparison: according to IGN, GTA 5 made 800 million US dollars in its first 24 hours in 2013 and passed one billion after three days. Whether GTA 6 breaks that record will only be clear after launch. Important: this is an estimate by a market research firm, not figures from Rockstar or Take-Two. GTA 6 launches on 19.11.2026 for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S, and a PC version has still not been announced.", "_src": "e55d6220"}, "2026-11-04-windows-paint-luecke": {"titel": "Windows 11: Security flaw in Paint (CVE-2026-83844) – patched version not reaching many users", "schlagzeile": "Flaw in Windows Paint: The fix exists, but many users aren't getting it", "kurz": "The Paint app in Windows 11 has a security flaw that attackers could use to run code remotely. Microsoft already shipped a fix via the Microsoft Store on 13.10.2026. According to reports, however, many users and admins are not offered the patched version at all.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft tracks the Paint vulnerability as CVE-2026-83844 and rates it 8.1 out of 10 points. Microsoft itself classifies it as \"Important\", one level below \"Critical\". It is an out-of-bounds read that, in the worst case, allows malicious code to be executed over the network without the user having to click anything. According to Microsoft, however, an attack is difficult to pull off, and no attacks in the wild are known so far. Because Paint is updated via the Microsoft Store, the regular Windows Update alone does not protect against the flaw. According to Windows Latest, Paint is considered safe from version 11.2609.401.0, but this version did not show up in the Store even with automatic updates enabled. Admins on Reddit and in the Microsoft forum also report that they cannot get the stated version. According to Neowin, Microsoft's security page initially listed a different version number, possibly a typo. According to Neowin, a staggered rollout is also possible. The installed version can be checked in PowerShell with the command \"Get-AppxPackage Microsoft.Paint\". If you don't need Paint, you can also uninstall the app for now.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Latest: Paint flaw and missing update", "Microsoft Security Update Guide: CVE-2026-83844"], "_src": "2d5490bd"}, "2026-11-04-nova-lake-90-grad-limit": {"titel": "Leak: Intel Core Ultra 4000 \"Nova Lake-S\" said to clock at most 5.1 GHz above 90 °C", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Intel's Nova Lake said to manage only 5.1 GHz above 90 °C", "kurz": "According to leaker Jaykihn, all desktop processors of the Nova Lake-S series will limit their clock to a maximum of 5.1 GHz above 90 °C. The limit reportedly cannot be raised. The information is preliminary and not confirmed by Intel.", "zusammenfassung": "On 04.11.2026, Intel leaker Jaykihn wrote on X that Intel's upcoming Core Ultra 4000 \"Nova Lake-S\" desktop processors will get a fixed temperature limit. Above 90 °C, the maximum core clock will reportedly be capped at 5.1 GHz on all models. This is said to work independently of the usual emergency brake at 100 °C (TjMax), at which the CPU throttles anyway. According to Jaykihn, the new 90-degree limit also cannot be shifted upwards. He explicitly calls the information preliminary. Models that don't clock above 5.1 GHz anyway would not be affected by the limit. Faster models could lose part of their boost if cooling is insufficient. TechPowerUp points out that the current Core Ultra 9 285K reaches up to 5.7 GHz and has a higher TjMax of 105 °C. In addition, according to earlier reports, the 28-core flagship is said to draw up to 296 W for short periods, which would likely require a strong cooler. According to TechPowerUp, Nova Lake-S is expected in the first quarter of 2027. Intel has not confirmed the details, so it remains a leak.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: The only source is Intel leaker Jaykihn on X, who himself calls the information preliminary. VideoCardz and TechPowerUp report on the post. Intel has confirmed nothing, and final clock speeds are not known.", "ursprungsquelle": "Jaykihn (@jaykihn0) on X", "weitere_links": ["Jaykihn on X (original post)", "TechPowerUp: Nova Lake-S throttles to 5.1 GHz above 90 °C"], "_src": "434bcacb"}, "2026-11-04-god-of-war-laufey-verschoben": {"titel": "God of War Laufey delayed: New date is 20.05.2027", "schlagzeile": "God of War Laufey delayed: Fans have to wait three months longer", "kurz": "Sony Santa Monica has officially delayed God of War Laufey. Instead of 16.02.2027, the game now launches on 20.05.2027. The studio wants to use the extra time for the final polish.", "zusammenfassung": "PlayStation studio Santa Monica announced on X on 04.11.2026 that God of War Laufey will release later. It was previously planned for 16.02.2027, and the new date is 20.05.2027. The studio explains the delay by saying it wants to give the game its final polish and push it to its full potential. Since the reveal in June, the team has been grateful for the fans' great excitement, the statement says. Laufey is the first mainline game in the series in which Kratos is not the main character. Instead, players take control of Faye, Kratos's wife and Atreus's mother, who died before the events of the 2018 God of War. According to the official description, she awakens after her death in a kind of afterlife of the gods, the \"Everywhen\". Eurogamer points out that the game thereby avoids a packed February with many big releases. The studio plans to share more news soon.", "weitere_links": ["Eurogamer: God of War Laufey delayed to May 2027", "Neowin: Sony delays God of War Laufey"], "_src": "87a1ab5a"}, "2026-11-04-amd-rekord-gaming-einbruch": {"titel": "AMD: Record revenue of $13.4 billion, gaming revenue down 40 percent – likely more revenue than Intel for the first time in Q4", "schlagzeile": "AMD earns more than ever – but gaming revenue collapses by 40 %", "kurz": "AMD made a record 13.4 billion US dollars in revenue in the third quarter of 2026, mainly thanks to data centers. Gaming revenue, on the other hand, fell by 40 percent because expensive memory is slowing down graphics cards, consoles and PCs. According to its own forecast, AMD is likely to make more revenue than Intel for the first time in the fourth quarter.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD reported record revenue of 13.4 billion US dollars for the third quarter of 2026. According to ComputerBase, 8.5 billion US dollars of that came from the data center business, which according to TechPowerUp grew 97 percent year over year. Gaming looks very different: this segment plunged 40 percent compared to the same quarter last year, to 773 million US dollars. AMD cites the shortages and price increases for memory, which make graphics cards, consoles with AMD chips and complete PCs more expensive. For the fourth quarter, AMD expects around 17 billion US dollars in revenue, plus or minus three percent. Intel only expects 15 to 16 billion US dollars for the same period. Even the low end of AMD's forecast is above the high end of Intel's, so according to TechPowerUp AMD would make more revenue than Intel for the first time. This only applies to revenue, not profit. At the same time, AMD CEO Lisa Su expects a double-digit decline in PC sales for 2027. For PC gamers, this means AMD's focus keeps shifting towards data centers and AI.", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp: AMD heading for its first quarter with more revenue than Intel", "PC Games Hardware: AMD quarterly results"], "_src": "0136260f"}, "2026-11-03-arc-b580-eol": {"titel": "Leak: Intel might discontinue the Arc B580 and focus on pricier Arc Pro cards", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Intel's budget graphics card Arc B580 about to be axed?", "kurz": "According to leaker Haze2K1, Intel might phase out the Arc B580 graphics card. The reason is said to be the more profitable Arc Pro cards using the same graphics chip. This is an unconfirmed rumor, and Intel has not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "On 02.11.2026, leaker Haze2K1 wrote on X that the Intel Arc B580 might be discontinued. According to the post, Intel wants to focus more on pro and workstation cards such as the Arc Pro B50, which are said to be selling well for AI applications. TechPowerUp and Wccftech picked up the post. The Arc B580 launched in December 2024 at 249 US dollars as an affordable gaming card with 12 GB of graphics memory. According to TechPowerUp, the Arc Pro B60 uses the same graphics chip but has 24 GB of memory and costs around 500 US dollars, which likely brings more profit per chip. According to TechPowerUp, the B580 is already sold out at many retailers or only available above its original price. Haze2K1 phrases it cautiously and only says the card might be phased out. The rumor does not say whether the smaller Arc B570 would also be affected. Intel has not commented on the rumor, so it is unconfirmed.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: the only source is a post by leaker Haze2K1 on X, who himself only says “might”. TechPowerUp and Wccftech repeat the post; there is no independent second source. Intel has not commented.", "ursprungsquelle": "Haze2K1 on X", "weitere_links": ["Haze2K1 on X (original post)", "Wccftech: Intel might discontinue Arc B580"], "_src": "115ef362"}, "2026-11-03-windows11-8gb-ram": {"titel": "Windows 11 runs noticeably better on PCs with 8 GB of RAM – Microsoft gives details and requirements", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 on 8 GB PCs: up to 40% faster multitasking promised", "kurz": "Microsoft has optimized Windows 11 for PCs with only 8 GB of RAM. According to Microsoft, the system responds up to 20 percent faster, and multitasking is up to 40 percent faster in a lab test. You need Windows 11 26H2 build 26300.9818 or later and up-to-date apps.", "zusammenfassung": "On 03.11.2026, Microsoft explained on the Windows Experience Blog how Windows 11 should run better on PCs with 8 GB of RAM. According to Windows chief Pavan Davuluri, Start, Search, the context menu, Settings, Snipping Tool and File Explorer respond up to 20 percent faster on such devices, measured via telemetry data. The up to 40 percent faster multitasking time comes from a single lab test on an HP laptop with a Snapdragon X Plus, and Microsoft itself says it is not a general benchmark. Thanks to better-tuned memory compression, Windows can keep up to 2 GB more active data in RAM instead of moving it to the slower SSD. As a result, open apps and browser tabs should need to reload less often. Together with Edge and the Microsoft 365 apps, extra memory use during multitasking drops by up to 900 MB, with Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Outlook alone saving around 360 MB. On 8 GB PCs, widgets only load when you open the widgets panel, which saves about 200 MB. The requirement is Windows 11 26H2 build 26300.9818 or later, which first arrives via the optional update of 28.10.2026 and, according to Windows Latest, rolls out to everyone on Patch Tuesday, 10.11.2026. Edge, Microsoft 365 and Teams should also be up to date, because some of the improvements come through app updates. For 3D modeling, demanding video editing or large datasets, Microsoft still recommends 16 GB or more.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Experience Blog (Microsoft): Raising the bar for 8 GB Windows 11 PCs", "TechPowerUp: up to 40% faster multitasking on 8 GB PCs"], "_src": "dd699a8a"}, "2026-11-03-rtx50-preise-china": {"titel": "Leak: board partners raise GeForce RTX 50 prices in China – up to 3,300 yuan more", "schlagzeile": "Leak: RTX 50 cards reportedly getting pricier again – up to 3,300 yuan", "kurz": "According to the Chinese industry platform Channelgate, NVIDIA board partners in China are raising GeForce RTX 50 prices again. The reported increases range from about 100 to 3,300 yuan depending on the model. This is not confirmed, and the figures only apply to China.", "zusammenfassung": "The Chinese industry platform Channelgate reports that graphics card makers in China are raising GeForce RTX 50 prices again in November. According to PC Games Hardware, Colorful has reportedly already implemented the new prices, and Galax is said to follow this week. According to TechPowerUp, the reported increases range from about 100 to 150 yuan for the RTX 5060 Ti with 8 GB up to 2,200 to 3,300 yuan for the China-only RTX 5090 D V2. For the RTX 5080 the report mentions 2,500 to 2,800 yuan, for the RTX 5070 Ti around 1,000 yuan and for the RTX 5070 about 600 to 900 yuan more. Converted, that would be roughly 15 to almost 500 US dollars. The report cites tight graphics memory supply and more expensive raw materials such as copper as reasons. According to TechPowerUp, the higher prices could reach retail one to two weeks later. Because RTX 50 cards are getting scarce in China, retailers are reportedly turning more to older models like the RTX 3060 and to Radeon cards, according to PCGH. NVIDIA and the named board partners have not officially confirmed the increases. Whether and how much this affects prices in Europe is unclear.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: all reports are based on the Chinese industry platform Channelgate (Board Channels circle). NVIDIA, Colorful and Galax have not confirmed anything officially. The prices apply to China and cannot be transferred 1:1 to Europe.", "ursprungsquelle": "Channelgate (Board Channels), China", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp: RTX 50 set for price hike of up to 500 US dollars"], "_src": "1fa9041b"}, "2026-11-03-elder-scrolls-6-sentinel": {"titel": "The Elder Scrolls 6 is officially called “Sentinel” – Bethesda reveals title and logo", "schlagzeile": "After 8 years of silence: The Elder Scrolls 6 finally has a name", "kurz": "For its 40th anniversary, Bethesda revealed the full title of the next Elder Scrolls role-playing game: The Elder Scrolls VI: Sentinel. Sentinel is a city in the region of Hammerfell. There is still no release date.", "zusammenfassung": "On 03.11.2026, in a video celebrating the studio's 40th anniversary, Bethesda officially confirmed that The Elder Scrolls VI carries the subtitle “Sentinel”. The video shows the title and logo, and Todd Howard also speaks in it. Sentinel is a port city in the province of Hammerfell in the northwest of Tamriel. According to IGN, a quote in the video is dated to a time after the events of Skyrim. The game was first announced at E3 2018, and there has been little official information since then. A report had already predicted the name the week before, and now it is confirmed. Bethesda did not show a release date or gameplay. According to IGN, the platforms are Xbox and PC, while a PlayStation release remains open. Eurogamer speculates that more could be shown at The Game Awards in December, but that is not confirmed.", "weitere_links": ["IGN Germany: The Elder Scrolls 6 is called Sentinel", "PC Gamer: The Elder Scrolls 6: Sentinel is official"], "_src": "0e2f52ba"}, "2026-11-03-gta6-preload-212gb": {"titel": "GTA 6: Rockstar confirms pre-load from 10.11.2026 and a download of up to 212 GB", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 eats up to 212 GB – and the pre-load starts earlier than expected", "kurz": "Rockstar Games has officially confirmed that the GTA 6 pre-download on PS5 and Xbox Series X|S begins on 10.11.2026. Depending on the console, the download is up to 212 GB. The game is still set to launch on 19.11.2026.", "zusammenfassung": "On the afternoon of 03.11.2026, Rockstar Games published the details of the Grand Theft Auto VI pre-download. On PS5, the pre-load starts on 10.11.2026 at midnight local time, on Xbox Series X|S on the same day at 0:00 GMT, which is 1 a.m. in Austria and Germany. According to Rockstar, the download is up to 212 GB depending on the device, and the PlayStation Blog also advises freeing up at least 212 GB of storage. This largely confirms a leak from late October that said the game would take up around 210 GB on PS5. According to the reports, the pre-load had originally been announced for 12.11.2026, so digital players can now start two days earlier. The boxed versions are due in stores on 12.11.2026 and, according to the reports, only contain a download code. The release stays on 19.11.2026 for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. At launch, Rockstar also plans to offer a printable cover poster and a map of Leonida on its website. The information does not clearly say whether the Xbox Series S needs less storage space.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation Blog: pre-download starts on November 10", "IGN Germany: pre-load times and install size confirmed", "VGC: Rockstar details pre-load date and file size"], "_src": "91689255"}, "2026-11-03-fedora-45": {"titel": "Fedora Linux 45 is out – with GNOME 51, KDE Plasma 6.8 and Linux kernel 7.2", "schlagzeile": "Fedora 45 is here: new desktop, new installer and verifiable builds", "kurz": "The Fedora Project has released Fedora Linux 45. The Workstation edition uses GNOME 51, the KDE edition Plasma 6.8, running on Linux kernel 7.2. New features include Stratis in the installer and reproducible package builds.", "zusammenfassung": "Fedora Linux 45 was released on 03.11.2026, about six months after Fedora 44 and, according to Phoronix, after two delays. The Workstation edition ships with GNOME 51, the KDE Plasma Desktop edition with Plasma 6.8. Linux 7.2 is used as the kernel. According to the official Fedora Magazine, one of the biggest new features is support for the Stratis storage system directly in the Anaconda installer. KMSCON now handles the virtual text console by default, and according to 9to5Linux Fedora relies on fully reproducible package builds. Signature checking for RPM packages is enabled by default and ptrace is restricted by default, which is meant to improve security. The Atomic variants such as Silverblue and Kinoite now install via the new WebUI installer. For developers, GCC 16.2, LLVM 23, Python 3.15, Go 1.27 and Podman 6 are among the included tools. The old VPN plugins NetworkManager-vpnc and NetworkManager-fortisslvpn are dropped, so anyone using them should migrate their connections before upgrading. Existing Fedora 44 installations can be upgraded via DNF system-upgrade.", "weitere_links": ["Fedora Magazine (official): Announcing Fedora Linux 45", "Phoronix: Fedora 45 Released"], "_src": "be19dcc2"}, "2026-11-02-zelda-oot-remake-puppenlook": {"titel": "Zelda: Ocarina of Time for Switch 2: Nintendo explains the remake's controversial puppet look", "schlagzeile": "The Zelda remake looks like a puppet show – Nintendo explains why", "kurz": "The remake of The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time launches on November 5 for Nintendo Switch 2. Its art style with puppet-like characters divides fans. In an interview, the developers explain that they deliberately wanted a “puppet-show feel” instead of pure photorealism.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Polygon, Nintendo has commented on the controversial art style of the remake of The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time. Link, Zelda and other characters look more like puppets than photorealistic people, which has sparked debate among longtime fans. Art director Aya Shida says in a developer interview that the goal was not simply to make everything look realistic. Hyrule was meant to feel like a dense world that could truly exist, while the colorful, quirky characters provide a contrast to it, just like in the original. According to Shida, the team's guiding keywords were a “puppet-show feel” and “the analog feel of practical effects films”. Series producer Eiji Aonuma explains that the team feels nostalgic when looking back at the Nintendo 64 original, and expressing that nostalgia led to the analog puppet look. According to Video Games Chronicle, the remake launches on Thursday, November 5, 2026, for Nintendo Switch 2. It is being developed by Nintendo's own division Nintendo EPD, which also made Breath of the Wild and Tears of the Kingdom. Whether the style convinces in the end will only become clear with the reviews after launch.", "weitere_links": ["Video Games Chronicle: Zelda: Ocarina of Time UK midnight launch"], "_src": "dda2e7e2"}, "2026-11-02-rtx5080-preis-heise": {"titel": "RTX 5080 barely available under 2,000 euros, report: 24 GB version could be delayed", "schlagzeile": "RTX 5080 breaks 2,000 euros: over 30% more expensive in just two weeks", "kurz": "According to heise online, the GeForce RTX 5080 can currently barely be found under 2,000 euros; its price has risen by more than 30 percent in two weeks. heise cites the rumors about the RTX 5090 being discontinued as the reason; that card now costs around 8,000 euros. According to an unconfirmed report by BenchLife, the expected 24 GB version of the RTX 5080 could be delayed.", "zusammenfassung": "After the RTX 5090, the RTX 5080 is now also becoming much more expensive, according to heise online: NVIDIA's second-fastest gaming graphics card is currently barely available under 2,000 euros. That is more than 30 percent more than just two weeks ago. In mid-October, rumors emerged that NVIDIA might take the RTX 5090 off the market, which according to heise fueled demand for the 5080. The RTX 5090 itself now costs around 8,000 euros; NVIDIA's last MSRP was 2,099 euros. NVIDIA denied that the 5090 is being discontinued, but only with the wording that the card will “continue to ship”. According to heise, this does not make clear whether it will continue to be manufactured. In October, there were also reports that an RTX 5080 with 24 instead of 16 GB of GDDR7 would be unveiled in January 2027. According to the Taiwanese site BenchLife, however, board partners have not yet received the necessary design documents from NVIDIA, even though they were reportedly planned for October. This is an unconfirmed report; NVIDIA has not commented on it. In addition, the stock of GB203 chips in China is said to be already sold and to last only one to two more months. heise names the AI boom as the cause of the shortage: the same chips and the scarce GDDR7 memory are also used in expensive workstation cards with higher margins. Anyone looking for a high-end card should therefore expect prices to stay high for now.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech: RTX 5080 24 GB may miss January 2027 launch"], "_src": "ecd4a72d"}, "2026-11-02-windows11-smart-app-control-fix": {"titel": "Microsoft fixes bug: Smart App Control could no longer be turned on after the October update", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11: protection feature grayed out after October update – fix is here", "kurz": "After the October security update KB5127648, the Windows 11 protection feature Smart App Control could no longer be turned on on some PCs. Microsoft fixed the bug with the updates from October 28, 2026 onward, including the optional preview update KB5127936. Where Smart App Control was already active, protection remained in place the whole time.", "zusammenfassung": "According to BleepingComputer, Microsoft has fixed a known bug in Windows 11 that appeared after the October 2026 security update KB5127648. On affected devices running Windows 11 24H2 and later, the Smart App Control option in Windows Security was grayed out and could not be turned on. Smart App Control works together with SmartScreen and Microsoft Defender to block potentially harmful apps. Only PCs on which the feature had previously been turned off were affected. Where it was already active, the devices remained protected, according to Microsoft. The bug is fixed with the Windows updates from October 28, 2026 and later, including the optional preview update KB5127936. Microsoft recommends installing the latest update. For company PCs that don't want to wait for the next Patch Tuesday, Microsoft provides a workaround via two registry entries or special Group Policies, each requiring a restart. According to BleepingComputer, KB5127936 also fixes Remote Desktop problems when “Administrator protection” is enabled and VPN errors after the September 2026 updates. Home users don't need to do anything except install the update.", "_src": "2c58e168"}, "2026-11-02-raspberry-pi5-16gb-preis": {"titel": "Raspberry Pi 5 with 16 GB RAM gets more expensive for the fourth time: 385 instead of 305 US dollars", "schlagzeile": "Raspberry Pi 5 with 16 GB now costs $385 – three times its launch price", "kurz": "Raspberry Pi is raising the list price of the Raspberry Pi 5 with 16 GB of RAM from 305 to 385 US dollars. It is the fourth increase since December 2025; at launch the price was 120 US dollars. The reason is rising RAM prices, but the Raspberry Pi 500+ is not getting more expensive this time.", "zusammenfassung": "According to heise online, the Raspberry Pi 5 with 16 GB of LPDDR4 RAM is getting more expensive again. The list price rises by 80 to 385 US dollars. It is already the fourth increase after December 2025, February 2026 and April 2026. At launch, this version cost 120 US dollars or around 135 euros, according to heise. The manufacturer cites constantly rising RAM prices as the reason. Raspberry Pi CEO Eben Upton explains that there is no alternative supplier for the 16 GB memory chip. The same chip is also used in the Compute Module 5 and the Raspberry Pi 500+. The 16 GB version of the Compute Module 5 becomes 40 US dollars more expensive, while the Raspberry Pi 500+ does not this time. According to heise, some other Raspberry Pi models are also getting more expensive. Because of the shortages, the manufacturer has introduced additional assembly options for several products so that memory chips from other manufacturers can be used. Golem.de reports that a Pi 5 now costs almost 350 euros. How much prices rise in stores depends on the retailer.", "weitere_links": ["Golem.de: Pi 5 und Compute Module – Raspberry Pi kostet mittlerweile fast 350 Euro"], "_src": "7815dfa5"}, "2026-11-02-rtx5090-pro5500-igorslab": {"titel": "RTX 5090 vs. RTX PRO 5500: igor'sLAB examines whether NVIDIA's pro card is taking chips away from the gaming GPU", "schlagzeile": "Over €8,000 for an RTX 5090: Is NVIDIA's pro card stealing its chips?", "kurz": "According to igor'sLAB, an RTX 5090 available for immediate delivery cost €8,059 at a German retailer on 1 November 2026, while the Founders Edition MSRP is €2,099. The analysis examines whether NVIDIA prefers to put suitable GB202 chips into the upcoming RTX PRO 5500 pro card, which has the same number of compute units. The verdict: economically plausible, but not publicly proven.", "zusammenfassung": "igor'sLAB has looked into why the GeForce RTX 5090 is hardly available at its original price anymore. In a retailer sample from 1 November 2026, an INNO3D RTX 5090 iCHILL X3 available for immediate delivery cost €8,059 at ALTERNATE, and a ZOTAC Solid OC White cost €8,499 at Caseking. The German MSRP of the Founders Edition is €2,099, but the Founders Edition is listed as unavailable there. The focus is on the upcoming RTX PRO 5500 Blackwell Workstation Edition: according to partner listings, it also uses the large GB202 chip with 170 active streaming multiprocessors and 21,760 CUDA cores, but has 84 GB of GDDR7 with ECC instead of 32 GB. Citing anonymous sources, Reuters reported on 20 October 2026 that more than three million PRO 5500 cards had been ordered from China at around $11,400 each. That would give NVIDIA an incentive to put suitable chips into the expensive pro card rather than the gaming card. However, igor'sLAB stresses that this has not been publicly proven: there is no data on chip yields or on how chips are split between the two products. In addition, supply of gaming cards was already tight before the reported PRO 5500 orders, and regular deliveries of the pro card are only expected to start in the first quarter of 2027. The analysis names GDDR7 memory as a further bottleneck, which according to TrendForce is increasingly being allocated to AI and server applications. The cost and margin examples in the article are explicitly based on freely chosen assumptions and are not real NVIDIA figures. The igor'sLAB verdict: the pro card is a serious competitor for chips and memory, but a measurable displacement of the RTX 5090 has not been proven.", "_src": "bff68b5d"}, "2026-11-01-linux-7-4-rc1": {"titel": "Linux 7.4-rc1 released: Largest merge window in kernel history, much of it triggered by AI", "schlagzeile": "Linux 7.4: Record update thanks to an AI flood – and Torvalds likes it", "kurz": "Linus Torvalds has released the first test version of Linux 7.4. With almost 20,000 commits, the merge window was the largest in kernel history, and a large part of it was triggered by AI tools. New features include preparations for AMD's Zen 6 processors and HDMI 2.1 enabled by default in the AMDGPU driver.", "zusammenfassung": "Linus Torvalds released Linux 7.4-rc1 on Sunday evening, closing the merge window on schedule. According to Torvalds, it was unusually large with almost 20,000 commits instead of the usual 15,000 or so, and according to Phoronix the largest in kernel history. Torvalds names the flood of AI-triggered changes as the main reason. He sees it positively: he would much rather have this work land in the merge window than as a wave of fixes during the test phase. According to Torvalds, another reason could be that Linux 7.4 is expected to become the next long-term support version. In his words, a third of the patch consists of AMD GPU register definitions alone. According to Phoronix, the new features include support for upcoming Ryzen processors with Zen 6, HDMI 2.1 enabled by default in the AMDGPU driver and the AMD PerfOpt feature for better AI performance on Radeon iGPUs. There is also Intel IPU8 support for upcoming Nova Lake laptops, more support for Snapdragon X2 laptops, initial groundwork for Apple's M4 (not yet ready for everyday use) and faster kernel builds. Several test versions will now follow before the final release. If everything goes to plan, Linux 7.4 will be released on 20 December 2026, according to Phoronix. Regular users are best off waiting until their distribution ships the new kernel.", "weitere_links": ["LWN.net: Kernel prepatch 7.4-rc1"], "_src": "4f089b1b"}, "2026-11-01-gta6-210gb-download": {"titel": "GTA 6: 210 GB download size for PS5 surfaces", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Does GTA 6 really need a whopping 210 GB on PS5?", "kurz": "According to the data account PlayStation Game Size, the PS5 download of GTA 6 is said to be around 210 GB, and Insider Gaming says it can corroborate this. Rockstar has not officially stated a size, so the figure is unconfirmed. What is certain: digital pre-orders can pre-load from 12 November 2026, and the game launches on 19 November 2026.", "zusammenfassung": "The X account PlayStation Game Size (@PlaystationSize), which specialises in store data, named a download size of 210 GB for the standard edition of Grand Theft Auto VI on PlayStation on 27 October 2026. Insider Gaming reported on it on 1 November 2026 and writes that it can corroborate the figure. According to Insider Gaming, that would make GTA 6 one of the largest games ever. Rockstar Games and Take-Two have not officially confirmed the size, so the figure is considered unconfirmed. Insider Gaming also points out that the size may still change before launch and that a day-one patch could take up additional storage. The source gives no figure for the Xbox version. The dates, on the other hand, are officially confirmed: according to Rockstar, digital pre-orders can pre-load from 12 November 2026, and the game launches on 19 November 2026 for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S. According to Rockstar, the boxed version only contains a download code and is also available from 12 November 2026. According to Rockstar, the standard edition costs $79.99 and the Ultimate Edition $99.99. Anyone who wants to play at launch should plan plenty of free space on their console in good time.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Comes from the data account @PlaystationSize (analyses store data); Insider Gaming says it can corroborate the figure. Not officially confirmed by Rockstar or Take-Two; the size may change before launch and through a day-one patch.", "ursprungsquelle": "PlayStation Game Size (@PlaystationSize) on X, 27 October 2026", "weitere_links": ["Take-Two/Rockstar: pre-orders, pre-load from 12 November 2026, launch 19 November 2026 (official)"], "_src": "386ea700"}, "2026-11-01-windows11-26h2-alle": {"titel": "Windows 11 26H2 now available for all eligible PCs, including directly from Windows 10", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 26H2 is now available to everyone – including Windows 10 PCs", "kurz": "Microsoft has completed the phased rollout of Windows 11 26H2: according to Microsoft, the update has been available for all eligible devices since 28 October 2026. According to Neowin, it is now also offered directly via Windows Update to compatible Windows 10 PCs. The requirement remains that the PC meets the hardware requirements of Windows 11.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft made Windows 11 26H2 generally available at the end of September 2026, but rolled it out in phases as usual. This is meant to prevent major problems from hitting many devices at once, which matters especially for businesses. According to Neowin, the rollout first reached full availability for devices running Windows 11 25H2 and 24H2. Microsoft now writes that, as of 28 October 2026, Windows 11 26H2 is available for all eligible devices. According to Neowin, this also applies to compatible Windows 10 PCs, which are now offered the update directly via Windows Update. The outlet says it observed this on one of its own Windows 10 machines. Anyone already on Windows 11 24H2 or 25H2 who has not yet been offered the update can manually install the eKB5121794 enablement package, according to Neowin. However, this does not work from Windows 10 or older Windows 11 versions. For a clean install, current ISO files are available via Microsoft's Media Creation Tool. According to Neowin, 26H2 needs less RAM and feels snappier, though that is the outlet's own assessment. One catch remains: only PCs that meet the hardware requirements of Windows 11 get the offer.", "_src": "7b79cfea"}, "2026-11-01-rtx2080ti-22gb-pcgh": {"titel": "Used RTX 2080 Ti with 22 GB: PCGH tests the memory mod from China", "schlagzeile": "22 GB on an old RTX 2080 Ti: how good is the China mod really?", "kurz": "PC Games Hardware tested an RTX 2080 Ti whose video memory was doubled from 11 to 22 GB in China. At 1440p the difference is usually small, but in 4K and AI workloads the modded card clearly beats the original. There is no warranty for a conversion like this.", "zusammenfassung": "PC Games Hardware tested a modified GeForce RTX 2080 Ti with doubled video memory that a reader had bought via Alibaba. Instead of 11 GB, the board carries eleven 2 GB Samsung chips, i.e. 22 GB of GDDR6 on the unchanged 352-bit interface with 616 GB/s. A changed strap resistor lets the card run without a modified BIOS and with normal drivers. At 1440p with DLSS Quality, the differences to the 11 GB version are mostly small, but frame times are more even. In Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024 and Spider-Man 2, the original card was around 20 percent behind according to the test. In 4K with DLSS Performance and FSR Frame Generation, the 11 GB card stuttered heavily, and Indiana Jones even crashed. Memory usage of up to 13.9 GB was measured in Spider-Man 2. In the AI test with ComfyUI, the 22 GB card needed about 315 seconds instead of around 540 seconds – an RTX 5070 Ti did the same in about 85 seconds. For buyers of used hardware this means: the mod can be worth it, but it is a modification without manufacturer warranty, and the quality of such conversions varies.", "weitere_links": ["PCGH test (original)"], "_src": "03eb821d"}, "2026-11-01-larrabee-fund": {"titel": "Complete Intel Larrabee developer system discovered in storage unit", "schlagzeile": "Storage unit find: unreleased Intel GPU discovered along with developer PC", "kurz": "A Reddit user discovered a complete developer system for Intel's Larrabee GPU, which never came to market, in a storage unit bought at auction. The PC boots Windows 7 and is even said to run Crysis, although the FPS figures have not been independently verified. The original software is now on the Internet Archive.", "zusammenfassung": "A Reddit user found a complete development system for Intel's never-released Larrabee GPU when a storage unit was auctioned off. The PC contains an Intel DX58SO motherboard with a C0-stepping engineering sample referred to as 'Intel Visual Adrenaline'. It came with two USB sticks containing the original software, which the finder has since uploaded to the Internet Archive. The system boots Windows 7 and supports Direct3D. According to the owner, Crysis ran at 720p on medium details at about 17 FPS, and allegedly at around 36 FPS with a different driver – these figures have not been independently verified. Intel cancelled Larrabee as a graphics card in 2010; the technology later lived on in the Xeon Phi accelerators. For hardware collectors, a complete system like this with software is a real rarity.", "_src": "e8e20545"}, "2026-10-31-nv-uefi-unlocker": {"titel": "Open-source tool unlocks more AI performance on RTX 20, 30 and 40", "schlagzeile": "Free tool gets up to 75% more AI performance from RTX cards – with a catch", "kurz": "The open-source tool “nv-uefi-unlocker” unlocks throttled compute units for AI workloads on RTX 20, 30 and 40 cards. In the reported tests, performance rose by around 29 to 75 percent depending on card and task. No benefit for games has been shown, Secure Boot must be off, and you use it at your own risk.", "zusammenfassung": "Developer physicsdolphin has released 'nv-uefi-unlocker', an open-source tool meant to unlock throttled compute units on GeForce cards for AI workloads. The tool boots from a USB stick before the actual driver and then also works under Windows. The change is not permanent and has to be reapplied after every cold boot. RTX 20, 30 and 40 are supported, GTX 16 only experimentally, RTX 50 not at all. Secure Boot must be disabled, and Turing cards also need GSP firmware. Reported results: an RTX 2070 gained 67 to 75 percent in FP32 GEMM, and an RTX 4060 laptop GPU rose from 29.89 to 49.33 TFLOPS in FP16. A user with an RTX 3080 LHR reported about 29 percent more speed in ComfyUI with SDXL, while the tool brings little for text generation with LLMs. Anyone who tries this does so at their own risk – no benefit for gaming performance has been shown.", "_src": "111abea6"}, "2026-10-31-amd-adrenalin-26-10-2": {"titel": "AMD Adrenalin 26.10.2: Optional Radeon driver fixes ten bugs, several issues remain open", "schlagzeile": "Radeon crashes: AMD's new driver fixes ten bugs – but not all of them", "kurz": "AMD has released the optional Adrenalin 26.10.2 graphics driver, which fixes ten bugs, including driver timeouts, crashes and system shutdowns on Radeon RX 7000 and RX 9000. It does not add support for new games. Several known issues, for example in Cyberpunk 2077 and Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced, remain open.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD released the optional Adrenalin Edition 26.10.2 graphics driver for Windows on 30 October 2026. According to the official release notes, it is a pure bug-fix update with ten fixes. Among other things, it fixes crashes or driver timeouts when other overlays such as the Xbox Game Bar are opened or closed while AMD's performance overlay is active. The Steam client also sometimes crashed on launch on Radeon cards, which should now be fixed. On the RX 7600, the driver fixes system shutdowns in Valor Mortis, and on the rest of the RX 7000 series driver timeouts in the same game. For the RX 9000 series, AMD fixes hangs in Death Stranding 2 with FSR enabled and crashes when switching between applications with FSR Frame Generation. There are also fixes for video playback on Windows 11 with hardware-accelerated GPU scheduling (HAGS) and a bug in the AMD Install Manager. Not everything is solved: in Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced, crashes can still occur on the RX 7000, and in War Thunder timeouts on the RX 5000. For War Thunder, AMD recommends the older 26.9.1 driver for now. In Cyberpunk 2077, some RX 9000 cards can crash when FSR upscaling, Anti-Lag and frame generation are active while a video plays on a second display; AMD then recommends turning off the in-game frame generation. According to AMD, Smart Access Memory may also be disabled after installation on Windows 10, so it is worth checking in the driver if in doubt. If you don't have any of the fixed problems, there's no need to install the optional driver right away.", "weitere_links": ["AMD: Release notes Adrenalin Edition 26.10.2 (official)"], "_src": "f1d0f566"}, "2026-10-31-altman-pc-ram": {"titel": "Sam Altman: PC RAM is a 'quite terrible' use of scarce DRAM capacity", "schlagzeile": "Sam Altman: the RAM in your PC is “quite terrible” use of memory", "kurz": "On the “Cheeky Pint” podcast, OpenAI CEO Sam Altman called it “quite terrible” that DRAM sits in PCs which, by his rough estimate, run only about five percent of the time. The background is the memory shortage, as manufacturers produce more and more server and AI memory. For PC builders this means RAM is unlikely to get cheaper any time soon.", "zusammenfassung": "OpenAI CEO Sam Altman talked about the current memory shortage on the 'Cheeky Pint' podcast with Stripe co-founder John Collison. He called it 'quite terrible' that DRAM sits in PCs that are only used about five percent of the time. The five percent is his own rough estimate, not a verified figure. The background is that memory manufacturers are increasingly shifting production to server and AI memory, which drives up prices for consumer RAM. VideoCardz clearly disagrees with Altman in its commentary. For PC builders, the statement is above all a sign that RAM prices are unlikely to fall again any time soon.", "_src": "be0c42aa"}, "2026-10-30-linux-kernel-tcp-luecke": {"titel": "Linux kernel: severe flaw in TCP code enables remote root attacks on MPTCP servers", "schlagzeile": "Linux: kernel flaw allows remote root access – update now", "kurz": "A use-after-free flaw in the Linux kernel's IPv4 TCP code (CVE-2026-98432) affects kernels as far back as version 4.4. Researchers have demonstrated remote root access on servers that offer Multipath TCP (MPTCP). Debian already has updates, other distributions are following.", "zusammenfassung": "According to BleepingComputer, the IPv4 TCP code of the Linux kernel contains a use-after-free flaw caused by a race condition (CVE-2026-98432). Kernels as far back as version 4.4 are affected. The kernel's CVE team rates the flaw 9.8 out of 10, while Red Hat rates it only 5.9 because exploitation is complex and crashes are the main risk. Researchers from Anthropic demonstrated remote root access on servers with an MPTCP listener; according to the report, an unreleased Claude model created the exploit in around 53 minutes. Regular TCP is also affected, but code execution has not been shown there. Attacks in the wild have not been confirmed. Tricky: programs built with Go 1.24 or later enable MPTCP on Linux by default. The Go security team nevertheless recommends a kernel update rather than disabling MPTCP per program, and according to the report, simply disabling MPTCP is not enough anyway. Debian has released fixed kernels for Bookworm and Trixie; for Ubuntu, updates were in progress on 30 October. RHEL 8 to 10 are affected; SUSE, Oracle and Amazon Linux had some updates at that time. The flaw is fixed in kernel versions 6.1.190, 6.6.159, 6.12.113, 6.18.56 and 7.3, among others. Anyone running Linux servers should update the kernel promptly and reboot.", "weitere_links": ["oss-security: notice from the Go security team on MPTCP", "LWN.net: new stable kernels"], "_src": "d946d2fe"}, "2026-10-30-windows-insider-suche": {"titel": "Windows Insider builds: new search with sliders and phone actions, Beta sets app permissions individually", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 tests new search with sliders and phone actions", "kurz": "In new Insider builds, Microsoft is testing a revamped Windows search. It shows sliders, for example for volume and brightness, directly in the results and can start calls or text messages via Phone Link. Beta build 26220.9836 also allows camera, microphone and location permissions per desktop app.", "zusammenfassung": "On 30 October, Microsoft released new Windows 11 Insider builds, including Beta 26220.9836 and Experimental 26340.9843. A new Windows search is starting in the Experimental channels. It shows sliders for volume, brightness or mouse pointer size directly in the results. Phone Link is meant to control calls, text messages and “Do not disturb” on the phone – initially with Android, with iPhone support due early next year. There are also more detailed results with file previews, web answers such as weather and stocks, and apps from the Store; this can be turned off under Privacy & security > Search. Results can be filtered and rated with thumbs up or down. For now, the search opens at the bottom centre; according to Microsoft, adapting it to the taskbar position is in the works. According to Windows Report, the Beta build also brings camera, microphone and location permissions for individual desktop apps, with previous decisions kept. As with all Insider features, it is unclear whether and when they will reach the regular version of Windows.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Report: Beta build 26220.9836 with per-app permissions"], "_src": "bbfec2ce"}, "2026-10-30-nova-lake-28c-prognose": {"titel": "Nova Lake-S with 28 cores: internal projection cites 16 to 33% more gaming performance", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Intel's next gaming CPU said to be up to 33% faster", "kurz": "According to VideoCardz, internal Intel projections promise 16 to 33 percent more gaming performance for Nova Lake-S than the Core Ultra 9 285K, depending on the variant. However, part of the lead comes from the faster DDR5-8000 memory used in the comparison. These are unconfirmed target values that may still change before launch.", "zusammenfassung": "According to VideoCardz, internal Intel projections from August 2026 show how much faster Nova Lake-S is supposed to be in games. The basis is Intel's own 'Gaming Index', compared against the Core Ultra 9 285K. A 28-core variant with a 285 W PL1 is said to be up to 1.16 times as fast as the 285K at 250 W. A variant with two compute tiles and 296 W is said to be up to 1.33 times as fast. Important: Nova Lake ran with DDR5-8000 via XMP, Arrow Lake only with DDR5-6400 – so part of the lead comes from the faster memory. Further claims by X user Haze, such as +8 percent single-thread without and +17 percent with a large last-level cache, have not been verified according to VideoCardz. Such early projections are target values and may still change before launch. Officially, Intel has so far only confirmed that Nova Lake is based on the 18A-P process and that more details will follow at CES in January.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Alleged internal Intel slides shared via third parties; not independently verified, targets may have changed.", "ursprungsquelle": "Haze (@Haze2K1) / alleged Intel slides", "_src": "6e13f4ff"}, "2026-10-30-rtx5080-marketplace": {"titel": "RTX 5080 disappears from NVIDIA's US store – after the RTX 5090", "schlagzeile": "First the RTX 5090, now the RTX 5080: NVIDIA's US store is emptying", "kurz": "The GeForce RTX 5080 has disappeared from NVIDIA's official marketplace in the US, a good two weeks after the RTX 5090. At US retailers, the cheapest RTX 5080 costs about twice its MSRP of 999 dollars. This does not prove an end of production, but supply is visibly tight.", "zusammenfassung": "The GeForce RTX 5080 has disappeared from NVIDIA's official marketplace in the US; Reddit users first noticed it in the filter list. The RTX 5090 had already been removed on 16 October, briefly reappeared at 5,599 US dollars and disappeared again – its MSRP is 1,999 dollars. On 28 October, the cheapest RTX 5080 cost 1,979.99 dollars at US retailers and 1,999.99 dollars at Best Buy, against an MSRP of 999 dollars. NVIDIA had previously denied that the RTX 5090 was discontinued. All cards in the RTX 50 series are currently selling well above MSRP. A card being dropped from the store does not by itself prove an end of production – but it does show how tight supply is.", "_src": "99a9c410"}, "2026-10-30-witcher4-sprecher": {"titel": "The Witcher 4: voice actors' statements fuel rumours about familiar characters", "schlagzeile": "Leak: are Dandelion and Yennefer returning in The Witcher 4?", "kurz": "Several voice actors have commented on The Witcher 4, sparking speculation about familiar characters. Dandelion's Polish voice actor says he has recorded a few lines, while Geralt's voice actor Doug Cockle has not recorded anything yet. CD Projekt RED has not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "According to ixbt.games, Geralt's voice actor Doug Cockle said on the Kinda Funny Games podcast in late October that he has not yet recorded anything for The Witcher 4 and does not know the scope of Geralt's role. He expects a supporting role rather than a lead. According to VGTimes, Jacek Kopczyński, the Polish voice of Dandelion, said at the PSX Extreme Party on 5 September that he has already recorded a few lines for The Witcher 4 – “not much”. For the also-announced project “Songs of the Past”, however, he has not recorded anything yet. According to Notebookcheck, a Reddit user reported that Yennefer's voice actress Denise Gough said at a signing session that she had recorded new dialogue involving Ciri; it is unclear for which project. In 2025, Gough had told Eurogamer that her involvement in The Witcher 4 was uncertain. CD Projekt RED has not commented on any of these statements. Officially confirmed: Ciri is the main character, and the game is coming to PC, PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. In August, co-CEO Michał Nowakowski named 2028 as the targeted release window. CD Projekt will present its next quarterly results on 24 November.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Statements by voice actors, partly only second-hand (Reddit, event reports) and partly unclear which project they recorded for; CD Projekt RED has confirmed nothing.", "ursprungsquelle": "Statements by the voice actors (Kinda Funny Games podcast, PSX Extreme Party 2026, signing session according to a Reddit user)", "weitere_links": ["VGTimes: Dandelion's voice actor has recorded lines for The Witcher 4", "Notebookcheck: Witcher 4 leak hints at return of popular character"], "_src": "9d06ea0f"}, "2026-10-30-amd-preiserhoehung": {"titel": "AMD reportedly raising Radeon and GDDR6 prices again in November", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Radeon cards could get more expensive again as soon as November", "kurz": "According to the Chinese retailer forum Board Channels, AMD raised Radeon wholesale prices in October and could follow up in November. Separately, graphics card prices rose by around 35 percent in three months according to Hardware Unboxed. AMD has not confirmed the planned increase.", "zusammenfassung": "According to information from the Chinese retailer forum Board Channels, AMD raised wholesale prices for Radeon GPUs on 1 October and could follow up in November. AMD reportedly reviews its prices quarterly. GDDR6 memory also became about 8 to 10 percent more expensive in the third quarter. Separately, Hardware Unboxed recorded graphics card prices in ten countries: over three months they rose by around 35 percent, by 10 percent in October alone. According to the data, the RX 9060 XT 16GB became 17 percent more expensive, and the RX 9070 and RX 9070 XT about 12 percent each. AMD has not confirmed the planned increase. Anyone who needs a graphics card should keep an eye on prices – the used market is likely to be affected too.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Retailer forum Board Channels; Hardware Unboxed's price data is documented, the planned AMD increase is not.", "ursprungsquelle": "Board Channels", "_src": "61551511"}, "2026-10-30-intel-q3-nova-lake-18a-p": {"titel": "Intel quarterly results: Nova Lake on 18A-P ahead of schedule, details at CES", "schlagzeile": "Intel steps on the gas: Nova Lake is ahead of schedule", "kurz": "On its third-quarter earnings call, Intel confirmed that Nova Lake will be the first client product on the 18A-P process and that development is ahead of schedule. Details are to follow at CES in January. However, Intel sees the PC market in a correction because of high memory prices.", "zusammenfassung": "On its earnings call for the third quarter of 2026 (29 October, US time), Intel confirmed that Nova Lake will be the first client product on the 18A-P process. Development is ahead of schedule, and Intel expects twice as many design wins as with Panther Lake. More details are to follow at CES in January. According to Intel, 18A yields are improving by double-digit percentages, and 18A-P is on track by the end of the year. At the same power, 18A-P is said to deliver about 9 percent more clock speed, or around 18 percent lower power at the same clock. For 14A, PDK 0.9 was released in October, version 1.0 follows in the first quarter of 2027, and production is planned for 2028. On the server side, Diamond Rapids arrives in 2027 on 18A-P and Coral Rapids in 2028 on 14A. Intel, however, sees the PC market in a correction until memory prices normalise – it expects the overall market to be around 10 percent smaller. According to Tom's Hardware, Intel is also taking Panther Lake capacity offline to build more Granite Rapids server CPUs.", "datum_hinweis": "Time estimated (published on the morning of 30 Oct)", "weitere_links": ["Transcript (The Motley Fool)", "Notes by harukaze5719 on X"], "_src": "728b9684"}, "2026-10-30-rtx5080-24gb": {"titel": "RTX 5080 with 24 GB said to arrive by January 2027 and replace the 16 GB version", "schlagzeile": "Leak: RTX 5080 with 24 GB said to arrive around the turn of the year", "kurz": "According to Board Channels, NVIDIA is planning a GeForce RTX 5080 with 24 instead of 16 GB, launching first in China between December 2026 and January 2027. The 16 GB version is to be phased out there. Name, clock speeds and price are unknown, and NVIDIA has confirmed nothing.", "zusammenfassung": "According to a report from the Chinese retailer forum Board Channels (ChannelGate), NVIDIA is planning a GeForce RTX 5080 with 24 GB of memory. It is to launch in China in December 2026 at the earliest and January 2027 at the latest. The current 16 GB version and the RTX 5090 D V2 are to be phased out there; the remaining stock of 16 GB GPUs is said to last about two more months. BenchLife had already reported a launch in the first quarter of 2027 on 12 October, but board partners had reportedly only received verbal hints. The 50 percent more memory would likely come from 3 GB GDDR7 modules on the same interface. Name, clock speeds and price are unknown. In early October, the X accounts hongxing2020 and MEGAsizeGPU had also speculated about the end of the 16 GB variant and of GB202 shipments for the RTX 5090, respectively. NVIDIA has confirmed none of this.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Retailer forum Board Channels (China) plus BenchLife; several sources, but no NVIDIA confirmation.", "ursprungsquelle": "Board Channels / BenchLife", "weitere_links": ["harukaze5719 on X", "hongxing2020 on X (10 Oct)", "MEGAsizeGPU on X (10 Oct)"], "_src": "60b93d53"}, "2026-10-29-windows11-kb5127936": {"titel": "Windows 11: optional update KB5127936 brings new context menu and cloud reinstall", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11: preview update brings new context menu and cloud repair", "kurz": "Microsoft has released the optional preview update KB5127936 with 41 changes for Windows 11 25H2 and 26H2. They include a faster, customisable context menu in File Explorer and a reinstall via Windows Update without a USB stick. The new features are to roll out to everyone from Patch Tuesday on 10 November.", "zusammenfassung": "On 28 October, Microsoft released the optional preview update KB5127936 for Windows 11 25H2 and 26H2; it contains no security fixes. According to BleepingComputer, the builds rise to 26200.9818 and 26300.9818 respectively, with 41 changes and fixes in total. The context menu in File Explorer is said to open faster and become customisable. “Cloud Rebuild” lets you reinstall Windows via Windows Update without a USB stick or ISO file – even if the system no longer boots. Xbox mode gets a revamped task view with a navigation bar, for example for “Go to desktop” and the power options. The “Privacy & security” settings page groups camera, microphone and location, and the WinRE recovery environment can use saved Wi-Fi profiles. Hibernation becomes adaptive: above 80 percent battery it kicks in less often, below 10 percent sooner. Because Secure Boot certificates are being updated, an additional restart may be required. The update is installed via Settings > Windows Update or the Microsoft Update Catalog. Microsoft is rolling out the features gradually, so they will not appear on every PC right away. According to Thurrott, the new features are to roll out to everyone from Patch Tuesday on 10 November.", "weitere_links": ["Microsoft Support: KB5127936 (builds 26300.9818 and 26200.9818)", "Thurrott: Week D preview updates for Windows 11"], "_src": "b3b29ee6"}, "2026-10-29-gta6-edge-polizei": {"titel": "GTA 6: Rockstar shows police with K-9 unit, scheduled buses and dynamic weather", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: police with sniffer dogs, buses and trains on a timetable", "kurz": "In a cover story for the British magazine Edge, Rockstar revealed new details about GTA 6. The police track players via cameras, trackers in cars and witness tips, and there is also a K-9 unit. GTA 6 launches on 19 November 2026 for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Polygon, Rob Nelson, co-studio head of Rockstar North, gave the British magazine Edge exclusive new details about Grand Theft Auto VI. The police are said to track players via their last sighting, surveillance cameras, trackers in cars and tips from passers-by. New is a K-9 unit: in the demo shown, a German shepherd caught Jason after a motorcycle crash. Pedestrians are said to have their own character traits – some flee, others attack. Buses and trains run on fixed routes according to a timetable; development director Phil Hooker said he places the greatest importance on them always arriving on time. The weather is dynamic, with clouds shaped by wind, humidity, fog, time of day and season. Rockstar itself pointed to the cover story in Edge issue 430 on X. According to Take-Two, GTA 6 launches on 19 November 2026 for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S. The Standard Edition costs 79.99 US dollars in the US, the Ultimate Edition 99.99 US dollars. The digital pre-load and the physical edition are planned from 12 November.", "weitere_links": ["Rockstar Games on X: pointer to the Edge cover story (30 Oct 2026)", "Take-Two: GTA VI pre-orders, date and prices"], "_src": "e7ef25df"}, "2026-10-28-galax-dementi": {"titel": "Rumour debunked: GALAX is not leaving the graphics card business", "schlagzeile": "GALAX shutting down? The manufacturer says clearly: no", "kurz": "A Spanish site had reported “exclusively” that GALAX was leaving the graphics card business. GALAX and partner Palit have officially denied this, and production continues as normal. Nothing changes for buyers of KFA2 cards, as GALAX is called in Europe.", "zusammenfassung": "The Spanish site El Chapuzas Informático had reported 'exclusively' that GALAX was leaving the GPU market due to a lack of NVIDIA chips and that Palit was closing the associated factory. GALAX denied this in an official statement: no production facilities had been closed, and business continues as normal. Palit, which shares factories with GALAX, also confirmed to media that production is continuing. A similar rumour had already circulated in April in connection with a restructuring under Palit's headquarters in Taiwan. Only on 22 October, GALAX had unveiled the RTX 5080 HOF Extreme. For buyers of KFA2 cards – as GALAX is called in Europe – nothing changes regarding warranty or support as things stand. The case shows why we label 'exclusive' single reports without a second source as unconfirmed.", "datum_hinweis": "Time estimated", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz", "Tom's Hardware", "Original rumour (El Chapuzas Informático)"], "_src": "cf83f08b"}, "2026-10-25-ddr6-camm2": {"titel": "DDR6: 192-bit memory interfaces and CAMM2 instead of classic DIMMs", "schlagzeile": "DDR6 is coming – and classic RAM sticks could disappear", "kurz": "As things stand, DDR6 is set to use the flat CAMM2 format instead of classic DIMM sticks, and desktop CPUs are to get a 192-bit memory interface. Data rates from 8,800 to over 17,600 MT/s are mentioned. According to an SK Hynix roadmap, however, consumers should not expect DDR6 before 2030.", "zusammenfassung": "3DCenter has compiled what is known about the upcoming DDR6 standard and added an update on 25 October. DDR6 is to use PAM4 signalling and work with 24-bit-wide memory chips. A module would consist of four 24-bit channels, and CPU memory interfaces grow in 96-bit steps – typically to 192 bits on the desktop. CAMM2 is planned as the form factor instead of today's UDIMM and SO-DIMM sticks. Data rates from 8,800 to over 17,600 MT/s are mentioned. According to an SK Hynix roadmap, DDR6 is not expected before 2029 in servers and 2030 for consumers. The JEDEC specification is not yet final, and an alternative proposal with 16-bit channels is also being discussed.", "datum_hinweis": "Date of the update; time estimated", "_src": "eef0b055"}, "2026-10-02-core-ultra-4000-lineup": {"titel": "Core Ultra 4000 'Nova Lake-S': lineup topped by Core Ultra 9 4970K BFC", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Intel's 28-core flagship with huge cache said to hunt AMD's X3D chips", "kurz": "A leaked list names seven desktop CPUs in the Core Ultra 4000 series, topped by a Core Ultra 9 4970K with 28 cores and a large cache. The extra cache is seen as Intel's answer to AMD's X3D processors. Intel has not confirmed any model names, and details may still change.", "zusammenfassung": "In early October, a list of seven desktop processors from the upcoming Core Ultra 4000 series surfaced. At the top is a Core Ultra 9 4970K 'BFC' with 28 cores, a large last-level cache (bLLC) and 125 W base power, ranking even above the 4950K. The bLLC is seen as Intel's answer to AMD's X3D processors with 3D V-Cache. Well-known leaker kopite7kimi commented on the report on 13 October: the large cache is supposed to rescue Nova Lake's gaming performance, because the regular models without bLLC are about as fast as Arrow Lake in games. Intel itself has not named any models so far – officially, only the 18A-P process and an unveiling at CES are confirmed. Model names, core counts and TDP values may still change before launch.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Lineup leak commented on by kopite7kimi (high reliability); not confirmed by Intel.", "weitere_links": ["kopite7kimi on X (13 Oct)"], "_src": "53d234c7"}, "2026-09-21-kopite-gr20x-2028": {"titel": "kopite7kimi: NVIDIA's GR20x generation not until 2028", "schlagzeile": "Leak: we'll probably have to wait until 2028 for NVIDIA's next gaming GPUs", "kurz": "Well-known leaker kopite7kimi writes that NVIDIA's GR20x chips are a 2028 product, meaning the next generation is slipping. For 2027, refreshes of the RTX 50 series would then be more likely. NVIDIA has not confirmed this timeline.", "zusammenfassung": "Well-known NVIDIA leaker kopite7kimi writes on X that the GR20x chips are a product for 2028 – meaning NVIDIA has postponed again. By the common reading, this refers to the gaming generation after Blackwell, which is likely to be named after NVIDIA's data centre architecture 'Rubin'. He also announced that he will post fewer updates until there is solid news, citing 'lessons learned' – apparently a reaction to changed plans in earlier leaks. Our take: for 2027, refreshes of the RTX 50 series would then be more likely, for example with more memory like the reported RTX 5080 24GB. NVIDIA itself has confirmed nothing about this timeline. Even with reliable leakers: dates shift more often than technical specs.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "kopite7kimi has a long track record with NVIDIA leaks; timing claims, however, are less certain than technical details.", "ursprungsquelle": "kopite7kimi", "_src": "89b4f8c9"}};
